{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought","id":1236152,"title":"On What Fire Has Wrought","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-17T14:38:24-07:00","id":1236152,"title":"On What Fire Has Wrought","content":"I said I wouldn't make this thread, but people seem to be interested, so...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar223_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"223\" data-vbnamecard=\"223\">Calboon</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12730_4.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12730\" data-vbnamecard=\"12730\">PneumaPilot</a>, you all expressed specific interest, so I'm tagging you.<br /> <br /> <b>Preface and Background</b><br /> I said, in a different thread, that <i>Dragon-Blood: What Fire Has Wrought</i> was a &quot;huge disappointment&quot; to me. With this post, I'm going to try to explain <i>why</i>.<br /> <br /> Firstly: at the time of the Kickstarter, I wasn't particularly focused on Exalted. My attention was elsewhere, and I figured my budget could do without investing into a Kickstarter. Then, I started hearing positive buzz about the first previews, and... well, it was warranted.<br /> <br /> When I say that I regard WFHW as a disappointment, I do <i>not</i> mean the first four chapters of the manuscript. They are nothing but engaging, and they drew me back in and got me quite excited to play a Dragon-Blood again<sup>1</sup>. I was, in a word, <i>hyped</i>.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, with the release of the third preview, that hype was dashed. The Charmset was \u2013 <i>is</i> \u2013 not to my tastes, in ways I can only call &quot;frustrating.&quot;<br /> <br /> <sub>1: Before the Kickstarter, I had been playing using a homebrew set of DB mechanics known as <i>A Clutch of Dragons</i>.</sub><br /> <br /> <b>Issue 1: Purchased Excellencies</b><br /> I was aware that DBs would have purchased Excellencies going in, and I actually supported the decision. Having been running a Solar game for some time, I'd started to get frustrated with the ease that a Solar can drive their dice pools to overcome challenges, particularly within their area of focus. However, the Excellencies of WFHW brought back what might be my least favourite quirk of the purchased Excellencies of previous editions, one I had hoped and <i>assumed</i> would never return: Excellency prerequisites.<br /> <br /> Excellencies acting as prereqs for other Charms is the bane of my character creation process. They're mostly a speedbump within a character's main area of focus \u2013 which isn't <i>great</i>, but I can live with it \u2013 but once you start branching out, they rapidly deplete chargen resources, narrowing your options. For me in particular, who likes to dip into Abilities outside my intended area of focus to round out my characters, this resource drain is particularly pronounced.<br /> <br /> Now, the Excellencies of WFHW pull double duty as baseline dice tricks, but a lot of them aren't enough to make up for the cost. Some are good \u2013 I'm partial to Become the Hammer \u2013 but too many have effects along the lines of ignoring penalties from a narrow band of sources, or worse, a <i>single point</i> of penalty. On top of this, bar Resistance, every Ability requires you to purchase the Excellency to access most or all other Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Issue 2: Charm Power and Utility</b><br /> WFHW Charms have a tendency to be, well, weak. Sometimes in raw numbers, which is to be expected, but often also in when you can actually apply them. The Occult set is good for illustrating this, since it's readily comparable with its Solar counterpart.<br /> <br /> For example, let's compare Spirit-Detecting Glance to Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique.<br /> The former costs 3m, and the latter 4m \u2013 not a real issue, in isolation.<br /> SDG can be used at any time, while SDMT requires you to touch a reflective surface \u2013 a limitation, but a flavourful one, giving the Charm a distinct feel from the Solar equivalent.<br /> SDG carries no penalty, while SDMT leaves you with -1 penalty on your attack roll \u2013 again, harmless in isolation, but...<br /> <i>Together</i>, these qualities add up to a Charm that is numerically weaker, more limited, and more expensive than its Solar counterpart. I can't help but find that excessive.<br /> <br /> Now, while that particular combination of issues shows up more than a few times in the set, it's not really fair to constantly compare it to the Solar one. Even so, too many Charms have riders or limitations that just don't sit right with me \u2013 Graceful Dryad Dance is useless if your game is set in Chiaroscuro or on the high seas, for example while Stone Carving Fingers Form only works with stone and is a prerequisite for 7/17 Craft Charms, with Shaping Hand Style to mitigate the artificial problem it creates.<br /> <br /> <b>Issue 3: Effect Distribution</b><br /> This isn't a major one, but I should get it out of the way.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the WFHW sets relies too much on the cool factor of the Signature Charms and Essence 3+ effects, and leaves the chargen Charms feeling rather... bland, in places? I would've wanted more flashy effects at Essence 1 and 2, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <b>Issue 4: Aura and the Elemental Keywords</b><br /> This, on the other hand, is a major issue for me.<br /> <br /> The manuscript sells Aura really well, presenting it as a strength of the Dragon-Blooded, and a flashy visual to boot, but I can't help but see it as one thing: overhead.<br /> Overhead, on top of the motes, Willpower, Initiative, and Charm resets I'm already keeping track of.<br /> Overhead that is singularly concerned with limiting my options at any given time and cutting off what seem like cool synergies.<br /> <br /> This is compounded by a tendency for Aura-dependent Charms to be really weak outside of it and, perhaps more importantly, the way the Charm trees veer between different elements, leaving you with things like the Melee capstonse requiring Aura states that most of the Melee set can't provide.<br /> <br /> <b>Positives</b><br /> With all my complaints, though, I have to say that when the set is good, it's <i>good</i>. I'm partial to Imago-Hatching Realization, Blazing Hoard of Hesiesh, Smoke Ascends to Heaven...<br /> <br /> A number of Charms, actually, even if my issues with the Charmset as a whole drags them down.<br /> <br /> <b>Martial Arts, Sorcery, and Evocations</b><br /> The martial arts and sorcery in the book were lacking something, too, though I can't rightly say I dislike them. They just... lack <i>something</i> that the corebook examples have, and I can't quite put my finger on what.<br /> <br /> The Evocations, on the other hand, are the mechanical standouts of the manuscript. They don't feel quite as flashy and character-defining, in general, as the examples in <i>Arms of the Chosen, </i>but I like all of them. Perdurant Vault is a particular favourite.<br /> <br /> <b>In Summary</b><br /> The <i>What Fire Has Wrought</i> manuscript got me excited about playing Dragon-Blooded, but left me with tools to do so that I simply don't <i>enjoy</i>. It's disappointing, and it's honestly a shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:03:05-07:00","id":1236187,"title":"","content":"That sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> I have one, small point of contention:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">leaving you with things like the Melee capstonse requiring Aura states that most of the Melee set can't provide</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> When I hear points such as this, I get an impression that it's approaching Aura as though it's something that needs to be built up consistently.<br /> <br /> And that might just be projection on my part; I need to constantly remind myself that Aura is a simply binary state, activated by the use of so much as a single Charm.<br /> <br /> However, with that consideration, it does feel to me like the necessity of setting up an Aura is not quite as weighty.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:31:56-07:00","id":1236200,"title":"","content":"Thanks for writing this out,<br /> <br /> My experience is broadly aligned with what you layed out, ie the fluff is great but the mechanics are lacking.<br /> <br /> The big one for me though is in the two times I have tried to run a 3e db game, and what killed it both times, was the aura mechanic. exalted asks a lot of the players in regards to bookkeeping with the payout of that bookkeeping being a really cool and powerful effect.<br /> <br /> With dragon blooded though the pay out is not only worse, ie a lesser effect than what solar gets but requires even more bookeeping, that slowed the game down and killed the interest in the game fast.<br /> <br /> The buying of excellencies was another one that I was surprised of how detrimental it ended up being. In Chargen no one really cared that much but in the session to session buying of charms having that roadblock of having to spend a charm purchase just on a excellency and a dice trick really sucked.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T17:50:56-07:00","id":1236223,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar223_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"223\" data-vbnamecard=\"223\">Calboon</a> At character creation, which Aura effects are you trying to make sure you pull off? I tried to make a Solar killer just now, and I literally ran into no effects that required Aura in order to work.<br /> <br /> I might be misunderstanding, though. I\u2019d love to see an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:32:40-07:00","id":1236241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236223#post1236223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar223_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"223\" data-vbnamecard=\"223\">Calboon</a> At character creation, which Aura effects are you trying to make sure you pull off? I tried to make a Solar killer just now, and I literally ran into no effects that required Aura in order to work.<br /> <br /> I might be misunderstanding, though. I\u2019d love to see an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>There where no big effects or killer combos to be honest. It was more that I think my group was already at their &quot;max&quot; so to speak as far as bookkeeping was concerned without me noticing. And while losing the aura buffs where not that big of a deal it still started to annoy them.<br /> <br /> It came to a head when our archer was using Sky Calming draw in air aura to duel a cataphract at range. He got attacked by a homebrewed lion monster I made and he used Hopping firecracker evasion to get on top of a nearby roof. Which knocked him out of air aura and made him unable to attack the cataphract on his next turn.<br /> <br /> There was also another fuck up involving demon crushing wolf bite that ended up giving a hobgoblin battle group another turn but I can't remember what charm was used to knock the player out of wood aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","user":"Calboon","date":". 07-17-2018, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T19:25:02-07:00","id":1236259,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the Auras seem to be a mechanic that rewards creative combo play between Abilities that aren\u2019t already automatically suited to the Aspect being utilized. Designing a Fire Aspect with a lot of synergistic Melee and Athletic Charms didn\u2019t lead me to even one Aura situation, even though the character will stay in Fire Aura pretty much permanently. So it seems to benefit those who can cross into out-of-Aspect Abilities whole maintaining the theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T22:32:47-07:00","id":1236304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236259#post1236259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, the Auras seem to be a mechanic that rewards creative combo play between Abilities that aren\u2019t already automatically suited to the Aspect being utilized. Designing a Fire Aspect with a lot of synergistic Melee and Athletic Charms didn\u2019t lead me to even one Aura situation, even though the character will stay in Fire Aura pretty much permanently. So it seems to benefit those who can cross into out-of-Aspect Abilities whole maintaining the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do but they also kind of do suffer a drawback. One expects every charm they purchase to be useful but aura kind of screws that. The charms should have been ordered by aura due to it's importance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:30:54-07:00","id":1236351,"title":"","content":"I actually like the way that some particularly strong synergies are not possible as a result of incompatible elements, because I think that it's both an effective way of putting in some individually strong Charms and preventing them from disrupting the place of the Dragon Blooded in the rankings, and that it emphasizes the fact that they benefit more from the coordinated group than the grand individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:58:11-07:00","id":1236354,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, taking Melee for example, it's incredibly frustrating that you need an Aura that <i>you can't produce with the ability at all</i> in order to use what is clearly its best Signature Charm.<br /> <br /> (Okay, technically, you <i>can</i> produce Water Aura... <i>if </i>you have access to a large body of water and spend an action on doing so, <i>or</i> an opponent attacks you during your own turn, <i>or </i>you pick up a once-per-scene E3 Melee Charm which has another E3 prerequisite which is explicitly incompatible with the Aura state you want to reach, rendering it largely a speedbump for your purposes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T04:00:23-07:00","id":1236356,"title":"","content":"I haven't actually played with the DB charms yet, but power-level wise they seem fine; they are honestly, supposed to be the weakest.<br /> <br /> However, my friend runs a DB game, and he said only two of the players do stuff with Aura, the others find it too awkward so they just don't use Aura-dependent charms. Which are often the coolest or most powerful, so it's kind of a pity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T04:09:31-07:00","id":1236357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236187#post1236187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> I have one, small point of contention:<br /> <br /> <br /> When I hear points such as this, I get an impression that it's approaching Aura as though it's something that needs to be built up consistently.<br /> <br /> And that might just be projection on my part; I need to constantly remind myself that Aura is a simply binary state, activated by the use of so much as a single Charm.<br /> <br /> However, with that consideration, it does feel to me like the necessity of setting up an Aura is not quite as weighty.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>One single charm on your turn; defensive charms are no good (unless someone attacks you on your turn).<br /> <br /> Anyway, by melee they're referring (I assume) to the fact that near the end of the Melee tree, there's a number of really powerful charms that require water-aura, but there's no way to get Water aura using melee. You need to either hit people with brawl then switch to melee the following turn, or play a water aspect, get yourself into fire aura, then go iconic so it switches into fire aura. And if you expend your aura, you'll have to do it again.<br /> For a player who's interested in these kind of mechanical complications and combos, it can be quite rewarding, but it's a bit complex for some players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T04:29:39-07:00","id":1236361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236357#post1236357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One single charm on your turn; defensive charms are no good (unless someone attacks you on your turn).</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Anima Powers also qualify - if you use nothing but balanced Charms otherwise, you can trivially access your appropriate Aura for a 1m expenditure to stunt with your element, or know where your hearthmates are or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24174-mystictemplar","name":"MysticTemplar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T04:51:08-07:00","id":1236365,"title":"","content":"Ah, I missed that. Doesn't help you enter other elements' auras, but it does make playing a water-aura swordsman much more viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T04:51:27-07:00","id":1236366,"title":"","content":"Are there copoes out already? I never got a notice about one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T04:53:13-07:00","id":1236367,"title":"","content":"Yes, and outside of your aspect element, there's plenty of charms of an element you might be able to use. A number of Balanced charms are ALSO element-tagged. If I recall correctly, using such a charm will in fact place you in the appropriate Aura. So... just buy Cloud-Piercing Focus to access Earth, Fire, or Water Aura any time you like. I haven't trawled the entire charms section, but I would be surprised if Air and Wood didn't have appropriate minor 1m charms you could use.<br /> <br /> Is it a 'mote tax' of sorts to use your way-cool Aura-expending charms? Sure. There's a cost to trying to use an out of aspect signature charm. If it's of your aspect and you're building along aspect lines, MysticTemplar's comment is absolutely correct - it's almost entirely trivial. Fire Melee master? Buy the fire signatures and never worry about Aura, ever.<br /> <br /> I view the more complex mix-and-match Aura element kind of builds to be advanced shenanigans akin to finding two martial arts styles that synergize; it's great you <i>can</i>, but most people won't be hurt if they just focus on the one they like the most.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T05:04:51-07:00","id":1236371,"title":"","content":"If you stay in Fire Aura through using Melee Charms, you can immediately blind someone for three rounds when you crash them with Blinding Spark Throw. That\u2019s a cool and natural use of the Aura mechanic that really doesn\u2019t get in anyone\u2019s way. I think there are lots of little things like this.<br /> <br /> In other words, look for opportunities to do something powerful along the lines of what you\u2019re already doing, rather than try to shoehorn in something that doesn\u2019t really flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T05:05:23-07:00","id":1236372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236366#post1236366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there copoes out already? I never got a notice about one</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for those who kick-started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T06:23:38-07:00","id":1236386,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth mentioning that Air and Water Aspect swordsmen will have their Fire Auras convert into Air or Water Auras when their animas achieve the bonfire level. Which could make up for the difficulty of maintaining Fire Aura despite their anima powers. <br /> <br /> Water Aspects are probably expected to be rewarded for mixing Brawl tricks into their Melee, with Air Aspects whipping out surprise hidden throwing daggers.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are constantly rewarded for playing to type, and struggle to escape that type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T06:37:37-07:00","id":1236389,"title":"","content":"I am thankful for this discussion guys. I think there's a tiny minor chance that some things might change before the publication of WFHW. Maybe?<br /> <br /> If not, there's still Heirs to the Shogunate. I think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T07:42:29-07:00","id":1236405,"title":"","content":"I was just looking through the grapple Charms in Brawl, and it seems like it would be very easy to make an Earth-Aura wrestler that can take advantage of a lot of those synergies in Brawl, and of course lots of Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> After looking at this for a while now, the clever placement of the Balanced keyword (especially on Excellencies) really does seem to make it quite easy to get some of these bonuses.<br /> <br /> In my mind, the manuscript form of the book is a little difficult to flip through, and I think that this difficulty, plus the fact that you have to be a little strategic in your character designs, causes some people to think that the system is somehow flawed, but it looks glorious to me. Maybe look through the Charms before coming up with a final character concept, so you aren\u2019t frustrated by not being able to get all the benefits you think you should, and instead you can let the dynamics of the Charm set guide some of your decisions. But remember, even if you throw Aura to the wind, the Charms all still work just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:00:57-07:00","id":1236407,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the complexity of trying to activate the appropriate auras when needed. This is the first edition where I might willingly choose to play a Dragonblood. However, I know not everyone has my love for games/puzzles, so I appreciate the fact that it's off-putting for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> I will say, I believe the Devs did a great job with the strength of Dragonblooded charms. Everyone who complains about them, compares them to Solar charms. That's a mistake IMHO. Dragonblood charms should fare more favorably against Lunar and Sidereal charms, but should still fall short of them in power. This means Dragonblood charms didn't just need to be weaker then Solar charms, they needed to be a lot weaker. They need the space for another tier of power in between the Dragonbloods and Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 07-18-2018, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:03:55-07:00","id":1236408,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2103_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2103\" data-vbnamecard=\"2103\">TalosX</a> Exactly! And also, there are quite a few awesome Charms that utilize the group/teamwork aspect of Sworn Kinships. In a group, they can be VERY dangerous to Solars - precisely as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:13:37-07:00","id":1236411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236407#post1236407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like the complexity of trying to activate the appropriate auras when needed. This is the first edition where I might willingly choose to play a Dragonblood. However, I know not everyone has my love for games/puzzles, so I appreciate the fact that it's off-putting for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> I will say, I believe the Devs did a great job with the strength of Dragonblooded charms. Everyone who complains about them, compares them to Solar charms. That's a mistake IMHO. Dragonblood charms should fare more favorably against Lunar and Sidereal charms, but should still fall short of them in power. This means Dragonblood charms didn't just need to be weaker then Solar charms, they needed to be a lot weaker. They need the space for another tier of power in between the Dragonbloods and Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping that the other exalts aren't a Tier below. They were always supposed to be just behind them, rather than an entire Tier below them. I do agree that the strength of DB charms is correct. I do think things should shift aura to allow some breathing room. A dragonblooded shouldn't have to learn an entire different ability just to use a signature tree charm. However, that can be fixed by just retooling a few elemental auras around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-18-2018, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:15:10-07:00","id":1236414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236411#post1236411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that the other exalts aren't a Tier below. They were always supposed to be just behind them, rather than an entire Tier below them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the metrics of &quot;an entire Tier&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:22:49-07:00","id":1236418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236414#post1236414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are the metrics of &quot;an entire Tier&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I put &quot;tier&quot; in quotes originally but I suppose the ability to somewhat compete. Being able to not quite be as good as but still hold their own for a bit. Notable flaws but still not incapable. I suppose the difference between a total blowout and a close win.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:39:30-07:00","id":1236425,"title":"","content":"I think the lack of supernal will go a long way to making solars come out ahead in the early game.<br /> <br /> Even if the charms are equal, lunars and sids will be limited by essence prerequisites. So a solar who can pull out essence 5 charms from the get go will be stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:46:28-07:00","id":1236428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236425#post1236425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the lack of supernal will go a long way to making solars come out ahead in the early game.<br /> <br /> Even if the charms are equal, lunars and sids will be limited by essence prerequisites. So a solar who can pull out essence 5 charms from the get go will be stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to ask in the other thread but I guess Lunars don't have something similar to supernal? Also, almost all the core charms tend to be e3 most of the e5 charms tend to be die tricks. Powerful die tricks but not decisive ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:48:36-07:00","id":1236429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236386#post1236386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth mentioning that Air and Water Aspect swordsmen will have their Fire Auras convert into Air or Water Auras when their animas achieve the bonfire level. Which could make up for the difficulty of maintaining Fire Aura despite their anima powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, my concern with Roaring River Slash isn't how difficult it is to use as a Water Aspect swordsman, it's that it is powerful enough that pretty much everybody wants it, even Fire Aspects - and as a Fire Aspect, you're shit out of luck if you ever want to use it (unless you cheese Cloud-Piercing Focus, which is definitely a solution, but <i>not having to do that</i> would be even better).<br /> <br /> (Granted, &quot;Thunderbolt Attack Prana, but better&quot; is maybe a place where the Dragon-Blooded charmset <i>should not go</i>, Signature Charms and Aura restrictions be damned.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:58:51-07:00","id":1236434,"title":"","content":"How good is Roaring River Slash when you\u2019ve got your target in a clinch thanks to Water Charms and they can\u2019t apply their Defense against your signature attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:28:02-07:00","id":1236443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236407#post1236407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like the complexity of trying to activate the appropriate auras when needed. This is the first edition where I might willingly choose to play a Dragonblood. However, I know not everyone has my love for games/puzzles, so I appreciate the fact that it's off-putting for a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the thing, and I think will make playing a DB a bit of a love/hate thing. If you're the sort of player who likes setting up complex mechanical combos to unleash great power, they work well.<br /> If you're the sort who isn't very good at mechanics, and just wants stuff that's easy to use, yet doesn't feel weak compared to the previous player-type, it's going to be really annoying.<br /> (If you're the sort who doesn't like complex mechanics, but also doesn't care that much about unleashing the most powerful charms, then it doesn't really matter. There's plenty of charms that don't worry about Aura.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This means Dragonblood charms didn't just need to be weaker then Solar charms, they needed to be a lot weaker. They need the space for another tier of power in between the Dragonbloods and Solars. </div> </div> </div>I agree with your first part. DBs outnumber Celestials what, 25-1? Something like that. If DB charms were just a bit behind Solar charms, that'd mean most DBs would be more powerful than most Solars (because most DBs have far, far, far more experience than most Solars, plus better teachers and more magical equipment), and you'd wonder why the significance of 150 guys just a bit more powerful than the 20,000 DBs* coming back is a big deal.<br /> <br /> I don't really agree with your point about needing a big space for Sidereals and Lunars to be between Solars and DBs though.<br /> DBs outnumber Lunars something like 50-1, yet things have been pretty even between the Realm and the Silver Pact. Hey, the Silver Pact has even managed to push the Realm out of most of a continent with some of the DBs most sacred pilgrimage sites.<br /> I think Lunars and Sidereals should be much closer to Solars than to Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> *Are there 20,000? Or 30,000? I can't remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-18-2018, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:33:08-07:00","id":1236444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236434#post1236434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How good is Roaring River Slash when you\u2019ve got your target in a clinch thanks to Water Charms and they can\u2019t apply their Defense against your signature attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a lot better than it is when they <i>can</i> apply their defense, but at the same time, I'd wager most people who want to play a Dragon-Blooded meleeist don't necessarily think &quot;girl who shanks grappled people with her water knife&quot; when they imagine their character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:18:15-07:00","id":1236458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236187#post1236187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I hear points such as this, I get an impression that it's approaching Aura as though it's something that needs to be built up consistently.<br /> <br /> And that might just be projection on my part; I need to constantly remind myself that Aura is a simply binary state, activated by the use of so much as a single Charm.<br /> <br /> However, with that consideration, it does feel to me like the necessity of setting up an Aura is not quite as weighty.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good point, actually.<br /> <br /> I suppose the weight of Aura lies more on maintaining and keeping track on it than establishing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236405#post1236405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIn my mind, the manuscript form of the book is a little difficult to flip through, and I think that this difficulty, plus the fact that you have to be a little strategic in your character designs, causes some people to think that the system is somehow flawed, but it looks glorious to me. Maybe look through the Charms before coming up with a final character concept, so you aren\u2019t frustrated by not being able to get all the benefits you think you should, and instead you can let the dynamics of the Charm set guide some of your decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div> I resent the implication that WFHW being unappealing to me is somehow my fault.<br /> <br /> It's... not anyone's fault? It's just an unfortunate <i>thing</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236407#post1236407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone who complains about them, compares them to Solar charms. That's a mistake IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. Solar Charms \u2013 as well as the non-splat powersets of martial arts, sorcery, and Evocations \u2013 are what we have for comparison, so it's natural and <i>expected</i> that we should make it. Doubly so when there are Charms that, like Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique and Strength of Stone Technique, have clear equivalents in the Solar set, and fall short on so many fronts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:25:59-07:00","id":1236464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236414#post1236414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are the metrics of &amp;quot;an entire Tier&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's something like boxes. The problem with mid tier is that although it's near top tier, it cannot contain things from the top tier cause they are beyond it.<br /> <br /> At least that's why I hate the idea of tiers. I think there should be an overlap area between mid-powered exalts and the solars. The same between low-power and mid-powered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:26:43-07:00","id":1236465,"title":"","content":"Have you tried tracking aura with a d6? <br /> <br /> You could make little coloured stickers to put on the sides or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:43:02-07:00","id":1236472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236458#post1236458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I resent the implication that WFHW being unappealing to me is somehow my fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I wasn\u2019t addressing you directly. In fact, it doesn\u2019t look like I\u2019m laying blame anywhere. I was just commenting on the fact that the manuscript is hard to navigate, and that some people aren\u2019t wired for finding combos in the mechanics. I was merely giving my perspective on why I find something awesome that someone else may find lackluster.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an attempt at understanding, not an indictment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:57:00-07:00","id":1236503,"title":"","content":"(Pardon me for not quoting, I'm posting from a Playstation)<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can still see how keeping track of if Aura and which Aura can deter someone.<br /> <br /> I actually am inclined to compare them to Solars, since measuring the difference is part of the point to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:09:14-07:00","id":1236506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236411#post1236411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that the other exalts aren't a Tier below. They were always supposed to be just behind them, rather than an entire Tier below them. I do agree that the strength of DB charms is correct. I do think things should shift aura to allow some breathing room. A dragonblooded shouldn't have to learn an entire different ability just to use a signature tree charm. However, that can be fixed by just retooling a few elemental auras around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your interpretation of &quot;tier&quot;. My own interpretation is that the tiers exist, but they are fairly close to one another, and aren't hard lines on abilities. Meaning Solars should only have a few dice, motes, etc as an advantage over Lunars and Sidereals. Just like Lunars/Sidereals have a few dice, motes, etc advantage over Dragonbloods. It's difficult to quantify as just numbers, because each exalt has thematic/flavorful charm effects that don't translate as dice/motes. The Dragonblood charm mentioned earlier in the thread, that requires them to touch a reflective surface to see spirits is a good example of an effect that doesn't translate to dice or motes.<br /> <br /> Also, when I say Solar's are a tier above Lunar's, that doesn't mean a Solar will always have a better charm for the same effect. I'm talking in a general sense of power. I absolutely believe that Lunar's will have charms in certain purviews, that surpass what Solar charms are capable of doing. Their are also purviews in which Lunar's and Sidereal's will have charms, that Solar's simply don't. Even in area's which Solar's do compete with Lunars/Sidereals, I don't think the Solar's have any &quot;auto-win&quot; buttons (nor should they).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236428#post1236428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to ask in the other thread but I guess Lunars don't have something similar to supernal? Also, almost all the core charms tend to be e3 most of the e5 charms tend to be die tricks. Powerful die tricks but not decisive ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar's have access to shapeshifting from E1. Having additional forms is a serious force multiplier. You not only have access to animal forms, but also all the corresponding abilities unique to those animals. This is on top of the advantages of taking another human's form can provide (near perfect disguise at E1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 07-18-2018, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:34:38-07:00","id":1236513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236443#post1236443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the thing, and I think will make playing a DB a bit of a love/hate thing. If you're the sort of player who likes setting up complex mechanical combos to unleash great power, they work well.<br /> If you're the sort who isn't very good at mechanics, and just wants stuff that's easy to use, yet doesn't feel weak compared to the previous player-type, it's going to be really annoying.<br /> (If you're the sort who doesn't like complex mechanics, but also doesn't care that much about unleashing the most powerful charms, then it doesn't really matter. There's plenty of charms that don't worry about Aura.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like I said, I'll enjoy it. I do however understand that not everyone will though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236443#post1236443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with your first part. DBs outnumber Celestials what, 25-1? Something like that. If DB charms were just a bit behind Solar charms, that'd mean most DBs would be more powerful than most Solars (because most DBs have far, far, far more experience than most Solars, plus better teachers and more magical equipment), and you'd wonder why the significance of 150 guys just a bit more powerful than the 20,000 DBs* coming back is a big deal.<br /> <br /> I don't really agree with your point about needing a big space for Sidereals and Lunars to be between Solars and DBs though.<br /> DBs outnumber Lunars something like 50-1, yet things have been pretty even between the Realm and the Silver Pact. Hey, the Silver Pact has even managed to push the Realm out of most of a continent with some of the DBs most sacred pilgrimage sites.<br /> I think Lunars and Sidereals should be much closer to Solars than to Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> *Are there 20,000? Or 30,000? I can't remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree that Lunars/Sidereals should be closer Solars in power then Dragonbloods. My original post said as much, but I changed it a bit before posting it. It was a bit of a wall of text, but apparently I lost to much of my intent by cutting what I did. Lunars/Sidereals are a step beyond Dragonbloods. Solars are a step beyond Lunars/Sidereals. This makes it difficult to compare Dragonbloods and Solars, because of the gap. Having said that, outside a few specific themes, none of them should be so far beyond the others that it devolves to an &quot;auto-win&quot; scenario. An example:<br /> <br /> Two separate players each build a Solar and a Dragonblood. Both spend the same amount of points on combat abilities and combat charms. Dragonbloods aren't meant to match a Solar one-on-one. There is a reason they outnumber Solars 50-to-1 or more. However, you don't need 50. Three or four Dragonbloods with similar combat experience, is a definite threat to that Solar. Moreover, even in a 1v1 scenario, the Solar isn't guaranteed victory. If the Solar has a few bad rolls, or the DB has a few good rolls, that Solar player could need to make a new character. If a similar scenario happens with a Solar and a Lunar, I expect them to be close enough in ability that while not 50/50, the Solar's advantage may be something like 60/40, or even 55/45!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:48:09-07:00","id":1236518,"title":"","content":"We\u2019re actually testing that last scenario right now: a combat DB vs a \u201cnormal\u201d Solar (not completely committed to combat charms). My guess is that the Solar is in trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:48:46-07:00","id":1236519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236458#post1236458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Solar Charms \u2013 as well as the non-splat powersets of martial arts, sorcery, and Evocations \u2013 are what we have for comparison, so it's natural and <i>expected</i> that we should make it. Doubly so when there are Charms that, like Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique and Strength of Stone Technique, have clear equivalents in the Solar set, and fall short on so many fronts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your point, in that you don't really have anything to compare DB charms to except Solar charms. However, the Solar charms are the furthest from being comparable to DB charms, then any other exalt (barring unique purviews). In your example of Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique, you mention how inferior it is to the Solar's Spirit-Detecting Glance. Yet it's very likely Lunar's will have a similar charm, and it's power is likely to fall between the DB charm and the Solar version. Honestly, the Sidereal version might be on par or better then the Solar's, because of their unique purviews and duties in Heaven. My point is the gap in power is intentional. The Devs had to give themselves some wiggle room in their for Lunars/Sidereals to fall into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:32:51-07:00","id":1236539,"title":"","content":"My concerns with WFHW all stem from excellencies in some way. Purchased excellencies are the big one, not for balance concerns, but because they make Dragon-Bloods a lot more boring. The problem with purchased excellencies was always that it's a giant sucking fun tax. Charms are what Exalted revolves around, they define your characters and employing them in fun and interesting ways is the big mechanical draw of the system, so having to spend a big chunk of your sorely limited charm picks on the boringest charms in the game feels pretty crappy. It's especially bad if you want to be more of a generalist character who's competent in multiple fields. When you're playing a Solar, you can be pretty damn solid at a whole bunch of different abilities just by allocating dots in the right places and leaning on your free excellencies in fields where you haven't bought charms, but DBs trying to scatter out dots and excellencies to the point where they're good at combat, social intrigue and one or two other things can easily end up spending half their starting charms on just excellencies. Which is further exacerbated by the fact that of your remaining charm picks, about half again will probably be spent on the fairly bland entry charms that DBs get - and to be fair, a lot of Solar trees start off with pretty bland effects too, but proportionately they eat up much less of your character.<br /> <br /> Now, yeah, you can get around all of that by just focusing harder on one thing. If all your want your DB to do is be Sword Guy, having to spend one fifteenth of your starting charms on a melee excellency is inconsequential. But a) without supernal, DBs aren't really set up to mono-focus like that, and more to the point b) that's <i>really boring</i>. Or at least, it is for me. I don't want to be pushed into making hyper specialised characters who kick ass at their one job and then go get pizza once the combat ends and the super specialised social person takes over for the talky scene. So I'm being hemmed in by the crushing tides of boring. On one side, I could play the all-rounder characters I enjoy and not have a good time because I've got maybe three charms total that have interesting, narrative-changing effects, or on the other I could play a one-note character who works better mechanically but who I don't enjoy on a fundamental level. And it's not like any of this is some big important power tier thing that needs to be in the game, nothing in the setting breaks if DBs can be adequate generalists.<br /> <br /> The other big problem with excellencies, which this apparently all stemmed from, is that they're just plain better than a lot of DB charms. This is the big objection I have to the arguments that DB charms are fine power-wise, and we're just too used to Solar charms to properly judge them. Yes, DBs are a couple 'tiers' below Solars, but the weak DB charms aren't bad because they're worse than Solar charms. They're bad because they're worse than <i>excellencies</i>. If every Exalt is going to have excellencies, there should never be any Exalted charm that is weaker than one, because then what is the point of that charm even existing? And there are quite a lot of effects throughout the DB charmset that are, if not objectively worse than excellencies because they're giving bonuses to different things, overpriced enough that I'd pretty much never want to spend those motes on such a weak effect when I could instead be converting those motes to dice on a one for one basis. And this sucks, because excellencies are fundamentally boring. They're a useful way to demonstrate Exalted superiority, but if the design of the game is pushing you to spend your limited resource of cool points on adding numbers instead of using your unique, fun abilities that change how you interact with the world, that design is failing.<br /> <br /> So then to balance out excellencies with these overly weak charms, excellencies were made purchased instead of free. Then to make excellencies feel like less of a tax, free perks were added onto the excellencies. But this hasn't addressed the problem at all. Actually, it's done the exact opposite and made the problem twice as bad. Not only are there a bunch of charms that are weak in comparison to excellencies, but it's now actually a competition where it wasn't before. With free excellencies, you pick up 15 proper, interesting charms at chargen, and while some of them are weak, maybe you'll end up seeing situations where you can justify using them. They're on your sheet, after all, might as well look for a chance to make use of them. With purchased excellencies? You're going to spend a bunch of those 15 charm picks on excellencies. They're the better charms. Which means that you won't even have the weaker charms sitting on your sheet, waiting for a chance to employ them. You're a walking collection of dice adders, who doesn't even have the <i>option</i> of using the interesting but weak charms. And then to make matters even worse, excellencies gained their little dice tricks and such, which makes them <i>even stronger</i> in comparison to other charms, so now the pool of proper, interesting charms that are both using, and worth buying in the first place, grows even smaller. DBs are pushed so hard towards just adding dice and never interacting with the fun side of the game. And that's not an issue of 'power tiers' or whatever, it's just bad gameplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:46:31-07:00","id":1236545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236472#post1236472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, I wasn\u2019t addressing you directly. In fact, it doesn\u2019t look like I\u2019m laying blame anywhere. I was just commenting on the fact that the manuscript is hard to navigate, and that some people aren\u2019t wired for finding combos in the mechanics. I was merely giving my perspective on why I find something awesome that someone else may find lackluster.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an attempt at understanding, not an indictment.</div> </div> </div> </div>My <i>thing</i> is finding combos in mechanics. What Fire Has Wrought does not offer much in way of appeal. &quot;Wow, if I optimize really hard I...don't suck completely, woo.&quot; There just isn't much in the way of fun Charms before Essence 3, and so much of your charmslots are taken up by freaking excellencies, and worst of all, there's the damn aura debuff, where if you want a Charm to actually reach a level where it's worth anything, you need to turn off all your other Charms. The whole thing is an exercise in frustration trying to find Charms worth using and filling a sheet up full of bleugh. Every time I've tried to make a character, I just end up realizing what I <i>should</i> be doing is pure MA and Evocations, and not interacting with my actual Charms at all.<br /> <br /> At which point I get incredibly angry that the Charmset makes me feel like this and I bitterly regret opening the PDFs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T15:48:25-07:00","id":1236587,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3559_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3559\" data-vbnamecard=\"3559\">Lanaya</a> You make some compelling points to be sure. I just can\u2019t help but think, though, that I just made a Fire Aspect in an attempt to disprove some of these things written here (specifically he has no Martial Arts or Artifacts), and I\u2019m still very excited to play him. He can form a sword out of pure fire, shoot flame from his hands, run up walls, throw blinding sparks out to medium range that blinds for 3 rounds, and a bunch of other cool stuff. I didn\u2019t feel like I was being held back. I was actually surprised by how much coolness I could fit in there. Sure, I bought about 4 excellencies, but I also got two more Charms from BP, and 13 non-excellency Charms is WAY beyond what starting DBs had in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll make a few more just to see if I get that same annoyance that you feel (a few more of these non-MA, non-Artifact characters), but they all seem really exciting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:09:39-07:00","id":1236598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236539#post1236539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other big problem with excellencies, which this apparently all stemmed from, is that they're just plain better than a lot of DB charms. This is the big objection I have to the arguments that DB charms are fine power-wise, and we're just too used to Solar charms to properly judge them. Yes, DBs are a couple 'tiers' below Solars, but the weak DB charms aren't bad because they're worse than Solar charms. They're bad because they're worse than <i>excellencies</i>. If every Exalt is going to have excellencies, there should never be any Exalted charm that is weaker than one, because then what is the point of that charm even existing? And <b>there are quite a lot of effects throughout the DB charmset that are, if not objectively worse than excellencies because they're giving bonuses to different things, overpriced enough that I'd pretty much never want to spend those motes on such a weak effect when I could instead be converting those motes to dice on a one for one basis.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^Basically this.<br /> <br /> I don't <i>dislike</i> the Dragon-Blooded charmset. Some elements I'm outright happy with.<br /> <br /> But their design is <i>very much</i> slanted towards a linear progression of increasingly powerful effects instead of the cool helix structure of the Solar set, where you had very strong entry-level Charms, followed by more situational picks, followed by those sexy E3 power spikes. Take Melee, for example - as a Solar, five Charms in melee make you King Shit of Fuck Mountain: you pick Excellent Strike for what is essentially a permanent accuracy boost that grants you mote efficiency superiority against an opponent who can match you dice for dice, Dipping Swallow Defense so you'll never ever have to worry about penalties in your life, One Weapon Two Blows and Peony Blossom Technique for action economy superiority, and Call the Blade so you're never caught with your pants down if someone disarms you. Note that none of these Charms have a prerequisite higher than 3 points in Melee.<br /> <br /> What can a Dragon-Blooded get?<br /> <br /> The set starts out promisingly enough - Stoking Bonfire Style effectively rolls the function of Excellent Strike into the excellency itself, while being both weaker and more situational than its Solar equivalent (which it should be). Cool, what do I do to get something similar to DSD? I apparently need to pick Flame-Borne Interception, an effect that... matches my onslaught with an equivalent Charm bonus <i>but only as long as I keep successfully parrying</i>? Placing a &quot;win more&quot; effect like this at the basis of the weakest Exalt type's Melee tree is... certainly a decision. But once I do have FBI, I <i>can</i> actually grab Graceful Flowing Defense, which is actually a very well-designed Charm for the splat's power level. This, by itself, is a microcosm of the design difference between the Solar and the Dragon-Blooded set - we have the effect that gives a powerful basic capability hidden behind a more situational pick. The issue is the same with the set's equivalent of Fire and Stones Strike - the Dragon-Blooded version is split between two inferior Charms (Crimson Fang Bite and Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite, the former of which costs Willpower and the latter comes with an inconvenient Aura setup which, again, <i>I personally like*</i>), but those Charms, again, are locked away behind the ridiculously situational effect of being able to ignore a few points of Hardness. Then, predictably, we don't get anything like OWTB and PBT (Dragon-Blooded don't get to break the action economy over their knees willy-nilly, something we've known since we've seen the core's Terrestrial-keyworded effects), followed by what feels like an absolute slap in the face, which is their equivalent of Call the Blade: Dragon-Graced Weapon. Taken in isolation, it would be a fine enough Charm - it is more expensive than Call the Blade, but it comes with a neat bonus effect (sometimes even a multiple choice option for said bonus effect, depending on the battlefield setup) and it never, ever fails. However, it has a prerequisite of <i>5 dots in Melee,</i> and another Charm that might very well be completely useless to you, depending on whether you happen to have an artifact weapon that is made of jade. Amazing. I need to be a master swordsman just to avoid being completely shut down by any schmuck who can succeed on a Disarm gambit, and even if I am, I also need to pick a dead Charm for the privilege.<br /> <br /> This is generally a theme with the way the Dragon-Blooded charmset is put together: it discourages dipping by forcing you to pick a few Charms with effects that range from situational to useless for every worthwhile effect you might actually be interested in. <b>The problem is not actually that you have to purchase excellencies, it's the fact that the designers decided to forego the basic structure of the Solar charmset in favor of a more linear power progression for dubious gain.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> *Can we talk about how cool Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite is, designwise? Fire and Stones Strike's power lies in the fact that it adds post-soak damage dice, something these Charms don't do... <i>but</i> DCWB elegantly side-steps the issue by adding its bonus to Overwhelming, which works out to be effectively same in a lot of cases where you suddenly need a bunch of post-soak damage dice; then it adds some extra power to the effect while driving player behavior/build diversity by allowing a more generalized use of the Charm in an atypical Aura state; then it takes a lot of power away relatively to FSS by making the Charm's cost fixed instead of variable on a 1-for-1 basis, forcing players to either build specifically to maximize its benefit (which, funnily enough, takes them in a direction where they will benefit more from other Wood Charms as well), or to effectively waste motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-18-2018, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:34:54-07:00","id":1236610,"title":"","content":"Dragon graced weapon isn't really the equivalent of call the blade. <br /> <br /> It's more like their version of glorious solar saber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T16:46:50-07:00","id":1236612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236610#post1236610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon graced weapon isn't really the equivalent of call the blade.<br /> <br /> It's more like their version of glorious solar saber.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glorious Solar Saber is a Simple Charm that produces an artifact weapon when you don't have one.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Graced Weapon is a Reflexive Charm that produces a regular weapon, which has a &quot;summon your jade artifact from Elsewhere&quot; effect as its prerequisite, meaning that the intended use-case is &quot;grab a quick backup after your <i>actual</i> weapon is taken away from you&quot;. (Technically, it may not necessarily be the <i>intended</i> use-case, but if I have Elemental Sheath and don't happen to have a weapon on me, why would I use DGW to create a weapon if I can summon my more powerful artifact instead?) (<i>Technically</i>, you don't have to have a jade weapon, but if I'm throwing 8 XP out already just so I can <i>then</i> buy the Charm that gives me the ability to disarm-proof myself, I better spend 3 merit dots on an artifact in order to not make that investment <i>completely</i> wasted.)<br /> <br /> (I'd be more amenable to accept the argument that DGW is not meant to be used to disarm-proof yourself if the Dragon-Blooded set had <i>any</i> alternatives before hitting E3, which takes 30 sessions under the current rules.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:16:01-07:00","id":1236620,"title":"","content":"You really can't think of any situation where reflexively summoning any weapon you can think of on the fly would be useful? <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, hey, I need to grapple that dude on the horse. Too bad I don't have a whip...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Man, I could really use something with the thrown tag right now&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, hey, I need to run over there but there are arrows and shit. I wish I had a shield&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:16:16-07:00","id":1236621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236587#post1236587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3559_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3559\" data-vbnamecard=\"3559\">Lanaya</a> You make some compelling points to be sure. I just can\u2019t help but think, though, that I just made a Fire Aspect in an attempt to disprove some of these things written here (specifically he has no Martial Arts or Artifacts), and I\u2019m still very excited to play him. He can form a sword out of pure fire, shoot flame from his hands, run up walls, throw blinding sparks out to medium range that blinds for 3 rounds, and a bunch of other cool stuff. I didn\u2019t feel like I was being held back. I was actually surprised by how much coolness I could fit in there. Sure, I bought about 4 excellencies, but I also got two more Charms from BP, and 13 non-excellency Charms is WAY beyond what starting DBs had in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll make a few more just to see if I get that same annoyance that you feel (a few more of these non-MA, non-Artifact characters), but they all seem really exciting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but...is that sword of fire actually, like, <i>good.</i> How reliable are those blinding sparks against actually magic opponents? How much does it cost to run up those walls? How strong is the shooting flames? My issue with the set is the <i>implementation,</i> that is to say, I felt distinctly uncool because the cool things I could pull off tended to be extremely limited, or buried in stuff like &quot;Negate a single point of penalty, or three points in Aura&quot;, which is just...not a Charm any Exalt should have to pay XP for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:23:12-07:00","id":1236624,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"800\" data-vbnamecard=\"800\">Fenrir666</a> I'm fairly confident all of those things would straight up annihilate mortals. Now, how would they do against a Solar? Well, we're putting that to the test right now - not against a combat Solar, but against the kind of Solars that a lot of players make at chargen. I would expect that most celestial Exalted would wipe the floor with him if they are kitted right (as it should be), and a lot of Solars would be able to straight up handle him (as it should be), but those aren't the kinds of enemies I would throw against a Dragon-Blood, and when I ran a DB game, I didn't. I threw ghosts at them, spider mutants, normal mortals, etc. That made for a really fun game. If we were playing with Third Edition rules, it would have been a LOT more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:40:32-07:00","id":1236628,"title":"","content":"I usually play online via irc, but, if I was going to do an in person DB game with 3e, I\u2019d probably get a set of these dice to make keeping track of aura pretty simple. I suppose I\u2019d need a white gel pen to handle one side, but they mostly work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://smile.amazon.com/SmartDealsPro-Blank-Different-Teaching-Plastic/dp/B010RY4RHA/ref=sr_1_3?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1531960528&amp;sr=8-3&amp;keywords=Color+dice\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://smile.amazon.com/SmartDealsPro-Blank-Different-Teaching-Plastic/dp/B010RY4RHA/ref=sr_1_3?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1531960528&amp;sr=8-3&amp;keywords=Color+dice\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://smile.amazon.com/SmartDealsPro-Blank-Different-Teaching-Plastic/dp/B010RY4RHA/ref=sr_1_3?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1531960528&amp;sr=8-3&amp;keywords=Color+dice\" target=\"_blank\"> https://smile.amazon.com/SmartDealsPro-Blank-Different-Teaching-Plastic/dp/B010RY4RHA/ref=sr_1_3?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1531960528&amp;sr=8-3&amp;keywords=Color+dice </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:42:06-07:00","id":1236629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236624#post1236624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"800\" data-vbnamecard=\"800\">Fenrir666</a> I'm fairly confident all of those things would straight up annihilate mortals. Now, how would they do against a Solar? Well, we're putting that to the test right now - not against a combat Solar, but against the kind of Solars that a lot of players make at chargen. I would expect that most celestial Exalted would wipe the floor with him if they are kitted right (as it should be), and a lot of Solars would be able to straight up handle him (as it should be), but those aren't the kinds of enemies I would throw against a Dragon-Blood, and when I ran a DB game, I didn't. I threw ghosts at them, spider mutants, normal mortals, etc. That made for a really fun game. If we were playing with <b>Third Edition rules</b>, it would have been a LOT more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait your are not actually using 3e rules? Have you played 3e dragonblooded at all in a game or just white room scenario's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:47:40-07:00","id":1236632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236620#post1236620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really can't think of any situation where reflexively summoning any weapon you can think of on the fly would be useful?<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, hey, I need to grapple that dude on the horse. Too bad I don't have a whip...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Man, I could really use something with the thrown tag right now&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, hey, I need to run over there but there are arrows and shit. I wish I had a shield&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't think of any situation where the utility of being able to do so outweighs the utility of <i>not dying because my main defense suddenly became inapplicable</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T17:48:38-07:00","id":1236633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236587#post1236587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3559_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3559\" data-vbnamecard=\"3559\">Lanaya</a> You make some compelling points to be sure. I just can\u2019t help but think, though, that I just made a Fire Aspect in an attempt to disprove some of these things written here (specifically he has no Martial Arts or Artifacts), and I\u2019m still very excited to play him. He can form a sword out of pure fire, shoot flame from his hands, run up walls, throw blinding sparks out to medium range that blinds for 3 rounds, and a bunch of other cool stuff. I didn\u2019t feel like I was being held back. I was actually surprised by how much coolness I could fit in there. Sure, I bought about 4 excellencies, but I also got two more Charms from BP, and 13 non-excellency Charms is WAY beyond what starting DBs had in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll make a few more just to see if I get that same annoyance that you feel (a few more of these non-MA, non-Artifact characters), but they all seem really exciting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with any of that. I'm not hating WFHW, despite my problems with it. I could rant for far longer about flaws in the design of Solars and their charmset, but that hasn't stopped me from having a blast playing them over and over again. But there's a big difference between a situation where you can have fun despite flaws in the design and one where those flaws don't exist. I'm just a bit disappointed with DBs having a big roadblock shoved in their way. You <i>can </i>get around it and have fun regardless, and I'm sure that I will, but it would have been so much easier if the problem just hadn't been put there in the first place. C'est la vie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T18:00:25-07:00","id":1236636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236629#post1236629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait your are not actually using 3e rules? Have you played 3e dragonblooded at all in a game or just white room scenario's?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the DB 3e rules are fairly recent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T19:45:47-07:00","id":1236656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236629#post1236629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait your are not actually using 3e rules? Have you played 3e dragonblooded at all in a game or just white room 