play experience with Dragonblooded within the Exalted third edition ruleset?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T20:15:01-07:00","id":1236659,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar223_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"223\" data-vbnamecard=\"223\">Calboon</a> I\u2019ve made a few characters and have run them through some tests of mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T23:13:53-07:00","id":1236684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236372#post1236372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just for those who kick-started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um....I did contribute to that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T23:44:31-07:00","id":1236686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236684#post1236684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um....I did contribute to that</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about the preview PDFs from the Kickstarter; the book itself hasn't been released yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T01:00:22-07:00","id":1236690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236621#post1236621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Negate a single point of penalty, or three points in Aura&quot;, which is just...not a Charm any Exalt should have to pay XP for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what do you think the floor for Exalted power should be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T02:30:28-07:00","id":1236700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236632#post1236632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can't think of any situation where the utility of being able to do so outweighs the utility of <i>not dying because my main defense suddenly became inapplicable</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does it need to? I was pointing out that the charm is extremely useful even if you still have your primary weapon to hand. <br /> <br /> And really, while we can debate whether it's the equivalent of call the blade or gss all day, in truth, it's neither. It's Dragon Graced Weapon, a completely different charms that sort of combines the utility of both. And that's kind of like a bonus power. The <i>intended</i> use is to boost the jade weapon the prerequisite requires. That's why it has that as a prerequisite. <br /> <br /> The charm isn't &quot;shitty call the blade&quot; it's &quot;supercharge jade weapons and also make any mundane weapon you need on the fly, which will also be boosted&quot; You're looking at one possible application of an extremely versatile charm and acting like that's all it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T02:47:23-07:00","id":1236701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236700#post1236700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The charm isn't &quot;shitty call the blade&quot; it's &quot;supercharge jade weapons and also make any mundane weapon you need on the fly, which will also be boosted&quot; You're looking at one possible application of an extremely versatile charm and acting like that's all it does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't claim it's &quot;shitty call the blade&quot;, I claimed it's <i>part of a larger design pattern</i> where always useful basic effects (negate defense penalties, deal more damage, defend yourself from being disarmed) are locked away behind more situational effects, and that it has a ridiculously overinflated ability score prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The whole ridiculous tangent about which solar charm is it equivalent to (which, by the way, <i>you</i> started) actually has nothing to do with the point I originally made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T03:20:40-07:00","id":1236708,"title":"","content":"Is it though? The only thing between it and the excellency is Elemental sheath, which I'd hardly call situational. And the prerequisite is a result of it being a side benefit of a much more powerful charm. <br /> <br /> <i>That</i>, I grant you, may be a flaw in the design, but at the same time, maybe it isn't? Because if <i>everyone</i> can easily recover from being disarmed it kinda cheapens the gambit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, yeah, you can knock weapons out of people's hands. Don't bother though. It's just a waste of a turn 90% of the time. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T03:49:21-07:00","id":1236715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236708#post1236708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it though? The only thing between it and the excellency is Elemental sheath, which I'd hardly call situational. And the prerequisite is a result of it being a side benefit of a much more powerful charm. </div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Elemental Sheath is literally useless to anybody without a jade artifact weapon.\u200b With Signature Charms being head and shoulders above anything else in the Dragon-Blooded arsenal while also being universally gated behind an ability 5 prerequisite, I think the set already has a pretty big problem with enforcing a level of mechanical optimization that, viewed through the lens of what the individual ability ratings represent, heavily strains my suspension of disbelief; funneling meleeists into picking a jade weapon no matter what is a tremendously unhelpful addition to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236708#post1236708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That</i>, I grant you, may be a flaw in the design, but at the same time, maybe it isn't? Because if <i>everyone</i> can easily recover from being disarmed it kinda cheapens the gambit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, yeah, you can knock weapons out of people's hands. Don't bother though. It's just a waste of a turn 90% of the time. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, this is actually a valid line of argument - but I think it's balanced out by the anima requisite (forcing characters who don't juggle out of aspect aura states a lot to give up free damage) and the relatively high cost (4m versus CtB's 1m). <br /> <br /> (Incidentally, this is why I really like Root-and-Hand Merging: it's expensive enough that you can't afford to always have it on, and it doesn't just undo the effect of a Disarm gambit - but it makes the option difficult and expensive enough to force your opponent to think deep and hard about whether they want to risk it. Too bad it's at least 32 sessions until you can pick it.)<br /> <br /> Another insidious effect of the Melee 5 prerequisite on Dragon-Graced Weapon is how it funnels weapons-only martial artists towards IMA. &quot;Welp, I can't just dip into Melee to defend myself from being disarmed, I clearly need a secondary combat ability I can rely on... and I already paid for the Martial Artist merit... and unlocking the ability to ignore Terrestrial restrictions would be <i>really really nice</i>...&quot; Whether that's a good or a bad thing is left to the reader's imagination.<br /> <br /> (It's the same issue with Elemental Sheath, actually - the set naturally funnels the players towards the most effective builds, but it has the side effect of screwing over players who knowingly forgo their most powerful options twice as hard.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T04:48:15-07:00","id":1236721,"title":"","content":"I guess the way I see it is if you can \u201cshape a sword from the razor-sharp edge of a biting gale\u201d, you must be one of the greatest swordsmen in the entire world. I\u2019m glad they kept it at Essence 2 so that we can have it at chargen, but Melee 5 does seem appropriate for such an awesome move.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a particularly great sword anyway. A more optimized build would just carry a 4-dot Artifact blade and be done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T05:50:45-07:00","id":1236734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236721#post1236721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the way I see it is if you can \u201cshape a sword from the razor-sharp edge of a biting gale\u201d, you must be one of the greatest swordsmen in the entire world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not really seeing the causal relationship there.<br /> <br /> In the Solar set, sure - Solars are the unparalleled masters of all human endeavors, so if you want something blatantly supernatural, you better be already the best at the skill it's related to. Dragon-Blooded, however, channel their expressions of raw elemental fury through the medium of human abilities. A Solar can create a sword out of nothing as the ultimate expression of her self-identity as a swordsman (swordsperson?); a Dragon-Blooded can create a sword out of an element because she can already manipulate elements by default (see also: anima powers), and she only has to channel this natural talent towards the purpose of arming herself.<br /> <br /> (Also, even in 1E, the &quot;make a sword out of your element&quot; Charm only wanted you to have 4 dots in Melee.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:19:43-07:00","id":1236739,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's basically the same logic. A solar gets so good with a weapon they can hit you with the manifested form of that skill alone. A dragonblooded gets good enough at channelling the elements through a weapon that they no longer need the weapon to shape them. <br /> <br /> If a DB wants to just hit people with an element there are other charms for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:36:06-07:00","id":1236743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236739#post1236739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dragonblooded gets good enough at channelling the elements through a weapon that they no longer need the weapon to shape them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why does a 3E Dragon-Blooded need to be better at swording than their 1E equivalent to do that?<br /> <br /> (&quot;Because the relevant Charm does more&quot; is kind of a copout answer, since we're talking about the way a given splat expresses their power through skills, which should be system-agnostic.)<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: You know what, there is a better question we should ask:<br /> <br /> Glorious Solar Saber<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins: Melee 3, Essence 2</b><br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Summoning the Loyal Steel<br /> <br /> Why is a Dragon-Blood's ability to express her swordsmanship skills by arming herself with a spontaneously created weapon more strongly tied to her ability to wield weapons than that of the splat <i>whose entire powerset is based on their expression of skill?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-19-2018, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:59:28-07:00","id":1236752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236545#post1236545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My <i>thing</i> is finding combos in mechanics. What Fire Has Wrought does not offer much in way of appeal. &quot;Wow, if I optimize really hard I...don't suck completely, woo.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're largely starting from a false premise, that of &quot;your baseline is a loser&quot;. Of course you will be disappointed, you are actively looking for that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T08:28:53-07:00","id":1236782,"title":"","content":"I have to second Synapse here. Of course not every book will be fore everyone, but my experience from actual play is that you can do a whole lot with the starting dots an Exalted Character receives, of course DBs aren't going to scratch the spheres of Solar Awesome, power-wise, but there's a lot of space for them to exist in, and especially if you don't try to go 1on1 with Anathema you can have a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> It is true, however, that Exalted already makes you track a lot of resources, even when you're not a Single Point stylist wielding Stormcaller, and we hardly needed another thing to track with Aura. On the other hand I've seen worse ideas, it is pretty fun in theory. I, too, am one of the people who would like to have to track less things, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T08:43:29-07:00","id":1236784,"title":"","content":"Without Aura, you have the Dragon-Blooded of previous editions.<br /> <br /> With Aura, you can achieve more.<br /> <br /> When you play Warframe, nothing demands that you learn how to slide into a super jump followed by a double jump, or how to use your three special abillities, or even just your melee weapon. You could use nothing but your firearm and be just fine. Treat it like a cover-based shooter game.<br /> <br /> But achieving the absolute best performance with your character requires mastering her resources.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are the Exalted who have to spend the most time learning how to be awesome. They start early as kids and go to school specifically to learn from other Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Having a deeper and more complex meta-game to their Charms than Solars honestly seems to fit. A player starts out powerful and learns through experience (or the wisdom of those who came before) how to maximize their potential.<br /> <br /> Also, the Dragon-Blooded are fueled by five different, conflicting elemental Essences. Naturally you can\u2019t always blend Air and Earth seemlessly together.<br /> <br /> Usually, \u201cachieving balance\u201d is about doing two, irreconcilable things in turns, rather than at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T08:44:51-07:00","id":1236785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236721#post1236721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the way I see it is if you can \u201cshape a sword from the razor-sharp edge of a biting gale\u201d, you must be one of the greatest swordsmen in the entire world. I\u2019m glad they kept it at Essence 2 so that we can have it at chargen, but Melee 5 does seem appropriate for such an awesome move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ability 5 <i>can</i> seem appropriate to just about any Charm that it's attached to, but I don't think the logic behind the Charm was necessarily predicated on it requiring the user to be among the best sword wielders in the world.<br /> <br /> I do agree with the idea that, for these and for Solars, it's unfortunate that <b>so</b> many Charms have that minimum. Not just because of what that does for playing them, but the sense of what they're like as people in the world. I believe that somebody else already brought up the point that it creates the weird distortion for the Dragon Blooded in particular where there are ever many thousands of them that are the best in the world at things, or else there are a significant number that can barely develop their powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T09:07:40-07:00","id":1236795,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I completely agree that such a thing seems very weird. It seems out of step with the way they\u2019ve defined the various \u201cpower levels\u201d of the 1-5 dots in Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T09:39:41-07:00","id":1236805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236743#post1236743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is a Dragon-Blood's ability to express her swordsmanship skills by arming herself with a spontaneously created weapon more strongly tied to her ability to wield weapons than that of the splat <i>whose entire powerset is based on their expression of skill?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You forget that Dragon Bloods are just as much ability-based as solars are. They express this power differently but being the best in [<i>ability</i>] still defines everything that Dragon Bloods can acheive, just as it does so for solars.<br /> <br /> Various quotes from the Devs on the design philosophy of solars vs DB:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1175295#post1175295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as Abyssal Charms branch out and develop, they emulate the themes and powers of the Deathlords,<b> much as those of the Solars emulate the Unconquered Sun</b>. An Abyssal who serves the Mask of Winters (or no Deathlord at all!) is free to take Charms that invoke the themes of the Silver Prince or the First and Forsaken Lion.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1196054#post1196054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a thematic perspective, Abyssals have less need to rely on non-soulsteel Evocations to access &quot;out-there&quot; effects. Unlike the <b>Solar Charms, which progress towards the singular point that is the Unconquered Sun's mythos</b>, Abyssal Charms spiral out in a bunch of thematic directions as they build on the themes of the many Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1220046#post1220046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Charms are manifestations of superhuman power of the Attributes, often expressed through their shapeshifting. As their power progresses, it diverges from pure applications of Attributes to emulate the miracles of the witch-goddess Luna, much as <b>Solars move towards emulating the Unconquered Sun</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And perhaps the most important one:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1144744#post1144744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aesthetics of a Charmset are typically gradated through its progression. <b>For example, both Solar and Dragon-Blooded Charms at the lower end begin as expressions of superhuman skill, but Solars progress towards embodying the divine perfection of the Unconquered Sun while the Dragon-Blooded progress towards overt manipulation of elements and embodiment of elemental Essence.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Solars in 3E are not about 'being the best X in the world anymore. They may definitely become the best in the world in their field of expertise, but they're more focused and channeling and emulating the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> It's not about being based on expressions of skill in either case. Or at least, no more for one than the other. I think this is something that a lot of people have missed about 3E and it is SO IMPORTANT!<br /> <br /> You can set out to be the greatest swordsman in the world as either a solar OR a Dragon Blood. Both will be able to do things that the other cannot dream about. Will a solar defeat a dragon blood in one-on-one combat in a duel, at Essence 5 with an even playing field? I think it's likely but honestly I don't know. I know it would be a hell of a closer match than in any other edition, and that it would be a hell of a show, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T09:57:45-07:00","id":1236811,"title":"","content":"While I agree with you, Armyofwhispers, that they're ability-based Exalts and so it's fine for their magic stuff to be based on ability levels, I think Isator is right about the general trend of requiring high ability scores being problematic.<br /> <br /> I already find that the character gen encourages optimisation, and a lot of players start with a smaller number of very high ability scores* (though it depends on the players) rather than a range. I don't really see the need for charms to further encourage that.<br /> <br /> *When I first saw people complaining about how awkward it was that it required Melee 5, my initial thought was &quot;I don't understand why they're complaining, what character who favours melee as their primary ability doesn't have Melee 5 at character gen?&quot;<br /> That's probably not a good attitude, but it's what my experience has got me used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:13:53-07:00","id":1236817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236805#post1236805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars in 3E are not about 'being the best X in the world anymore. They may definitely become the best in the world in their field of expertise, but they're more focused and channeling and emulating the Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And what does the Unconquered Sun represent?<br /> <br /> (Hint: it's not &quot;glowy stuff&quot;.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236811#post1236811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*When I first saw people complaining about how awkward it was that it required Melee 5, my initial thought was &quot;I don't understand why they're complaining, what character who favours melee as their primary ability doesn't have Melee 5 at character gen?&quot;<br /> That's probably not a good attitude, but it's what my experience has got me used to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the <i>worst </i>attitude to have in a party-based role-playing game. When everybody is special, nobody is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:27:49-07:00","id":1236821,"title":"","content":"But everybody isn't special, just the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:37:11-07:00","id":1236824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236821#post1236821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But everybody isn't special, just the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet the player who thought being the party's combat monster is the coolest shit in the world will be very happy when it turns out that the four other people she's traveling with also happen to have reached complete mastery of their respective ways of combat.<br /> <br /> Even if they are a bureaucrat, a sorcerer, a craftsman and a doctor, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:37:24-07:00","id":1236825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236821#post1236821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But everybody isn't special, just the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Halfway through a game, you'll notice that charms may as well not have ability minimums because the enemy exalts will have as many as they need., If only to provide a challenge to the party. The ability mins could stand to be toned down because as is all it means is that you are going to fight a lot of beings who will already meet them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:43:02-07:00","id":1236828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236817#post1236817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This is the <i>worst </i>attitude to have in a party-based role-playing game. When everybody is special, nobody is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. But it's what I'm used to.<br /> Most (not all, but most) Solars turn up with Dex 4-5 and 5 in a combat ability. The difference of course, is the charms, but on a day-to-day level, you get exactly the thing you pointed out; it doesn't really feel you're that special when most of the rest of the party has a 5 in that ability (even if one character has 10 melee charms; after all, you've all got the same number of dice, because you all have excellencies).<br /> <br /> 4 of the 5 Solars in the game I play have Melee 5. None of them is supposed to be the world's greatest swordsman. But I mean, what are we going to do, <i>not</i> have Melee 5? How would Golden Hero get his demon-killing charms? How, more importantly, would the Adamant-circle sorceress and the Cult of the Illuminated preacher get Heavenly Guardian Defence? How would Fulgens the warlord get... actually I'm not sure he has any Melee charms beyond excellent strike. But, you know, what self-respecting warlord doesn't have Melee 5?<br /> The only one who doesn't have a combat ability at 5 is the player who doesn't really like combat and wanted to be a 99% social character.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it's only combat abilities, I see plenty of characters who only have a few dots of social abilities.<br /> And it's slightly better than it used to be, because everyone is fed up of the way it works like that (and I changed the character gen rules to discourage it). Yet they still do it a bit, because the rules reward you for doing it and punish you for not doing it.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I didn't really think of this until you guys started talking about it (I just put it down to optimisation), but I can see it. Decent charms not requiring 5 in abilities would definitely help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-19-2018, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:47:41-07:00","id":1236830,"title":"","content":"If you can think of a way of making rules that don't reward maxing out your stats, I'm all ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:58:38-07:00","id":1236832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236825#post1236825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Halfway through a game, you'll notice that charms may as well not have ability minimums because the enemy exalts will have as many as they need., If only to provide a challenge to the party. The ability mins could stand to be toned down because as is all it means is that you are going to fight a lot of beings who will already meet them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find that halfway through a game is when people start paying attention to ability minimums.<br /> <br /> Initially, PCs have 5 in all the abilities they really care about, and 3 in the ones they kind of care about (which is enough to get, like, 1-2 charms).<br /> Halfway through the game they start buying dots in other abilities that they become interested in (for example, a few dots of Occult because of all the magic, or a few dots of Socialise because they keep going to parties), and then they start thinking about getting some charms, and find that they need to buy their abilities up a bit higher.<br /> For example, I played a Twilight once, and halfway through the game people kept telling me I needed some defensive charms, so I slowly bought up Dodge from 0, and I had to buy it quite high to get Seven Shadow Evasion.<br /> (I didn't need it. I was fine. It was 2nd ed and I had the Twilight anima banner.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:59:18-07:00","id":1236833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236828#post1236828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. But it's what I'm used to.<br /> Most (not all, but most) Solars turn up with Dex 4-5 and 5 in a combat ability. The difference of course, is the charms, but on a day-to-day level, you get exactly the thing you pointed out; it doesn't really feel you're that special when most of the rest of the party has a 5 in that ability.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it's only combat abilities, I see plenty of characters who only have a few dots of social abilities.<br /> And it's slightly better than it used to be, because everyone is fed up of the way it works like that (and I changed the character gen rules to discourage it). Yet they still do it a bit, because the rules reward you for doing it and punish you for not doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I generally abide by a rule of &quot;only one stat at 5, no ability above 3 unless it's a large part of my character's concept&quot;. Solars are actually amazing for this - you can throw your Charms around to the point of not having more than 3 in any single ability (including your Supernal), and just by virtue of the free excellencies and the strength of starting Charms, you'll still have a viable and fun to play character at the end.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded require a bit more finagling, but after playing them a bit (we've had like four sessions), I find that the combination of having to purchase excellencies and kinda crappy low-level Charms is weirdly helpful - you can use a good 40% of your starting Charms to start with a reliable broad expertise, and you'll still be able to meaningfully contribute in your secondary areas of focus while ceding the spotlight when it comes to challenges you're completely unsuited to. (Also, the Ability 1 prerequisite on excellencies means that you can get away with dropping a few in favor of cooler stuff in your primary area of expertise, then picking them up one by one in play on a &quot;whenever needed&quot; basis, because the training time is literally just &quot;spend half an afternoon on this&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:03:30-07:00","id":1236836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236832#post1236832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find that halfway through a game is when people start paying attention to ability minimums.<br /> <br /> Initially, PCs have 5 in all the abilities they really care about, and 3 in the ones they kind of care about (which is enough to get, like, 1-2 charms).<br /> Halfway through the game they start buying dots in other abilities that they become interested in (for example, a few dots of Occult because of all the magic, or a few dots of Socialise because they keep going to parties), and then they start thinking about getting some charms, and find that they need to buy their abilities up a bit higher.<br /> For example, I played a Twilight once, and halfway through the game people kept telling me I needed some defensive charms, so I slowly bought up Dodge from 0, and I had to buy it quite high to get Seven Shadow Evasion.<br /> (I didn't need it. I was fine. It was 2nd ed and I had the Twilight anima banner.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that for enemies. The fact is regardless of how the world is intended to be, the characters the PCs are facing will scale with them as necessary.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:08:09-07:00","id":1236839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236830#post1236830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can think of a way of making rules that don't reward maxing out your stats, I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried replacing bonus points with 50xp, but it didn't really work. People didn't max out as many stats, admittedly, but they still had 2 or 3 abilities at 5 (but then, that's not 5, so maybe it works a bit). I gave up in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:14:32-07:00","id":1236841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236830#post1236830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can think of a way of making rules that don't reward maxing out your stats, I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Flat XP costs and a Charm structure where about 50% of a given tree's Charms have prereqs in the 1-3 range, another 30% wants you to have 4 dots, and only the top 20% mandates having 5 would be a start.<br /> <br /> (Maxing out your stats will still be <i>really good</i> - it's basically the equivalent of a Permanent Charm that adds a non-Charm bonus die on every relevant action and allows you to raise your excellency cap by 1, except it's cheaper than buying an extra Charm -, but at least you won't feel like you're actively being punished for not jumping on the 5 train.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:52:29-07:00","id":1236848,"title":"","content":"I mean, I do actually know how to stop everyone maxing out their abilities.<br /> I really hope I can convince my friends to play the all-Lunars game I've always wanted to do.<br /> In my experience, not having the favoured ability BP cost reduction (only the 25% off on favoured attributes), and the way putting 5 in one attribute screws another attribute that your character probably wants, really does encourage more balanced characters. And even if half of them do have Dex 5, very few have 5 in a combat ability (or any ability, tbh: in 2nd ed a lot had Martial Arts 5 as it was favoured, but in 3rd ed I don't think any of the 4 Lunars I've seen played had/have any abilities at 5).<br /> <br /> That doesn't help with DBs or Solars though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-19-2018, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:28:32-07:00","id":1236858,"title":"","content":"I've toyed with changing all the ability mins: what was 1-2 becomes 1, 3 become 2 and 4/5s become 3. That along with an agreement that PCs (and NPCs) have skill levels that makes sense for their concept should allow everyone to shine in their area and get the charms they want/need without having 5s in everything by the end of a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:35:41-07:00","id":1236879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236841#post1236841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Flat XP costs and a Charm structure where about 50% of a given tree's Charms have prereqs in the 1-3 range, another 30% wants you to have 4 dots, and only the top 20% mandates having 5 would be a start.<br /> <br /> (Maxing out your stats will still be <i>really good</i> - it's basically the equivalent of a Permanent Charm that adds a non-Charm bonus die on every relevant action and allows you to raise your excellency cap by 1, except it's cheaper than buying an extra Charm -, but at least you won't feel like you're actively being punished for not jumping on the 5 train.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I disagree with flat XP costs here. The chargen/xp split gives a big encouragement to get 5s early, so pure flat costs is probably better than mixed, but pure scaling costs would make getting 5s at any time be a higher cost, and getting 1-3s be cheaper. (It would have the classic scaling cost drawback of being a pain to calculate, but that's mostly distinct from the incentive structure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:10:55-07:00","id":1236896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236817#post1236817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what does the Unconquered Sun represent?<br /> <br /> (Hint: it's not &quot;glowy stuff&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at the high end solar charms for your answer.<br /> <br /> But my point is that Solars are no more based on abilities than Dragon Bloods are. They're based on expressing the Power of the Unconquered Sun via their abilities. <br /> <br /> Dragon Bloods are expressing the themes of their elemental blood expressed through their abilities. <br /> <br /> I fully expect that Abyssals, Infernals, Sidereals, and Getimians will all have different ability minimums for roughly similar effects simply because each one is expressing different themes and those themes work better for different effects.<br /> <br /> We could see infernals forge a weapon out of the air at melee 1 because it's easier to cause damage without external aid by channeling adjorjan's themes than it is for a solar to pull one out of pure excellence or a DB to create one out of elemental essence. <br /> <br /> It's honestly pretty disingenuous to the writers to make these kind of comparisons. A better way of asking these questions would be to say: What level of mastery does it make sense for a Dragon Blood to pull a weapon out of thin air? Or: What level of mastery does it make sense for a Solar to pull a weapon out of thin air? Obviously the writers felt that a Dragon Blood had to master swordsmanship to a greater extent because that fits with the overarching themes of DB and their power structure as a whole. Whereas a solar swordsman of 'expert' level should be able to do so as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T15:15:28-07:00","id":1236918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236833#post1236833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally abide by a rule of &quot;only one stat at 5, no ability above 3 unless it's a large part of my character's concept&quot;. Solars are actually amazing for this - you can throw your Charms around to the point of not having more than 3 in any single ability (including your Supernal), and just by virtue of the free excellencies and the strength of starting Charms, you'll still have a viable and fun to play character at the end.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded require a bit more finagling, but after playing them a bit (we've had like four sessions), I find that the combination of having to purchase excellencies and kinda crappy low-level Charms is weirdly helpful - you can use a good 40% of your starting Charms to start with a reliable broad expertise, and you'll still be able to meaningfully contribute in your secondary areas of focus while ceding the spotlight when it comes to challenges you're completely unsuited to. (Also, the Ability 1 prerequisite on excellencies means that you can get away with dropping a few in favor of cooler stuff in your primary area of expertise, then picking them up one by one in play on a &quot;whenever needed&quot; basis, because the training time is literally just &quot;spend half an afternoon on this&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have a very similar chargen rule when I'm the storyteller. Only one attribute or ability (players choice) can start at 5. No starting abilities above 3 dots without significant backstory explaining higher proficiency, and even in those cases, no more then three abilities above 3. This rule is specifically for Solars. I haven't yet run a Dragonblood game, but I would probably relax the limitations a bit due to the unique education Dragonbloods receive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T15:25:45-07:00","id":1236920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236879#post1236879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I disagree with flat XP costs here. The chargen/xp split gives a big encouragement to get 5s early, so pure flat costs is probably better than mixed, but pure scaling costs would make getting 5s at any time be a higher cost, and getting 1-3s be cheaper. (It would have the classic scaling cost drawback of being a pain to calculate, but that's mostly distinct from the incentive structure).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, man, but... have you ever tried making an Ars Magica character?<br /> <br /> I'd rather take flat costs and immediately intuitive/easy-to-use chargen over scaling costs that serve my stated purpose better, because a game that is imperfect but actually gets off the ground is better than a game that <i>might have been</i> amazing if the group hadn't abandoned it after the fourth session of chipping away at the massive hurdle that is character creation. (This is literally a thing that happened to us and Shadowrun 5E, and that game doesn't even have scaling costs!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236896#post1236896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly pretty disingenuous to the writers to make these kind of comparisons. A better way of asking these questions would be to say: What level of mastery does it make sense for a Dragon Blood to pull a weapon out of thin air? Or: What level of mastery does it make sense for a Solar to pull a weapon out of thin air? Obviously the writers felt that a Dragon Blood had to master swordsmanship to a greater extent because that fits with the overarching themes of DB and their power structure as a whole. Whereas a solar swordsman of 'expert' level should be able to do so as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really don't want this to come across as overly harsh, but, uh, neither of those provides an explanation? &quot;It is so because the devs decided that this is appropriate&quot; is a tautology - <i>everything in the book</i> is there in its current form because the devs decided that's the way it is appropriate for them to be there. &quot;It is so because themes&quot; is meaningless unless you actually explain how those themes manifest.<br /> <br /> Allow me to provide an example:<br /> <br /> Solars embody the themes of the Unconquered Sun in their Charmset. As they grow in Essence, they emulate the perfection of the Unconquered Sun in all of their endeavors.<i>Therefore</i> it makes sense for their Charms to come with high ability prerequisites - if you fail to constantly strive to perfect yourself in the most basic foundations of your abilities, how could you possibly grasp the deeper mysteries of the divine essence that courses through your veins?<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Dragon-Blooded Charmset expresses the Exalt's growing command over the elements. They start out with fairly straightforward expressions of pure skill tinged with elemental symbolism, but as they progress in Essence, their ability to influence natural phenomena grows more overt, until it blossoms into literal command over the elements themselves.<br /> <br /> One of these themes lends itself well to the ability to create an item out of nothing. The other one, not so much.<br /> <br /> Yet apparently it is harder for the &quot;as I grow in power, I gain control over the elements&quot; splat to <i>create a sword out of natural elements</i> than it is for the &quot;I emulate the perfection of the Unconquered Sun through my skills&quot; splat to sword so hard that their ability to do so literally becomes a sword.<br /> <br /> Thus Spake Zaram\u00f8rke:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see Glorious Solar Saber as summoning a magic blade, but rather the blade as a fundamental outgrowth of your skill, your anima bursting outward and hardening into the shape of that skill to form a weapon. It is your soul made physical.<br /> (...)<br /> [Glorious Solar Saber] comes out of the sword as an outgrowth, an extension of his hand, his spirit. (...) He wouldn't ever feel like he has the power to form objects of light. Only the power to manifest pieces of his soul that he has spent a long time forging through skill and practice. </div> </div> </div>Glorious Solar Saber is a transcendent miracle made possible only by such a dedication to wielding weapons that doing so became a fundamental part of who you are. The other Charm is a fancy way to control the elements, an extension of the most basic capability any Dragon-Blooded can just do by default.<br /> <br /> <i>Yet the latter requires a deeper dedication to swordsmanship than the former.</i><br /> <br /> The <i>entire point</i> of my complaint is that there is a discrepancy between the themes expressed by the placement of these Charms in the context of their respective charmsets and the mechanical requirements of obtaining them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T18:24:02-07:00","id":1236966,"title":"","content":"But what if we look at it like this: remember that the books are always saying that the Charms are not actually named magic powers that the characters have, but are just written that way for us - the readers - so that we can remember them. In all actuality, what is being represented by these Charms are the inner strengths and wonders that the characters are able to achieve.<br /> <br /> So, if that's the case, then how could someone who is only the best swordsman in town (Melee 3) do some of the things that are covered by these Charms that currently have Melee minimums of 4 or 5?<br /> <br /> Think of it in Superman terms. Let's say you want to create Superman as an Exalt type that focuses on Attributes instead of Abilities. And you want him to have a Charm that is called &quot;Stronger than a Locomotive&quot; that will allow him to stop a train running at full speed. Well, how can the minimum Strength for that Charm be anything less than 5? We think of the power coming from the Charm, but it's actually coming from the character. The Charm is just a way for us players to keep track of what's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T18:26:19-07:00","id":1236967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236920#post1236920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glorious Solar Saber is a transcendent miracle made possible only by such a dedication to wielding weapons that doing so became a fundamental part of who you are. The other Charm is a fancy way to control the elements, an extension of the most basic capability any Dragon-Blooded can just do by default.<br /> <br /> <i>Yet the latter requires a deeper dedication to swordsmanship than the former.</i><br /> <br /> The <i>entire point</i> of my complaint is that there is a discrepancy between the themes expressed by the placement of these Charms in the context of their respective charmsets and the mechanical requirements of obtaining them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason for this is simple. The ability to wield a sword is naturally sword-shaped, whilst the elements are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T23:27:11-07:00","id":1237034,"title":"","content":"I think the GSS vs DGW thing is kind of a moot point because they're pretty much incomparable. Solars get to summon an artifact weapon at melee 3 because Solars are extremely powerful. DBs on the other hand get a charm that they can use to almost always buff their already artifact weapon, which makes it more powerful than GSS because it enhances an already artifact weapon. Also any DB can get this from chargen whereas almost every Solar needs to wait 12 sessions before they get to start using theirs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than that I'm seeing a few problems here that I might be able to clear up with the limited wordcount I have.<br /> <br /> <b>DB Charms Suck in Power Level</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, compared to Solars they definitely do, they're closer to mortal power levels than any other splat. The thing is, you need to start thinking more like a mortal to be effective. Things like the weapons with the Smashing or Chopping tag are actually important, you need to rely on your artifact weapon to give you more of your edge, as well as teamwork. I've played several games with DBs using the new rules and my players have torn through packs of claw striders and Dogs of the Unbroken Earth.<br /> <br /> Admittedly there was a little more back and forth there than I'd expect from a Solar group, but I liked that. Rather than just have the Dawn one-two AoE combo the group to death by herself the party had to work together. They also had to rely more on things like the small army they brought with them, and making clever deals and compromises rather than just ploughing through everything with their power.<br /> <br /> The one thing I will say is that it sucks to be so far from the super cool Essence 3 signature charms, since most games I know barely run long enough to get more than a session of play out of them. DBs are maybe supposed to be a slower burn game.<br /> <br /> <b>DB Charms are too heavily skewed to high ability dots</b><br /> <br /> Yeah they are. But lets not pretend like Solar trees are immune to this either. Sail doesn't even have one charm that's prerequisite is Sail 1, or Sail 2 for that matter.<br /> <br /> <b>Purchasing DB Excellencies is Restrictive</b><br /> <br /> Yes, but only at chargen, and only if you spread yourself thin. Which I encourage you to do. As a DB you're going to pick up 19 charms, not counting sorcery, MA or evocations, before you hit Essence 3. So you'll have a total of 34 charms by then. That's 2 charms away from buying every single Lore, Dodge, Archery, and Bureaucracy charm, to pick trees at random. So unless you're planning on being a complete master of 4 different trees, you can definitely afford to spread yourself out around 6-7, with some dips into a few more. It's that slow burn again.<br /> <br /> <b>Aura Sucks</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217268#post1217268\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...68#post1217268</a><br /> <br /> It may not be intuitive, which I understand might be a problem, but in the second half of that post &quot;Aspect&quot; I go into how to use aura effectively. Even being a fire aspect, who's specialty is using earth aspect charms inside the water aspected brawl tree. Just ignore the part where I talk about entering aura pre-combat, it's harder to do that I thought.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah also I forgot in the FIRST half of that post I talk about why being a DB martial artist is way cooler than being a Solar one, as long as the Solar isn't MA supernal, since you've got like, an 18 session lead on them. Or 4.5 months for a weekly game.<br /> <br /> <br /> It isn't for everyone, but DBs are a LOT less defined by their charms, and a LOT more defined by their merits and actual character. A Solar might be an amazing fighter who trained hard and can beat back an army with his bare hands, play a tear jerking flue tune, hurl an elephant through a stone wall, and leap over a mountain. He also heads a mercenary company, and has some contact in the guild.<br /> <br /> In contrast a DB is the Dragon Commander of the Fifth Eastern Fleet, granddaughter of The Ghost of the Sapphire isles, and keeper of Bal-Shara, the Jade Thunder direlance, who will stop at nothing to avenge her sister. Also she can lift a cart over her head, can hear through the earth, and can slay any mortal in single combat. The feats are less impressive and character defining, but that just makes the other flavours come out more.<br /> <br /> Also if you like being able to excellency almost anything you care to do, or hate how aura can change your combat style, or have difficulty finding fun in a game where you need to take things like essence 2 earth elementals seriously, then DBs aren't really for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 07-20-2018, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T02:12:07-07:00","id":1237059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236966#post1236966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it in Superman terms. Let's say you want to create Superman as an Exalt type that focuses on Attributes instead of Abilities. And you want him to have a Charm that is called &quot;Stronger than a Locomotive&quot; that will allow him to stop a train running at full speed. Well, how can the minimum Strength for that Charm be anything less than 5?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Since Charms represent the inner powers of a character, how could the ability to stand on a single blade of grass have anything less than an Athletics 5 prerequisite?&quot;<br /> <br /> (The &quot;Charms as discrete techniques anybody can learn&quot; versus &quot;Charms as mechanical abstractions that represent in-setting capabilities an individual character might have&quot; split has nothing to do with the issue being discussed.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(And frankly, I am somewhat insulted by the continued insistence on dragging Word of Dev into the discussion to attack points <i>I did not make</i>.)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237034#post1237034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>DB Charms are too heavily skewed to high ability dots</b><br /> <br /> Yeah they are. But lets not pretend like Solar trees are immune to this either. Sail doesn't even have one charm that's prerequisite is Sail 1, or Sail 2 for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;[Problem] is present in a different splat, too!&quot; does not make the problem not exist.<br /> <br /> Also, while it annoys me because it exacerbates the Glorious Golden Mary Sue problem, I can <i>understand</i> the design intent behind high ability minimums for Solar Charms: it incentivizes players to emulate the perfection of the Unconquered Sun in their abilities and provides midgame niche protection in conjunction with scaling ability costs by pushing players who'd like to branch out to stick with a broader suite of powerful lower Essence Charms instead of muscling into the territory of cool E3 tricks another player might like to feel are unique to them. I may not <i>like </i>this, but that's because I dislike the kind of heroic archetype Solars represent, and not because the design is wrong.<br /> <br /> DGW, on the other hand, represents a problem where a very basic capability is completely absent from a splat's native powerset unless one is willing to hyperspecialize. This is not a <i>huge</i> problem (you can carry a spare knife, there's a hearthstone that makes it harder for people to disarm you, picking a few dots in Brawl or Dodge won't kill you either, and if everything else fails, you can just make up an Evocation that deals with the issue), but to deny that the problem <i>exists in the first place</i> is pretty disingenuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T05:06:03-07:00","id":1237088,"title":"","content":"Been reading through up to now.<br /> <br /> I haven't tried a DBs game yet, and I'm fairly the opposite of a mechanics-monkey. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But, that said, the purchased-excellencies rule seems to me to be easy houserule fodder. Most especially if you want to have a mixed-splat Chronicle. <br /> <br /> It seems like a nice, self contained rule that's easy to binary-switch off and on, without having to dig through umpty-bajillion Charms to make power tweaks and bring everybody into the game.<br /> <br /> How much gap would it close between a DB and Solar, if the DB in the Circle also got free Excellencies within the scope of that game?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T05:21:21-07:00","id":1237095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237088#post1237088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much gap would it close between a DB and Solar, if the DB in the Circle also got free Excellencies within the scope of that game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A fair bit. Put them on equivalent XP tables, rule that only the DB can start with artifacts, push the player towards learning IMA, and you'll probably have a viable character on hand (especially if they know how to leverage their social advantages).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T05:25:49-07:00","id":1237097,"title":"","content":"Not much. At our table we decided to let chargen dbs build up to one aspected signature charm. For players it's just getting a really cool toy, for npcs it just guarantees every db has at least one nasty trick up its sleeve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:38:51-07:00","id":1237138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237088#post1237088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been reading through up to now.<br /> <br /> I haven't tried a DBs game yet, and I'm fairly the opposite of a mechanics-monkey. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But, that said, the purchased-excellencies rule seems to me to be easy houserule fodder. Most especially if you want to have a mixed-splat Chronicle. <br /> <br /> It seems like a nice, self contained rule that's easy to binary-switch off and on, without having to dig through umpty-bajillion Charms to make power tweaks and bring everybody into the game.<br /> <br /> How much gap would it close between a DB and Solar, if the DB in the Circle also got free Excellencies within the scope of that game?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you\u2019re talking about the gap between how a DB feels on chargen vs how the Solar feels, eg. I hate having to purchase excellencies, then the gap basically closes completely. Maybe even pushing the DB further since they can get essence 2 charms and evocations off the hop.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re talking about the power gap, it doesn\u2019t do much and in a mixed game you\u2019re likely not going to in any reasonable way. <br /> <br /> Solar charms are like big super combo machines that take this and that and add overflow successes and then double rolled successes that increases quadratically with the previous charm and KABOOM! 120 final damage! Dragonblooded charms are more like a big toolbox. You\u2019ve got some that combo together but otherwise they tend to do discreet things, like one charm might let you close a gap in melee, or reflexively disarm an attacker, or blind your enemy with a sparkshower, but none of these can combo together because they\u2019re not really enhancement charms, they just do their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:41:58-07:00","id":1237280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236690#post1236690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then what do you think the floor for Exalted power should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Free Excellencies, no Aura mode, all DB Charms now work as if the appropriate Aura was on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236752#post1236752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you're largely starting from a false premise, that of &quot;your baseline is a loser&quot;. Of course you will be disappointed, you are actively looking for that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually. What I was looking for when I opened preview 3, super excited to see the Dragonblooded mechanics for the first Exalted kickstarter I could back, was the awesome Dragonblooded charms and cool stuff they'd be able to do and ways to play fun characters.<br /> <br /> What I <i>got</i> was weak, overpriced, uninteresting mechanics that would require extensive homebrewing to approach something I'd have any interest in playing. I legit liked 2e Dragonblooded Charms better, and would have gladly taken surcharges again over Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:53:56-07:00","id":1237286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237280#post1237280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Excellencies, no Aura mode, all DB Charms now work as if the appropriate Aura was on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you also nix the effects of the Terrestrial keyword? Because otherwise I think you'd run into some weird balance issues where native Charms are just flat-out better than MA, no contest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:02:50-07:00","id":1237297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237286#post1237286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you also nix the effects of the Terrestrial keyword? Because otherwise I think you'd run into some weird balance issues where native Charms are just flat-out better than MA, no contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was running an Ex3 Dragonblooded game I would look into altering certain Terrestrial Keyworded Charms, yes, because some of them are overly punishing. This completely pales to the problem, however, of <i>every single DB Charm with Aura</i> being overly punishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T18:22:52-07:00","id":1237350,"title":"","content":"They can fucking <i>fly</i>.<br /> <br /> What's &quot;overly punishing&quot; about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-20-2018, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T19:17:38-07:00","id":1237364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237350#post1237350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can fucking <i>fly</i>.<br /> <br /> What's &quot;overly punishing&quot; about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>An experienced Dragonblooded months into the game can fly. I don't really give a crap about Signature Charms because every game I've ever been in ends by E3. If the game gets fun after a year of play, that's a problem because <i>I quit six months ago.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T19:25:06-07:00","id":1237367,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this discussion might be also a mix of expectations for What kind of narrative the splat is supposed to cater to. SLS noted in the same-sex marriage thread that DBs are designed to operate in the social space and be the political intrigue splat. I am curios what everyone's thoughts are that given Dragonblooded are written with political intrigue and social play in mind, do the charms and their effects change from y'all's point of view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T22:46:51-07:00","id":1237416,"title":"","content":"I suppose my first surprise is 'every game ends well before E3', which is not really my experience. (Then again, my primary mode of Exalted these days is online play.) But every group is different and I confess I do like giving DBs a one-ability pseudo-Supernal so they can play with <i>one</i> signature charm, so I can see how other folks would think differently.<br /> <br /> Honestly some of the complaints come off to me as &quot;how <i>dare</i> Dragon-blooded be designed like Dragon-blooded!&quot; (Like the Elemental Sheath thing. A charm that only works if... a Terrestrial is using an artifact weapon of the magical material they're most likely to possess and use, and they're the splat most likely to have the resources to <i>have</i> an artifact weapon in the first place, what with ruling much of the world.)<br /> <br /> To a certain degree Terrestrials get unfairly looked at because in every edition they come right after Solars, but the Dragon-blooded of this edition are not exactly &quot;just above mortals&quot;. We already have that as a category: that's &quot;mortal&quot; sorcerers, people with various unique supernatural merits, thaumaturgists, and the like. Certainly, comparing them negatively to 2nd edition Dragon-blooded seems, at best, ludicrous to me. That was the edition that gave Terrestrials a perfect defense, in a combat system where perfect defenses were very important, and that perfect <i>could not be used against anything you actually needed to use a perfect against</i>.<br /> <br /> At least, not until the Thousand Correct Actions errata and other 2.5-era adjustments, but it was still a half-measure and at no point did they bother to make Terrestrials feel like more than Solars with shitty Excellency caps that damaged everything in their vicinity as a consequence of using their powers.<br /> <br /> There's room for wriggling and house rules, but in every way the 3e treatment seems vastly superior to previous iterations of the concept and works closer to their thematics, not just invoking elements in fluff but working them into every tree in effect, and giving Terrestrials things that they are <i>better</i> than Solars at doing... <i>without</i> damaging their role as the &quot;individually weakest but most numerous type of Exalted&quot;. No matter how hard they train, no Solar is ever going to get the full effect of Immaculate Martial Arts. (On the other hand, they can come close, and the Solars are going to be superior at all <i>other</i> Martial Arts styles.)<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that the criticisms raised in this thread are without merit (some I agree with to a less serious degree, like the signature charm thing), but this is the first time I'm excited about playing a DB since first edition. And First Edition was mostly because it was something different after playing nothing but corebook Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T22:59:29-07:00","id":1237420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237416#post1237416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly some of the complaints come off to me as &quot;how <i>dare</i> Dragon-blooded be designed like Dragon-blooded!&quot; (Like the Elemental Sheath thing. A charm that only works if... a Terrestrial is using an artifact weapon of the magical material they're most likely to possess and use, and they're the splat most likely to have the resources to <i>have</i> an artifact weapon in the first place, what with ruling much of the world.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Fuck you if you're an Outcaste or want to have a weapon that isn't made of jade&quot; is, indeed, not a design decision that makes me feel very welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T23:22:14-07:00","id":1237423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237420#post1237420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Fuck you if you're an Outcaste or want to have a weapon that isn't made of jade&amp;quot; is, indeed, not a design decision that makes me feel very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the matter of outcaste Dragonblooded, unless it is the chronicle of a lone isolated Prince of the Earth, it strikes me that the societal groups that compose Dragonblooded outcastes would still have relatively decent access to jade weaponry, given the relative power and standing of Dragonblooded even in non-Realm/Non-Lookshy societies.<br /> <br /> As to Dragonblooded who don\u2019t wish to wield jade weapons, I think this is where we are just going to have a difference of opinion. Jade is as much a part of DBs imo as moonsilver is to Lunars or Starmetal to Sids, and the fact that their charms echo that affinity is just fine in my book. I am sorry that that specific affinity is an issue for you though, I just don\u2019t happen to share it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T01:15:16-07:00","id":1237433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237423#post1237423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the matter of outcaste Dragonblooded, unless it is the chronicle of a lone isolated Prince of the Earth, it strikes me that the societal groups that compose Dragonblooded outcastes would still have relatively decent access to jade weaponry, given the relative power and standing of Dragonblooded even in non-Realm/Non-Lookshy societies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, so how many jade artifacts are just randomly lying around in the Threshold, up for taking?<br /> <br /> 5000? Clearly, that's absurd. 1000? Maybe. A few hundred? Probably. 500 seems like a safe bet, between Artifacts that are forever unavailable (lost and forgotten, never to be found, or in the possession of foes you can't possibly hope to defeat) and the Realm constantly vacuuming them up to the best of their ability. So that gives my character a 1-in-10 chance to own one. You <i>can </i>explain it, but it's rare enough that you do have to explain it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237423#post1237423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to Dragonblooded who don\u2019t wish to wield jade weapons, I think this is where we are just going to have a difference of opinion. Jade is as much a part of DBs imo as moonsilver is to Lunars or Starmetal to Sids, and the fact that their charms echo that affinity is just fine in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dragon-Blooded already have a greater affinity with jade than anything else due to the way resonance works. Making one of your Charms literally nonfunctional unless you opt into a jade weapon on top of that is just... rude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-21-2018, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T01:43:46-07:00","id":1237436,"title":"","content":"Indeed, that there are charms that only work with artefacts made of the magic material to which the exalted are resonant, doesn't strike me as too bad a design descission.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T01:44:41-07:00","id":1237437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237420#post1237420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck you if you're an Outcaste or want to have a weapon that isn't made of jade&quot; is, indeed, not a design decision that makes me feel very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the one-liner response to a lengthy post, I guess.<br /> <br /> Outcastes are still some of the most powerful people in their region, <i>simply by virtue of being an Exalt</i>.<br /> <br /> They won't have that much trouble, if they want a jade weapon; Jade is by far the most common magical material (it's common enough to be used as <i>money</i>, which requires something rare but not <i>too</i> rare) and there's a ten-thousand-strong host of Dragonbloods as a userbase, plus the small matter of they're the only ones legally permitted to touch the stuff in those areas the Realm or Realm-influenced nations hold sway.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's perfectly in keeping with the Dragonblooded niche in general, and the presentation in this edition. If you want the crazy go nuts do-anything splat, Solars areright there. It's what they're all about. Dragonblooded seem to be much more about specializing and fighting to their strengths. Unlike previous editions, they can achieve impressive, stands-up-to-Solars results if they do that. If they are unable or unwilling, well, hello intro chapter fiction. Part of that is &quot;their elemental charms will work best if you have a weapon that <i>also</i> harmonizes with the elements, via being made of jade.&quot;<br /> <br /> I will say I think using DGW with a non-jade weapon, but limited to the user's aspect element (and possibly expending anima to do so) would be a fair edit. But as someone, right now, planning out a 3rd edition DB character who will be using a non-jade weapon (the Sun's Brush, from Arms of the Chosen) I can't say I'm terribly bothered by that particular aspect. To be fair, she's shaping up to be a smug-as-hell melee loremaster sort for whom the open display of a legendary scholar's weapon made of orichalcum as a dare to all Anathema who see it is <i>the point</i>, so if she goes up that branch of the tree it'll only be to grab Root-and-Hand Merging down the road. It's also a sacrifice I'm willing to make and I understand the ways in which it is suboptimal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T02:13:16-07:00","id":1237441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237420#post1237420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck you if you're an Outcaste or want to have a weapon that isn't made of jade&quot; is, indeed, not a design decision that makes me feel very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well even if you're an Outcaste you're a PC outcaste. If you' happen to be one of the only 500 Outcastes who have a jade daiklave I really don't think that's an issue. Most Outcastes won't have the fate of all Creation hinging on their actions either but you've got like a 40% chance of that happening to you as a PC.<br /> <br /> If you want a weapon that isn't Jade though, yeah it can make some of your charms less effective, but that's pretty reasonable, exalted have always strongly favoured their resonant material. It's an elemental material that allows elemental charms to uniquely affect it. Remember how last edition attuning to a material that wasn't resonant with your exalt type cost twice as many motes? AND you had to succeed at a (Wits + Lore) roll of difficulty 3 or else suffer unsoakable lethal damage and shattering any hearthstones. Botching that roll destroyed the item entirely. How's that for &quot;Want to be a DB with an orichalcum daiklave? Go fuck yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> At least in this edition a DB is only marginally worse with a Moonsilver daiklave than a Lunar is, and if you want to use it you just shouldn't take the banishing charm. It's not like you're a worthless swordsman without the ability to banish your favourite sword to Elsewhere. Either way it's a HUGE step up in friendliness from last edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T04:30:43-07:00","id":1237452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237280#post1237280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I <i>got</i> was weak, overpriced, uninteresting mechanics that would require extensive homebrewing to approach something I'd have any interest in playing. I legit liked 2e Dragonblooded Charms better, and would have gladly taken surcharges again over Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might not be able to change your mind, but let me give it a shot. I really don't want to come across as a dick, and I know how big long posts can make it seem like I'm being a dick, I just think that the effects of the DB charmset are actually not nearly as bad as they look at first glance.<br /> <br /> I've used the example of a Fire aspected brawler, using Earth aspected charms in the traditionally Water aspected brawl tree. I'll just do a quick re-hash of that, but basically it works out like this, as of essence 2.<br /> <br /> Balanced Charms:<br /> Become the Hammer<br /> Pounding Surf Style<br /> Water Dragon Coils<br /> Inescapable Whirlpool Hold<br /> <br /> Earth Charms:<br /> Crushing Avalanche Grasp<br /> Stone Fist Strike<br /> Rolling Boulder Blow<br /> <br /> <br /> That's a decent charm spread which will keep you in Earth Aura until you go bonfire as a fire aspect, which is something that you need to control. Which you can do as long as you do things like spend 9 motes* on your attacks, and carefully pick your defenses. For example use Resistance charms like Impervious Skin of Stone to defend yourself, or keep your dodge charm usage to only Threshold Warding Stance. It's not <i>super </i>easy, certainly, but you're a friggen Fire aspect using the Earth branch of the Water ability, you couldn't be more twisted up in your elements if you tried.<br /> <br /> Even if you get forced out of your Earth Aura though, that's okay. What you lose is the ability to ignore successful hits on your rounds of control, and 1 point of Overwhelming for withering attacks. What you gain is now you're free to use any water aspected charms that aren't balanced that you may have picked up, so it's not the end of the world. The thing is, that's as hard as it ever gets, because if you were, say, an Earth aspect, then no worries, bonfire never knocks you out of aura and you can just sit there in it using those charms forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, when you read through the charms you get the impression that you're useless without Aura, but actually when you play through it you can annihilate demons without even touching the powerful aura effects. <b>Using Aura is more like a special reward for people who want to really focus hard on one element. If Aura effects weren't powerful you'd just be handicaped in that endevour, they just help even things out.</b> Bolded because those two sentences are more important than the previous two paragraphs. I'll explain below.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other thing you mention is that the power of DB charms is underwhelming. Which is true compared to Solar charms, but DBs are still badasses. Like a fairly optimized chargen DB brawler can easily defeat a Blood-Ape, who's a terrifying overmuscled supernatural demon from hell, with his bare hands. Use Hammering Wave Technique and Oaken Thew Exertion to make your hands deal +22 base damage, rerolling 6s because of the excellency, then next turn grapple him and slam him into oblivion. The ape stands next to no chance, and it's only a matter of possible lucky rolls that will even make this a fight.<br /> <br /> Spoiler tags hold a quick math justification for this.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> So, you've got like 5/2/5 for physical stats, lets say. Something you can super easily get off chargen if you want.<br /> <br /> You attack with a full excellency, which gives you 18 dice to hit his parry of 4, on average ~5 overflow successes.<br /> <br /> Baseline damage is +22 with those charms, plus the 5 from the overflow that's 27 damage against his soak of 7. You're rolling 20 dice, rerolling 6s. So like 11 average damage there.<br /> <br /> With his join battle of 6, that means you just buried him on the first round, snagging 17 initiative for yourself.<br /> <br /> He attacks back, using his incredibly powerful howl ability, getting about 4.5 successes. If you dodge it and use Flickering Candle Meditation you're going to put your evasion at like, 8, while giving him a penalty to attack. That's almost an evasion equal to his attack pool.<br /> <br /> Next turn you take your 25 initiative and proceed to end the blood ape by whatever means you deem most satisfying.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For the enemies that the Exalted book presents to us, DBs are actually more than powerful enough to deal with them. They're still head and shoulders above almost any natural or supernatural threat that they may face, the only difference is that if they get surrounded and outnumbered or something they might be in trouble. That's a problem Solars don't tend to have in my experience, but I think it can lead to some good drama and better stories honestly.<br /> <br /> Anyway this has gone on too long... Is there any one area specifically where you think DBs are super weak, or over reliant on Aura? I covered Brawl up above but maybe Archery or something has more problems?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I know spending 9 motes technically does increase your anima by one level, but first you need to blow through all your personal, and then spend 3 turns getting to that point, at which point the fight will be over. I have maybe once in my whole life seen a third edition battle that lasted more than 5 rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 07-21-2018, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T05:36:03-07:00","id":1237460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237280#post1237280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, actually. What I was looking for when I opened preview 3, super excited to see the Dragonblooded mechanics for the first Exalted kickstarter I could back, was the awesome Dragonblooded charms and cool stuff they'd be able to do and ways to play fun characters.<br /> <br /> What I <i>got</i> was weak, overpriced, uninteresting mechanics that would require extensive homebrewing to approach something I'd have any interest in playing. I legit liked 2e Dragonblooded Charms better, and would have gladly taken surcharges again over Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so you set a bar for yourself (though starting with solars does limit what you can compare with) and was disappointed it was not met despite it being closer to what you claim you wanted than you may perceive.<br /> <br /> Such is the lot of subjective measurements, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:09:07-07:00","id":1237467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237437#post1237437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the one-liner response to a lengthy post, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Welcome to my life, lol.<br /> <br /> Now imagine how it feels, after expounding in multiple walls of text on the various thematic and mechanical reasons why it is a bad thing to lock away the Charmset's only non-E3 way to deal with the most basic strategy against a melee combatant behind an &quot;Ability 5, pick a Charm that might possibly be useless to you&quot; gate to get derailed time and time again into arguments about<b></b>:<br /> a/ Whether there is a strict equivalency between DGW and CtB (there isn't, but that doesn't change the fact that DGW is the only tool you have to deal with the situation of being disarmed unless you rely on external aids)<br /> b/ THEMES (not an argument unless it is explained how those themes are reinforced through the limitations above, aside from a vague handwave-y &quot;devs said so&quot;)<br /> c/ Whether Charms are an in-setting thing or just mechanical abstractions of the capabilities of heroic individuals (what)<br /> d/ Whether the Dragon-Blooded affinity with jade is enough of a reason to justify having to pick a dead Charm if you don't want to take a massive hit to your Defense and the max excellency cap thereof if somebody manages to pull off a disarm<br /> <br /> Fuck, it almost makes me think &quot;now I get why Jon Chung sounds so fucking irritated <i>all the time</i>&quot;, who is not a person I ever imagined I'll feel any particular amount of sympathy towards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237437#post1237437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say I think using DGW with a non-jade weapon, but limited to the user's aspect element (and possibly expending anima to do so) would be a fair edit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, this is a good solution, for example. Me, I'd also knock the requirement on DGW down to Melee 3, maybe give it and Elemental Sheath the Bridge (Martial Arts) keyword, and rephrase the weapon summoning effect as something like &quot;alternatively, she may use Elemental Sheath as a Simple Charm to shape a mundane weapon out of the elements (blah blah); by adding 1 point of Willpower to the Charm's cost, this effect can be activated reflexively&quot;. It's an inelegant, kludgy solution, but still better than &quot;lol fuck you Single Point, fuck you Steel Devil, and fuck anybody who was stupid enough to not warp her character concept around the platonic ideal of a jade weapon-wielding, Melee 5-having, perfectly spherical Dragon-Blooded sword wielder&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237441#post1237441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well even if you're an Outcaste you're a PC outcaste. If you' happen to be one of the only 500 Outcastes who have a jade daiklave I really don't think that's an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...But I shouldn't <i>have to</i> jump through hoops to justify myself if I want to play an Outcaste who has... Charms that do things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-21-2018, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:39:02-07:00","id":1237477,"title":"","content":"I really don't think disarming protection is the be-all end-all charm tech you're making it out to be. <br /> <br /> Have you considered just, y'know, going over and just picking the fucking thing back up? Fire gets dodge. They're good at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:46:06-07:00","id":1237480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237477#post1237477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think disarming protection is the be-all end-all charm tech you're making it out to be.<br /> <br /> Have you considered just, y'know, going over and just picking the fucking thing back up? Fire gets dodge. They're good at that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Way</i> ahead of ya.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237059#post1237059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DGW, on the other hand, represents a problem where a very basic capability is completely absent from a splat's native powerset unless one is willing to hyperspecialize. <b>This is not a <i>huge</i> problem (you can carry a spare knife, there's a hearthstone that makes it harder for people to disarm you, picking a few dots in Brawl or Dodge won't kill you either, and if everything else fails, you can just make up an Evocation that deals with the issue), but to deny that the problem <i>exists in the first place</i> is pretty disingenuous.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>(emphasis added)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:24:08-07:00","id":1237494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237467#post1237467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...But I shouldn't <i>have to</i> jump through hoops to justify myself if I want to play an Outcaste who has... Charms that do things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody will bat an eye at an Outcaste having a daiklave, I assure you. Some Outcastes lead traitor imperial legions, while others pilot warstriders.<br /> <br /> Also you've totally got charms that do things. You've got like 500 charms that do things. You just have one that requires you to have a magic weapon instead of a regular one, which as a DB is a great idea anyway since your charms are less effective than Solar ones but your artifacts are just as good. Even if you don't get one at character creation you're bound to pick one up somewhere in the story.<br /> <br /> The real problem here is that there is a charm in a tree with a prerequisite that you might not find useful, but that is kind of a problem with the charm cascade style in general. You might just want Blazing Solar Bolt because god damn that's so super cool, but you need to buy two charms that give bonuses to Creatures of Darkness. Which is great, until you're playing in a game where your Solar party is infiltrating the Realm civil war, and will almost never be fighting any CoD at all, but you still want Solar Bolt. Which is actually a WAY harder restriction to work around because you can't pick up a 3 dot merit that makes all Dragonblooded CoD.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not exactly an issue restricted to Elemental Sheath, or even DBs as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:47:32-07:00","id":1237501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237494#post1237494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody will bat an eye at an Outcaste having a daiklave, I assure you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is not about whether I need a particularly <i>convoluted </i>justification for a daiklave (my current Water Aspect's is literally &quot;I just grabbed it from the tomb of a local Dragon-Blooded hero and ran like hell from his hungry ghost&quot;).<br /> <br /> It's more like... if I'm playing an Outcaste, I'm doing it because <i>I want to be an underdog</i>. Being decked out in the same awesome bling my Dynastic brethren are taking for granted should be something of a triumph, a story beat where I rise above my station and the circumstances of my birth, and <i>not</i> just a checkbox I tick during my backstory.<br /> <br /> But playing Exalted Swordsman Hamilton is somewhat hampered by the fact that I can either just accept that I'll have a glaring major weak point my enemies can trivially exploit, or I'll effectively be one Charm down from everybody else in the team. This is a case where the mechanics are actively making certain stories harder to tell by creating a strong disincentive on top of the already-existing social and stat penalties I'm taking for being an Outcaste with a crappy regular weapon.<br /> <br /> And again, <i>this is not a major problem</i>. I'm not running around and yelling &quot;WAAAH THE SKY IS FALLING DRAGON-BLOODED ARE <b>RUINED</b> FOREVER&quot;, because this is trivial to fix (and I've never been a big believer in the idea that requiring a GM to do minimal design work - which is actually a <i>very basic part of a GM's job</i> - is somehow a bad thing that is always to be avoided). But I do find it very frustrating that everybody seems to be incredibly fixated on this one particular issue in their criticism, especially since the original post in which I mentioned it was not even about that, but the very basic differences in structure and design philosophy between the Solar and the Dragon-Blooded charmset - my thoughts on which just went completely unremarked upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:18:37-07:00","id":1237508,"title":"","content":"I want to point out that Heirs to the Shogunate might include a lot of new Charms that might cover some of the DB charmset problems pointed at in this thread. I am hopeful that the supplement will contain useful solid extra content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:37:13-07:00","id":1237510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237433#post1237433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's rare enough that you do have to explain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the case with every Artifact.<br /> <br /> I would expect jade ones to be relatively more abundant, assuming that the First Age contained vastly more Terrestrials, and that many of them had jade items.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:42:57-07:00","id":1237511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237501#post1237501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll effectively be one Charm down from everybody else in the team. This is a case where the mechanics are actively making certain stories harder to tell by creating a strong disincentive on top of the already-existing social and stat penalties I'm taking for being an Outcaste with a crappy regular weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that makes sense, but it's not like this is a thing that the DB book screwed up when the Solar book got it right. As long as charm cascades hold dozens of charms, and aren't branched off into 10 different sub-branches this sort of thing will tend to crop up. See Blazing Solar Bolt, for example, however...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237501#post1237501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But playing Exalted Swordsman Hamilton is somewhat hampered by the fact that I can either just accept that I'll have a glaring major weak point my enemies can trivially exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being vulnerable to a disarm gambit is not, I think, a glaring major weak point that your enemies can trivially exploit. It's not like this is the Perfect Defense of 3rd ed where if you don't have Call the Blade you might as well not enter into the combat. Martial artists, archers, boomerang throwers, they can't even do it at all, and they all seem to do fine. There's always going to be some hole in your defense, grappling, poison, stealth ambush, there's something you're going to be vulnerable to. The key is using your strengths and knowing your weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237501#post1237501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> my thoughts on which just went completely unremarked upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Yes I see.<br /> <br /> One of the points you make is something that Fire does a lot of which is &quot;Win more&quot;, which, as you point out, on the weakest exalt type seems pointless. I actually thought exactly the same thing until I saw it in action in combat. The first DB 3rd ed combat I ran was a test where the party was ambushed by a pack of claw striders. In that combat the Fire aspect got off to a bit of a rocky start and then eventually built up to a totally free excellency.<br /> <br /> Flame-Borne Interception is actually designed to be used <i>in conjunction</i> with the melee excellency. What it lets you do is be surrounded by foes with relatively weak attack dicepools and quickly build up that free excellency. For instance, there's a lot of things in the antagonist sections with dicepools of like 8-10, which for somebody with a mediocre defense of 4 is pretty scary. If you full excellency your defense you can make it like 7-8, which makes you effectively immune, but if you get surrounded by three of them you'll mote-tap yourself in a single round just parrying their attacks. Or a creature like the Blood Ape, who can attack multiple times in a turn, that's also possible.<br /> <br /> (Enter Flame-Borne Interception + Stoking Bonfire Style) he says in parenthesis.<br /> <br /> Now all of a sudden you excellency your attack, and hit, then spend 8 motes full excellency your defense and add FBI. You parry the first attack, now you only need to spend 2 motes to full excellency and parry the second attack, and THEN you full excellency for free your third parry and build up to a 4 mote discount for your next attack. Which you spend 2 motes full-exellencying and build up another stack, and so on. Now imagine that with an optimized character, who's baseline defense is 7, pumping up to 13.<br /> <br /> So surprisingly it actually works. Remember I did think exactly the same thing as you when I first saw it, I just didn't understand how it could be used until we played some. Against a Solar, or some other insane combatant with a dicepool of 25 or something, then yeah it's basically useless, but as a DB those fights are really few and far between. Unless your ST hates you.<br /> <br /> Burning Fury Wreath I have to admit I'm not sure if that's more useful than it appears. I've done a bit of DB stuff but not enough to definitively say one way or another.<br /> <br /> The other trees can tend to do this too though, like how Pounding Surf Style feels kind of lame, but then you start to use it in play and you see why it's actually pretty solid. At least in my experience, which I have to admit is somewhat limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:57:00-07:00","id":1237516,"title":"","content":"Actually, thinking about it, dragon graced weapon isn't just call the blade. It's also summon the loyal steel for an infinite amount of melee weapons. <br /> <br /> So you spend 2 charms to get two charms worth of power. And you don't even need to buy all the weapons. <br /> <br /> Sounds fair to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T11:20:25-07:00","id":1237546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237511#post1237511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flame-Borne Interception is actually designed to be used <i>in conjunction</i> with the melee excellency. What it lets you do is be surrounded by foes with relatively weak attack dicepools and quickly build up that free excellency. For instance, there's a lot of things in the antagonist sections with dicepools of like 8-10, which for somebody with a mediocre defense of 4 is pretty scary. If you full excellency your defense you can make it like 7-8, which makes you effectively immune, but if you get surrounded by three of them you'll mote-tap yourself in a single round just parrying their attacks. Or a creature like the Blood Ape, who can attack multiple times in a turn, that's also possible.<br /> <br /> (Enter Flame-Borne Interception + Stoking Bonfire Style) he says in parenthesis.<br /> <br /> Now all of a sudden you excellency your attack, and hit, then spend 8 motes full excellency your defense and add FBI. You parry the first attack, now you only need to spend 2 motes to full excellency and parry the second attack, and THEN you full excellency for free your third parry and build up to a 4 mote discount for your next attack. Which you spend 2 motes full-exellencying and build up another stack, and so on. Now imagine that with an optimized character, who's baseline defense is 7, pumping up to 13.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry, but this is not how Stoking Bonfire Style works as written. You seem to have forgotten the crucial last sentence of the effect: &quot;Missing an attack or failing to parry resets the discount, as does attacking or defending against another enemy, or going a round without using this Charm.&quot;<br /> <br /> In our example of a single unoptimized Parry 5 Dragon-Blooded going up against three claw striders, this is what would happen:<br /> <br /> DB wins Join Battle, activating Stoking Bonfire Style on the attack. Hits, 1m discount on SBS goes online, reflexive activation of Flame-Borne Interception happens before Claw Strider #1 would attack.<br /> Assuming we're extraordinarily lucky and CS #1 is the one we hit, still leading in Initiative despite our massive blow, we get a 1m discount on SBS. We full excellency for 3m, putting us to Defense 8 with a stunt; another 1m discount goes online, FBI gives us a further +1 enhancement to Parry which is immediately cancelled out by the onslaught penalty.<br /> CS #2 comes a-knocking. Since the Charm text of SBS actually says &quot;When she lands an attack against an enemy or blocks one with this Charm, the cost of using this Charm<b> against him</b> is cumulatively lowered by one mote on subsequent rounds&quot;, our cost reduction ain't worth jack right now, so we full excellency for 2m, putting us at Defense 7 with a stunt. At this point, the discount on SBS is also immediately reset because we defended against a different enemy.<br /> Good news though, we're at full excellency thanks to FBI anyway - so now we're looking at an attack against Parry 6. Successfully parrying this gets us another 1m discount if we attack CS #3 next turn though; question is, do we want to do that or are we better off pressing CS #1 in the hopes of getting a Crash and wasting the 1m discount?<br /> <br /> At this point, we should take stock. Assuming a 4m full excellency on our first attack, we've spent 4 (first attack) + 3 (FBI) + 3 (full excellency on Parry vs. CS #1) + 2m (full excellency on Parry vs. CS #2) +0m (we were already at cap when CS #3's turn came up); total of 12m.<br /> <br /> If we didn't use FBI, we'd be at 4m + 3m + 4m + 4m = 15m, so activating FBI did get us 3 free motes. Note that as the number of enemy combatants decreases, the gap between having FBI and not having it closes as well - if we only had two attackers, we'd be at 4+3+3+2=12 versus 4+3+4=11, so even if FBI works perfectly, it is only worth activating if you're looking at the possibility of getting attacked three times in the same round at minimum. This also means enemies can bait you into wasting motes by cleverly positioning and selecting their targets or actions - had CS #3 decided to take an Aim action instead, you would be looking at the same number of spent motes, but he'd gain a +3d bonus on his next attack while denying you a mote discount on your next attack against him (which is fine, you get it against CS #2 instead).<br /> <br /> However, a more pressing concern with FBI is that its bonus only procs on successful parries and resets if an attack goes through.<br /> Assuming our opponents have 8d on their first attack, they stand a mere 4% chance of hitting us; however, with our Defense steadily decreasing due to onslaught penalties, this initial slim chance goes up to 9.97% on the second, and 20.94% chance on the third attack.<br /> So, how things may go down looks like this:<br /> Initial roll - 96% to successfully defend; we've spent 4+3+3=10m thus far.<br /> Second roll - 90.03% to successfully defend; we've spent 10+2=12m thus far.<br /> Third roll - 79.06% to successfully defend; we've spent 12m total. (0.96*0.903*12=10.40m) // (0.877*0.767*12=8.0719)<br /> Second roll - 9.97% to fail to defend. We've spent 12m thus far, but the bonus is reset, so we'll need to dump another 4m into a full excellency on our third parry.<br /> Third roll - 79.06% to successfully defend; we've spent 16m total. (0.96*0.099*16=1.52m) // (0.877*0.233*16=3.2694)<br /> Initial roll - 4% to fail to defend; we've spent 10m thus far, but we gain no Parry bonus on our second roll, forcing us to full excellency for 4m.<br /> Second roll - 90.03% to successfully defend; we've spent 10+4=14m thus far. Parry increases by 1 due to FBI, so we only have to spend 2m to hit our excellency cap on the third hit.<br /> Third roll - 79.06% to successfully defend; we've spent 14+2=16m total. (0.04*0.903*16=0.57m) // (0.123*0.767*16=1.5094)<br /> Second roll - 9.97% to fail to defend. We've spent 14m thus far, failing to get FBI to do anything, forcing us to spend yet another 4m on a full excellency on our third parry.<br /> Third roll - 79.06% to successfully defend; we've spent 18m total. (0.04*0.099*18=0.07m) //0.515<br /> If we total the weighed costs, we come to the conclusion that the <i>actual </i>cost of using FBI against three opponents with 8d attack pools is closer to 12.5m than it is to 12. By itself, this does not seem significant - but against an opponent with just a 10d attack pool (literally a stunt's difference), we're looking at 87.7/76.7/61.2% chances of successfully defending, respectively; by plugging these numbers into the formulae above, we can calculate a total cost of 13.36 motes or thereabout, meaning that in a real scenario against attackers with 10d dice pools, it saves us less than 2m per turn even if we assume no counterplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-21-2018, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T12:45:47-07:00","id":1237556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237460#post1237460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so you set a bar for yourself (though starting with solars does limit what you can compare with) and was disappointed it was not met despite it being closer to what you claim you wanted than you may perceive.<br /> <br /> Such is the lot of subjective measurements, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not actually anywhere near what I <i>actually want,</i> and if you'd stop telling me that I'm too deluded to see how amazing this Charmset is, that'd be awesome. It's not even in the <i>ballpark</i> of what I wanted. Because it's designed around Aura, penalty negation, and fucking <i>signature Charms</i> (*spits*) being the meat of what's interesting about the set. I want a fun Essence 1&amp;2 experience, and I don't want to deal with fiddly mechanics trying to trick me into thinking I have a super mode rather than a &quot;remove pointless debuffs&quot; mode that also <i>shuts down my other Charms.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T12:58:01-07:00","id":1237560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237556#post1237556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(*spits*)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... extreme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">trying to trick me</div> </div> </div> </div>And that seems like another instance of seeing not getting what one wants as vindictive.<br /> <br /> I understand why some people would dislike the mechanical premises of this Charm set, and I understand being exasperated at that being continuously mischaracterized and misheard.<br /> <br /> But I think getting angry at the Charms and the writing is not the best reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T13:44:13-07:00","id":1237576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237556#post1237556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to deal with fiddly mechanics trying to trick me into thinking I have a super mode rather than a &quot;remove pointless debuffs&quot; mode that also <i>shuts down my other Charms.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a trick. These two things are literally identical depending on how you look at it. Any super mode &quot; removes debuffs&quot; if you assume the super mode is the default level of power. I know you're getting annoyed by us saying it's your attitude that's ruining this for you, but the problem is, <i>it's your attitude that's ruining this for you\u200b.</i><br /> <br /> The charms that <i>don't</i> have aura effects are what you should look at as the baseline for dragon blooded power. The Aura mechanic is designed to give dragonblooded a boost, with hoops to jump through to get it. It's so they can retain their status as the weakest of the exalted whilst <i>actually having good charms.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T14:33:11-07:00","id":1237587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237546#post1237546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CS #2 comes a-knocking. Since the Charm text of SBS actually says &quot;When she lands an attack against an enemy or blocks one with this Charm, the cost of using this Charm<b> against him</b> is cumulatively lowered by one mote on subsequent rounds&quot;, our cost reduction ain't worth jack right now, so we full excellency for 2m, putting us at Defense 7 with a stunt. At this point, the discount on SBS is also immediately reset because we defended against a different enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh wow I totally missed that wording. It's a good thing I haven't run a huge DB campaign since then. That test combat would have gone a lot differently too, fire aspect by the end definitely wouldn't have been nearly full up on motes.<br /> <br /> There's still a few situations where it's useful, but the character types and situations list there is way smaller. I agree DB melee needs a buff in that regard. I mentioned to Vance a while ago that the melee fire signature is also really situational in the type of character that can effectively use it, and he said he flagged it for another look so hopefully he can poke around the rest of melee as well.<br /> <br /> I don't THINK the other trees are as bad as melee, but now I'm not so sure, I'd need to look over the whole charmset again.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Is it possible that the bonus to party is supposed to apply as you block the attack, and then immediately resets to 0 if that block fails? It\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve deciphered Exalted charm text. If that IS the case, it makes the charm okay, not insanely good just okay, but if it isn\u2019t then yeah it\u2019s almost flat out useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 07-21-2018, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T14:59:30-07:00","id":1237594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237587#post1237587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still a few situations where it's useful, but the character types and situations list there is way smaller. I agree DB melee needs a buff in that regard. I mentioned to Vance a while ago that the melee fire signature is also really situational in the type of character that can effectively use it, and he said he flagged it for another look so hopefully he can poke around the rest of melee as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough, the fire signature is actually better than it's being given credit for around here. Just reduce the cost a bit and make the Dex 5 + spec effect the default one - 3 attacks for Init/2 each are about on par with the Water sig. What you lose out on in damage you make up for in flexibility and reliability (especially with the very easily available Charm to reduce Hardness), and crucially, it's a really good way to build up your excellency effect against a single target.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237587#post1237587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Is it possible that the bonus to party is supposed to apply as you block the attack, and then immediately resets to 0 if that block fails? It\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve deciphered Exalted charm text. If that IS the case, it makes the charm okay, not insanely good just okay, but if it isn\u2019t then yeah it\u2019s almost flat out useless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, you're right, the text is somewhat ambiguous on this matter - it says &quot;<i>Each time she blocks an attack, she gains +1 Parry until her next turn. This bonus resets if the Dragon-Blood is hit by an attack, or defends using an Ability other than Melee.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> I assumed &quot;blocks an attacks&quot; means a successful Parry but it does not say so explicitly - it might just refer to the application of Parry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T15:31:05-07:00","id":1237601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237594#post1237594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Funnily enough, the fire signature is actually better than it's being given credit for around here. Just reduce the cost a bit and make the Dex 5 + spec effect the default one - 3 attacks for Init/2 each are about on par with the Water sig. What you lose out on in damage you make up for in flexibility and reliability (especially with the very easily available Charm to reduce Hardness), and crucially, it's a really good way to build up your excellency effect against a single target.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>For me the dex 5 is just a bit too far. It\u2019s a signature charm for an in-aspect ability. It should still be useful at 2 dex.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237594#post1237594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, you're right, the text is somewhat ambiguous on this matter - it says &amp;quot;<i>Each time she blocks an attack, she gains +1 Parry until her next turn. This bonus resets if the Dragon-Blood is hit by an attack, or defends using an Ability other than Melee.</i>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I assumed &amp;quot;blocks an attacks&amp;quot; means a successful Parry but it does not say so explicitly - it might just refer to the application of Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that IS the case it still only saves you 1-3 motes if you\u2019re attacked twice in the same turn, or more in the reasonably uncommon event that you get attacked 3 times. <br /> <br /> But if not yeah you need to be attacked 3 times and successfully defend before it even does anything at all basically. Like you block the first, get a 2 note discount on the second and are still in the hole until the third attack, where you also have to block the second to get, and even then you\u2019re only saving like 3 motes? That\u2019s so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T15:38:34-07:00","id":1237602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237601#post1237601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a signature charm for an in-aspect ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's right.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't out-of-aspect Charms like Steel Tempest Strike and Mela's Flashing Tongue be made a bit stronger than usual, because of how difficult it would be for anyone but Air Aspects to use those effects, and given how difficult an Air Aspect's bonfire anima would make accessing the Aura effects of the Fire, Water, and Wood Melee Charms?<br /> <br /> Like how hard it would be to use the Earth-aspected Signature Dodge Charm, for anyone who isn't an Earth Aspect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T12:10:49-07:00","id":1237800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237576#post1237576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a trick. These two things are literally identical depending on how you look at it. Any super mode &quot; removes debuffs&quot; if you assume the super mode is the default level of power. I know you're getting annoyed by us saying it's your attitude that's ruining this for you, but the problem is, <i>it's your attitude that's ruining this for you\u200b.</i><br /> <br /> The charms that <i>don't</i> have aura effects are what you should look at as the baseline for dragon blooded power. The Aura mechanic is designed to give dragonblooded a boost, with hoops to jump through to get it. It's so they can retain their status as the weakest of the exalted whilst <i>actually having good charms.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's really more that I was expecting them to be stronger and more engaging than in second edition. Not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T12:34:31-07:00","id":1237803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237800#post1237800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really more that I was expecting them to be stronger and more engaging than in second edition. Not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have Charms that fail outright against Celestial Exalted, at least.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to think that they have a lot more than that as well, but respectfully think that we have very different standards by which to measure the strength of the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T12:54:35-07:00","id":1237805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237800#post1237800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really more that I was expecting them to be stronger and more engaging than in second edition. Not less.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> they certainly are if you ignore native charms in favor of IMA and resonant evocations huehuehue<br /> <br /> (My low-effort trolling aside, I actually think there's an interesting dynamic in the decision to go hog wild with MA/Evocations versus investing in native Charms - the martial artist will definitely dominate during the 30 sessions of early game and probably for another story arc thereafter due to DXP pileup allowing an immediate completion of a MA style if training times are not strictly observed, but someone who uses their DXP to bump multiple abilities up to 5 and buys a crapton of sigs right out of the gate will be able to compete rather effectively.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T14:20:12-07:00","id":1237811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237805#post1237805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> they certainly are if you ignore native charms in favor of IMA and resonant evocations huehuehue<br /> <br /> (My low-effort trolling aside, I actually think there's an interesting dynamic in the decision to go hog wild with MA/Evocations versus investing in native Charms - the martial artist will definitely dominate during the 30 sessions of early game and probably for another story arc thereafter due to DXP pileup allowing an immediate completion of a MA style if training times are not strictly observed, but someone who uses their DXP to bump multiple abilities up to 5 and buys a crapton of sigs right out of the gate will be able to compete rather effectively.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but you can't buy Signature Charms out the gate. By the time you can buy Signature Charms, 4 out of 5 times the game is either over, or it's about to end. Every game I've ever seen, with a single exception, over five years of near-exclusively playing Exalted, ends before 150xp. Usually around the 100xp mark, or about 20 sessions. Whether group friction, or some new distraction came out, or the ST getting overwhelmed by the demands of the game. Games <i>really don't last</i> long, not unless you get a special group of PCs to keep everyone glued to it. That's why I hate Signature Charms, they're concentrating the coolest things Dragonblooded are capable of around the point games tend to collapse, <i>and</i> the effects of Aura mean that the early game is going to be miserable, as you need to work your way around your Charms shutting off whenever you need an effect to spike.<br /> <br /> The Solar Charmset, meanwhile, gives you Supernals, so you can play with cool effects (Not that I want DBs to have Supernals, but it's a mitigating factor for a real problem), and more importantly the Essence 1 game of the Solar is interesting and engaging, while the E1 Dragonblooded game is like..please god no. The fact that they start at E2 helps, but bought Excellencies damage your ability to reach the fun Charms, and again every single time I'm left throwing up my hands in frustration, buying a bunch of Excellencies, and resolving to write Jade Evocations that actually feel fun.<br /> <br /> And then I realize that my favorite Exalted splat has such a mess of a Charmset that I'm trying to find ways to avoid engaging with it. And I get really depressed and don't talk to anyone for awhile.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the DB who works their way to signature Charms will be stronger than my Evocation using Martial Artist. <i>He'll never have the chance to reach me.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T14:56:37-07:00","id":1237815,"title":"","content":"So, I am conflicted on this. I conceptually like Aura as a keyword - a lot actually - but I also feel like the stuff it gives isn't actually good enough to justify the pain points it provides for character builds and charm use - this doubly so where Aura and Signature coexist on the same charm. It's a fine line to walk, but there is a way to make Aura feel more like a superpower more than a nuisance and it sure as shit isn't things like capping the damage of your anti-undead nuke charm against the precious goth-solaroids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T14:58:46-07:00","id":1237817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237811#post1237811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but you can't buy Signature Charms out the gate. By the time you can buy Signature Charms, 4 out of 5 times the game is either over, or it's about to end. Every game I've ever seen, with a single exception, over five years of near-exclusively playing Exalted, ends before 150xp. Usually around the 100xp mark, or about 20 sessions. Whether group friction, or some new distraction came out, or the ST getting overwhelmed by the demands of the game. Games <i>really don't last</i> long, not unless you get a special group of PCs to keep everyone glued to it. That's why I hate Signature Charms, they're concentrating the coolest things Dragonblooded are capable of around the point games tend to collapse, <i>and</i> the effects of Aura mean that the early game is going to be miserable, as you need to work your way around your Charms shutting off whenever you need an effect to spike.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a reason to hate half of the entire game, and not exactly a thing that the game can be blamed for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:07:34-07:00","id":1237820,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll just say it. Exalted 3 needs some CofD style Storyteller guides like nobody's business. You know, the kind where they talk about implementing rules hacks, alternate setting stuff, different approaches to existing mechanism, what systems to change or ignore based on the type of campaign you're going to run - things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 07-31-2019, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:11:34-07:00","id":1237822,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can blame the developers for not gearing the design to your weirdass gaming experience. Repeatedly ending games at that point is clearly <i>not the norm</i>, and if that <i>is</i> your experience, just start at essence 3. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:18:22-07:00","id":1237824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237811#post1237811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but you can't buy Signature Charms out the gate. By the time you can buy Signature Charms, 4 out of 5 times the game is either over, or it's about to end. Every game I've ever seen, with a single exception, over five years of near-exclusively playing Exalted, ends before 150xp. Usually around the 100xp mark, or about 20 sessions. Whether group friction, or some new distraction came out, or the ST getting overwhelmed by the demands of the game. Games <i>really don't last</i> long, not unless you get a special group of PCs to keep everyone glued to it. That's why I hate Signature Charms, they're concentrating the coolest things Dragonblooded are capable of around the point games tend to collapse, <i>and</i> the effects of Aura mean that the early game is going to be miserable, as you need to work your way around your Charms shutting off whenever you need an effect to spike.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the DB who works their way to signature Charms will be stronger than my Evocation using Martial Artist. <i>He'll never have the chance to reach me.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're absolutely correct. Designing a core functionality of a splat around an assumption that you will need 30 sessions to get there is absolutely ignorant of they way most games are played at the table. Even if you <i>do </i>get a game the group sticks with, scheduling issues will definitely crop up, meaning that the real-life time commitment before you actually get your cool toys is going to skyrocket. (I just tried to look up how long it took us to get to session 30 in the longest-running campaign our group played. Since we wrote session summaries on an ad-hoc basis, and individual summaries sometimes encompassed events from multiple sessions, I couldn't actually determine the exact cutoff point, but one thing is certain: finishing our first major story arc took us less than 20 sessions, which we took <i>four years</i> to play through. And that campaign started when some of us were still in the first few years of university, with practically unlimited free time.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the 30 session requirement does seem to serve a design purpose: the game wants you to stock up on enough DXP to be able to buy up all the abilities you want to sig up to 5 while still having enough to cover your MA/Evocations/Sorcery needs. I strongly suggest bumping up DXP values or making up new categories you can earn DXP in if you lower the XP requirement for E3 (which you should do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-22-2018, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:35:32-07:00","id":1237826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237822#post1237822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can blame the developers for not gearing the design to your weirdass gaming experience. Repeatedly ending games at that point is clearly <i>not the norm</i>, and if that <i>is</i> your experience, just start at essence 3.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I've always found &quot;I want to RP more but can't get my friends organized, can't find somebody to DM, and can't keep a session running past 4 sessions when I do&quot; to be the universal experience for most Tabletop groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:51:29-07:00","id":1237831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237826#post1237826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I've always found &quot;I want to RP more but can't get my friends organized, can't find somebody to DM, and can't keep a session running past 4 sessions when I do&quot; to be the universal experience for most Tabletop groups.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds a bit excessive to me, but I do think anybody who can get better than bi-weekly sessions on average is in a tiny, tiny minority. Then you adjust for unknown unknowns, and it turns out that 1.5-2 years to get to E3 isn't even a pessimistic estimate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:58:15-07:00","id":1237832,"title":"","content":"I was being a touch hyperbolic. My personal experience is closer to what you just said. I am more quoting what I tend to perceive the complaint to be on forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T16:59:17-07:00","id":1237839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237817#post1237817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like a reason to hate half of the entire game, and not exactly a thing that the game can be blamed for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more of a reason to get really annoyed when Essence 1&amp;2 play isn't engaging and the Essence progression is slowed to make a point about DBs sucking compared to Celestials. I was kind of expecting being an Essence 2 DB to still be pretty hardcore. And it is! Because they have Excellencies that you can use in place of your native Charms to support your Evocations and Martial Arts. Alas, playing a DB using the actual Charmset is a nonstarter because we have stuff like &quot;If your enemy rolls badly, you might get a whole bunch of extra dice on a footrace! You know. If they roll a ton of ones. Otherwise, you're out three motes.&quot; Or &quot;Spend four freaking motes and ignore difficult terrain and fatigue penalties for a <i>split second.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> We also have such gems as &quot;Spend three motes to ignore strength/2 hardness&quot;. Or Graceful Flowing Defense, which lets you spend two motes, one initiative to ignore a <i>single point of penalty.</i> But don't worry, it goes up to three whole penalty points in Water Aura! Which is, to it's credit, just barely worth a Charm, and all it costs you is access to all your attack Charms.<br /> <br /> This is the problem I have with the set. I have to have stuff like <i>this</i> cluttering up my sheet. There's some gems, yeah. But more often than not I have to buy something to reduce half my strength in hardness first. And I really am not interested in playing with mechanics that require me to ignore half of what I spend XP on if I want to pretend I'm actually <i>Exalted.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237822#post1237822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can blame the developers for not gearing the design to your weirdass gaming experience. Repeatedly ending games at that point is clearly <i>not the norm</i>, and if that <i>is</i> your experience, just start at essence 3.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ask around more RP groups. You'll quickly find it's not remotely unusual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T17:46:01-07:00","id":1237845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237602#post1237602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, that's right.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't out-of-aspect Charms like Steel Tempest Strike and Mela's Flashing Tongue be made a bit stronger than usual, because of how difficult it would be for anyone but Air Aspects to use those effects, and given how difficult an Air Aspect's bonfire anima would make accessing the Aura effects of the Fire, Water, and Wood Melee Charms?<br /> <br /> Like how hard it would be to use the Earth-aspected Signature Dodge Charm, for anyone who isn't an Earth Aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure, both Steel Tempest Strike and Flow With Strife have no prerequisite charms, so it's not that hard to snag just them and the balanced charms, and use other ways to get into your Aura. Elusive Crosswind Defense is a little bit harder to use because it's an Aura charm that requires you to purchase two fire charms along the way, which makes for a bit of a balancing act. If you're using ECD you're eating attacks from long or extreme range, probably, since that's when it really shines, in which case Hopping Firecracker Evasion isn't really that useful, since you're already at the limit of your own range.<br /> <br /> You COULD be in a case where you were in a melee, wanted out, and were taking fire from some other combatant at long range, in which case you'd have to gamble if you want to break your aura to hop away, or keep it and super boost your defense from range.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237839#post1237839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the problem I have with the set. I have to have stuff like <i>this</i> cluttering up my sheet. There's some gems, yeah. But more often than not I have to buy something to reduce half my strength in hardness first. And I really am not interested in playing with mechanics that require me to ignore half of what I spend XP on if I want to pretend I'm actually <i>Exalted.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>There's definitely some very situational charms. Like ignoring 2-3+ hardness is only really useful in situations like if you really need to deal just 1 more damage to an enemy but you just reset and he's got 5 hardness or something. You've got some pretty good ones too though, like Blinding Spark Distraction and Flame Warden Stance. Most charm trees go up and down though, like Excellent Friend Approach for Solars is just really not good.<br /> <br /> I'm really curious though, what battles do you think a DB should find easy or hard? Like I actually want to know, I'm not trying to imply that you're wrong, I just can't discuss it without knowing what you want. As it is right now a Blood Ape is a pretty easy fight for a reasonably optimized chargen DB, I'd consider that pretty exalted. You could also take out a battlegroup of bandits and their leader with ease, which is like fighting 20 men and a mortal hero, that's not bad. Fighting a pair of Blood Apes gets to be a bit harder though, and I wouldn't want to fight 3 without backup, but they are supposed to be the most powerful first circle demons. Fighting 3 Agata or Neomah would be no problem for a single Terrestrial Exalt.<br /> <br /> To me that SEEMS about right, but I'm not sure if that's what you're looking for. Like for it to feel Exalted would it be more like fighting a Blood ape and 20 cultists and the cult leader at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T20:29:28-07:00","id":1237872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237845#post1237845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure, both Steel Tempest Strike and Flow With Strife have no prerequisite charms, so it's not that hard to snag just them and the balanced charms, and use other ways to get into your Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>But every Signature Charm requires five dots in the Ability. Most Balanced Charms are around the 1-3 range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T23:06:53-07:00","id":1237897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237872#post1237872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But every Signature Charm requires five dots in the Ability. Most Balanced Charms are around the 1-3 range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm not a huge fan of that. Exalted as a whole has a weird design slant towards maximum abilities. Solar's Feats of Strength tree goes 3&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5, the DB weapon summoning tree goes 1&gt;3&gt;5, the Solar medicine efficiency tree goes 1&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5&gt;5. I'm really not super happy with that as a whole. I think it's a poor design decision, but if you're going to be grabbing signature charms for abilities that you use most often, then you'd probably end up in the range of 4-5 for it anyway. Like if you're getting the only other dedicated water dodge charm Ebbing Tide Recedes, you've got dodge 4.<br /> <br /> The nice thing about the dodge signatures, since dodge is a tree that doesn't have a lot of non-fire charms in it, almost all of them involve expending your aura to take effect. So if you take a bunch of non-balanced charms you can use them no problem after your second action.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth the Unmoving Center of Enlightenment is a really good charm, even by signature standards. It can lock down an entire enemy force into doing nothing but trying and failing to run while you and your entire Hearth beat them down with impunity. It can even just end a combat against a single incredibly powerful creature unless they've got really great resolve or a damn good disengage pool. Like if some hotshot Solar swordsman relies on their parry and has 0 dodge, they're one good (Stamina + Dodge) roll away from just losing this combat to a single charm. Unless I'm reading it wrong again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T06:39:09-07:00","id":1237945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237839#post1237839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or &quot;Spend four freaking motes and ignore difficult terrain and fatigue penalties for a <i>split second.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, the ability to ignore difficult terrain is legit amazing - it's basically the equivalent of an extra reflexive move action, which they otherwise can only do in extremely limited ways, and even then only with the assistance of E3 Charms and usually at the cost of a Willpower.<br /> <br /> In other news, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page859\">Vance says Flame-Borne Interception only triggers after a successful parry</a>, so that's settled. (Granted, having it grant its effect automatically would put it head and shoulders above most non-Excellency, non-Ox-Body E1 Charms, so I can't really say I'm surprised.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T07:22:34-07:00","id":1237956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237945#post1237945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be fair, the ability to ignore difficult terrain is legit amazing - it's basically the equivalent of an extra reflexive move action, which they otherwise can only do in extremely limited ways, and even then only with the assistance of E3 Charms and usually at the cost of a Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it\u2019s a really ST dependant thing, like penalty negators. If you\u2019re like me and throw out penalties for stuff like fighting on a ship deck during a storm, or firing a bow through the smokey haze of a burning battlefield, then penalty negators are great. I\u2019ve seen STs who never use them though and it makes those charms next to useless.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237945#post1237945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other news, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page859&amp;quot;]Vance</a> says Flame-Borne Interception only triggers after a successful parry[/URL], so that's settled. (Granted, having it grant its effect automatically would put it head and shoulders above most non-Excellency, non-Ox-Body E1 Charms, so I can't really say I'm surprised.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow that sucks, you need to be attacked three times for it to even be better than the excellency, and even then only if you parry both first attacks. This might be worth mentioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T07:41:36-07:00","id":1237959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237956#post1237956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it\u2019s a really ST dependant thing, like penalty negators. If you\u2019re like me and throw out penalties for stuff like fighting on a ship deck during a storm, or firing a bow through the smokey haze of a burning battlefield, then penalty negators are great. I\u2019ve seen STs who never use them though and it makes those charms next to useless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Players have agency though - I made my character a Water Aspect because that fit her personality, and instead of complaining that my anima powers are shit (which, compared to Earth/Wood/Fire, they <i>are</i>), I made up an Artifact that allows me to create difficult terrain so I can laugh in Water Aspect at everybody else waddling about with their -3 penalty on movement actions and need to take two movement actions to cross a range band.<br /> <br /> Part of player skill is controlling circumstances so you can use your more situational abilities to great effect. If somebody doesn't like that - well, it's not like Verdant Dragon's Footsteps is a prerequisite for anything, so just don't pick it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 07-23-2018, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:06:38-07:00","id":1237965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237959#post1237959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Players have agency though - I made my character a Water Aspect because that fit her personality, and instead of complaining that my anima powers are shit (which, compared to Earth/Wood/Fire, they <i>are</i>), I made up an Artifact that allows me to create difficult terrain so I can laugh in Water Aspect at everybody else waddling about with their -3 penalty on movement actions and need to take two movement actions to cross a range band.<br /> <br /> Part of player skill is controlling circumstances so you can use your more situational abilities to great effect. If somebody doesn't like that - well, it's not like Verdant Dragon's Footsteps is a prerequisite for anything, so just don't pick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s certainly possible, it\u2019s also campaign dependant too. I\u2019d have a harder time setting battles in really environmentally unfriendly places in a high intrigue campaign as opposed to a darkest jungle exploration one. <br /> <br /> If your ST is taking you into the thickest, harshest part of the eastern greenery VDF all the way.<br /> <br /> I also think I might have found out what FBI is for? But it\u2019s too specific for my tastes. If you\u2019re totally jacked up and have absolute max parry and the penalty negator and the charm that lets you reflexively defend other you can use it pretty effectively if your circle is attacked by a horde of low to mid accuracy enemies to save them, but that\u2019s about it and it absolutely requires maxed parry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:17:12-07:00","id":1237970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237822#post1237822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can blame the developers for not gearing the design to your weirdass gaming experience. Repeatedly ending games at that point is clearly <i>not the norm</i>, and if that <i>is</i> your experience, just start at essence 3. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I only need one finger to count the number of times I've participated in an Exalted game that broke 100xp, and it was 2e and I was the poor fucker running it. And it only made it to the very low 100s.<br /> <br /> As for the actual issue of DB Charms, I'm not sure about the charmset as a whole but I've definitely found cases where the aura mechanic seems to be set up as a major hurdle, like with Safety Among Enemies being the Dodge air signature, requiring Air aura to function at all, being the first Air charm in Dodge, and with only the Excellency even being Balanced. (That Dodge, a near-universal skill, is <i>so</i> Fire-slanted is itself a pain point.)<br /> <br /> There's also Charms that are weaker/less efficient than an Excellency in at least some applications. Like the clinch roll enhancing aspect of Oaken Thew Exertion, which is only as cost-efficient as the Excellency if you have 5 Stamina and at least 5 Brawl+spec.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 07-23-2018, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:25:57-07:00","id":1237973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237845#post1237845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious though, what battles do you think a DB should find easy or hard? Like I actually want to know, I'm not trying to imply that you're wrong, I just can't discuss it without knowing what you want. As it is right now a Blood Ape is a pretty easy fight for a reasonably optimized chargen DB, I'd consider that pretty exalted. You could also take out a battlegroup of bandits and their leader with ease, which is like fighting 20 men and a mortal hero, that's not bad. Fighting a pair of Blood Apes gets to be a bit harder though, and I wouldn't want to fight 3 without backup, but they are supposed to be the most powerful first circle demons. Fighting 3 Agata or Neomah would be no problem for a single Terrestrial Exalt.<br /> <br /> To me that SEEMS about right, but I'm not sure if that's what you're looking for. Like for it to feel Exalted would it be more like fighting a Blood ape and 20 cultists and the cult leader at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the blood ape thing is misleading because I'd actually buff blood apes a good bit if I could. A blood ape really isn't much stronger than an elite mortal hero, which is not my preference in the slightest. But my problem isn't actually in their pure strength. Their Excellency plus some Ox-Bodies is all they really need to be as <i>strong</i> as I want, in terms of the fights they can win. The problem I have is that so many of their effects are so glaringly <i>miniscule.</i> They feel like all they really are is their Excellency and two or three decent Charms around E2. That most of the Charms on my sheet are speedbumps to deplete my XP so I can't have too many <i>good</i> effects.<br /> <br /> This is why I say I'd only have Evocations or MA. So that I can just write or pluck the effects I want, the proper damage adders and boosters, and grab the social Excellencies, and thus everything on my sheet is a valueable thing with purpose. And not a lie meant to keep me from having cool powers I want to use.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I'm fairly certain if I made an Essence 1 Dragonblooded, I'd beat a size 5 battlegroup of battle ready troops, or Size 3 of Blood Apes. I'd back that same Essence 1 DB against two individually statted blood apes, or 4 individual mortal heroes. The powers that matter most in terms of winning fights are your artifacts and your Excellencies and your Ox-Bodies. Everything else is cool powers, flavor, it's the ability to do fun magic that feels like the strength of a Prince of the Earth, or do cool feats that your Excellency alone can't, or enhance your Excellency in some way.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded set has all the power I need it to have. It unfortunately <i>also</i> has a ton of speedbump Charms surrounding the powers I'd actually want to have, which clutter up my sheet and make character designing a mess, because so much of this is stuff I don't want.<br /> <br /> Thus, &quot;fuck it, I'm just making a daiklave and a suit of heavy armor to do the stuff I like&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then I get really depressed because Dragonblooded are my favorite Exalted of all and I can't engage with their Charmset in any way but getting angry at it, and then getting sad about how angry I am at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T02:15:26-07:00","id":1238158,"title":"","content":"Good news everyone!<br /> [/Farnsworth]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it looks like it might become more useful after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237973#post1237973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the blood ape thing is misleading because I'd actually buff blood apes a good bit if I could. A blood ape really isn't much stronger than an elite mortal hero, which is not my preference in the slightest. But my problem isn't actually in their pure strength. Their Excellency plus some Ox-Bodies is all they really need to be as <i>strong</i> as I want, in terms of the fights they can win.<br /> <br /> Snip<br /> <br /> And then I get really depressed because Dragonblooded are my favorite Exalted of all and I can't engage with their Charmset in any way but getting angry at it, and then getting sad about how angry I am at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay now I understand a lot more. I can see where you're coming from. In the Solar charmset you've got some charms that go up and down in power too, but the midline is high enough that they're all really powerful and not very situational, like some of the worse DB charms are. Hopefully if the above response from Vance is any indication we might see a slight power bump in those ones. There are some that probably won't though. Burning Fury Wreath isn't actually that bad, there's times when you'd want it, so it might stay.<br /> <br /> I think that the early game DB charmset really shines for effects that it gives you which aren't strictly speaking super powerful mechanically, but give you really cool options. Like how Dragon Graced weapon lets you add the Disarming tag to any weapon as roots and vines sprout from it, or how Sky Calming Draw can give you a fast way to snap off a Long range arrow. Or even just something like Water Dragon Coils, which lets you forgo dexterity entirely for your grappler character. I think Blinding Spark Distraction is pretty cool, too.<br /> <br /> The ones that just give a mechanical buff aren't that crash hot, because DBs with their artifacts and excellencies are kind of already as powerful as they need to be to strike fear into the hearts of just about anything short of a Second Circle Demon. So to stop them from getting too powerful, most of the charms that directly enhance attacks, accuracy especially, are less efficient than the excellency. That definitely sucks. Like Crossfire Flash is basically just (Essence) non-charm dice and if any of those dice end up a 10, add a further success for 5 motes. It's barely half as efficient as an excellency until you get to essence 4-5 and the only benefit is it's non-charm. The only reason you'd use it is if you were in a hard fight and losing 5 motes is worth it when compared to losing a clash, if those 2-3 successes will make the difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think it's SO bad though. There's maybe 2-3 charms like that in a few of the trees, I'd even argue that a few like Archery and Medicine don't really have any. The REALLY bad thing is that people apparently tend to get into exalted games that only last like 15 sessions, and unless one of those sessions has downtime with downtime xp you're going to miss out on a lot. Almost all of the mechanically mediocre charms are only kind of bad because they rely on (Essence) or sometimes a stat like (Stamina) which gets better as you gain boat loads of xp, obviously. I'm not sure how to fix that though except maybe suggest to your group to just start the game with 150xp and essence 3? Maybe grant 60-90 DXP to even it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T03:02:26-07:00","id":1238165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238158#post1238158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sky Calming Draw can give you a fast way to snap off a Long range arrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... what?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T05:10:36-07:00","id":1238181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238165#post1238165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238158#post1238158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... or how Sky Calming Draw can give you a fast way to snap off a Long range arrow.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um... what?</div> </div> </div> </div> In Air Aura <i>the charm</i> may be used without spending a round aiming. DrLoveMonkey appears to be interpreting this as negating the need to take an Aim Action <i>entirely</i>.<br /> <br /> (Normally an Aim Action must to be taken for an archery attack to be even <i>attempted</i> at long range.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-24-2018, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:02:43-07:00","id":1238193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238181#post1238181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In Air Aura <i>the charm</i> may be used without spending a round aiming. DrLoveMonkey appears to be interpreting this as negating the need to take an Aim Action <i>entirely</i>.<br /> <br /> (Normally an Aim Action must to be taken for an archery attack to be even <i>attempted</i> at long range.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is how it works. In Air Aura it just lets you negate the penalty without aiming that is all.<br /> <br /> Also, that range extension effect is pretty useless for Archery's main weapon, the bow. Only the Self Bow has a medium range. And that is the mortal version.<br /> <br /> Has some uses for crossbows and firewands though.<br /> <br /> Still, very underwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:07:01-07:00","id":1238194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237973#post1237973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A blood ape really isn't much stronger than an elite mortal hero</div> </div> </div> </div>What? How do you figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:12:58-07:00","id":1238195,"title":"","content":"Well, before charms they are basically a tougher tiger warrior.<br /> Then there's principle of motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:29:16-07:00","id":1238199,"title":"","content":"wrong thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:38:58-07:00","id":1238201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238195#post1238195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, before charms they are basically a tougher tiger warrior.<br /> Then there's principle of motion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, AFTER their Kicking Ass Charms, they are something more than their baseline.<br /> <br /> And presumably, that IS a Blood Ape\u2019s baseline. Tiger Warriors are mortal elites, but it is probably possible to find or make elite Blood Apes.<br /> <br /> certainly if you make one a familiar and start applying Survival Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:49:13-07:00","id":1238205,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I can see where that impression might arise because of that barebones stat block, but the presumption alone that such is the standard ape means a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:44:58-07:00","id":1238239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238194#post1238194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? How do you figure?</div> </div> </div> </div>The hero has comparable dice, better soak, better JB. The blood ape has Charms, none of which can be guaranteed to activate, and two extra health levels. The Charms <i>do</i> matter, but not nearly enough to make up for the massive soak and JB difference, IMO. The Blood Ape is stronger over all, but it's not enough to actually make me feel like it's this savage demon ape monstrosity. Given my druthers, it'd have an effect for just flat double tens on decisive damage, two more dice to attack, two more soak, and +1 to each of its defenses. Which takes it from &quot;A pretty even fight for an elite soldier that only has the blood ape dominate by Principle of Motion spam&quot; to &quot;Oh _fucking fuck_ it's a holy shitballs tough demon ape&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, my view of combat specced First Circle demons is that I'd like them to be closer to the Dog of Unbroken Earth than the Harvest God. With a single blood ape assassin tearing it's way through elite soldiers to get the king in his bed, and only being driven off when it turns out Solar Conan was waiting for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238158#post1238158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news everyone!<br /> [/Farnsworth]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1238015#post1238015 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it looks like it might become more useful after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay now I understand a lot more. I can see where you're coming from. In the Solar charmset you've got some charms that go up and down in power too, but the midline is high enough that they're all really powerful and not very situational, like some of the worse DB charms are. Hopefully if the above response from Vance is any indication we might see a slight power bump in those ones. There are some that probably won't though. Burning Fury Wreath isn't actually that bad, there's times when you'd want it, so it might stay.<br /> <br /> I think that the early game DB charmset really shines for effects that it gives you which aren't strictly speaking super powerful mechanically, but give you really cool options. Like how Dragon Graced weapon lets you add the Disarming tag to any weapon as roots and vines sprout from it, or how Sky Calming Draw can give you a fast way to snap off a Long range arrow. Or even just something like Water Dragon Coils, which lets you forgo dexterity entirely for your grappler character. I think Blinding Spark Distraction is pretty cool, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think it's SO bad though. There's maybe 2-3 charms like that in a few of the trees, I'd even argue that a few like Archery and Medicine don't really have any. The REALLY bad thing is that people apparently tend to get into exalted games that only last like 15 sessions, and unless one of those sessions has downtime with downtime xp you're going to miss out on a lot. Almost all of the mechanically mediocre charms are only kind of bad because they rely on (Essence) or sometimes a stat like (Stamina) which gets better as you gain boat loads of xp, obviously. I'm not sure how to fix that though except maybe suggest to your group to just start the game with 150xp and essence 3? Maybe grant 60-90 DXP to even it out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just am not ever gonna play Ex3 Dragonblooded. The problems with the set for me are too baked in. Starting at Essence 3 doesn't solve the problem of Aura, for instance, and the other problems still <i>exist.</i> I don't wanna deal with them as a splat, everytime I try my depression spirals and my night gets ruined. I'm just gonna use homebrew Dragonblooded when I need them as NPCs for Lunars later on, and hope 4th Edition Dragonblooded are better.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the double post, I tried to edit this into my post above but my browser is refusing to let me, it just says WORKING... at the top of the page and then doesn't save the change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 07-24-2018, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:50:47-07:00","id":1238243,"title":"","content":"Oh NOW it goes through","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T09:22:39-07:00","id":1238252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238193#post1238193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that is how it works. In Air Aura it just lets you negate the penalty without aiming that is all.<br /> <br /> Also, that range extension effect is pretty useless for Archery's main weapon, the bow. Only the Self Bow has a medium range. And that is the mortal version.<br /> <br /> Has some uses for crossbows and firewands though.<br /> <br /> Still, very underwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no penalty for firing at medium or long range without aiming. It's just an automatic failure. As per the rules on page 197 of the core, you must spend a round aiming to hit anything at all beyond short range, no matter what your weapon's range is.<br /> <br /> From my read, out of air aura it's basically just a standard charm ignoring penalties from environment. The range extension is pretty niche but useful if it applies. In Air Aura it lets you fire without aiming at medium or long range which effectively doubles your rate of fire at those distances.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that supplemental charms can be used as many times as you want in a turn so long as you're not stacking them. Is ignoring a need for an aim action on multiple different attacks considered stacking? Unknown but if it's not, you can flurry attacks at medium or long range which is not a small thing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, in addition since it does not specifically call out being able to extend the range of firewands it doesn't work on those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 07-24-2018, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T09:33:51-07:00","id":1238255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238252#post1238252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my read, out of air aura it's basically just a standard charm ignoring penalties from environment. The range extension is pretty niche but useful if it applies. In Air Aura it lets you fire without aiming at medium or long range which effectively doubles your rate of fire at those distances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Charm text does not say anything about allowing a character to fire at medium or long range without having to aim.<br /> <br /> Considering how incredibly broken that would be, I find myself heavily doubting an entry-level Charm was meant to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T09:52:10-07:00","id":1238259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238255#post1238255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Charm text does not say anything about allowing a character to fire at medium or long range without having to aim.<br /> <br /> Considering how incredibly broken that would be, I find myself heavily doubting an entry-level Charm was meant to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, yes it does:<br /> <br /> &quot;In Air Aura, the Dragon-Blood may use this Charm without needing to aim beforehand&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: I can see the disconnect here, but it absolutely allows you to make attacks out to medium range without aiming since you can just say &quot;I'm performing a short range withering attack and using this charm to extend it to medium range without spending a turn aiming&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm curious whether it is meant to do an end run around long-range attacks as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 07-24-2018, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:19:29-07:00","id":1238266,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a><br /> <br /> I believe you got the Charm wrong.<br /> <br /> It only negates penalty from bad weather, and also extends the range of the weapon by 1, up until long,and then only if you Aim. <br /> <br /> In Air Aura you can use the Charm without Aiming before.<br /> <br /> So, basically in Air Aura all it does is let you pay 4m to negate a bad weather penalty to the attack.<br /> <br /> The Charm says nothing of eliminating the need to aim for attacks at Medium+ range.<br /> <br /> I broached the subject with Vance, in the Ask the Devs, and he already said it is getting a revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:20:07-07:00","id":1238267,"title":"","content":"So looking at Sky-Calming Draw there are two distinct effects:<br /> <br /> Spend a round aiming and ignore environmental penalties to the shot<br /> <br /> Spend a round aiming and extend the range of a shot by one range band (max long)<br /> <br /> the first one is basically the first half of There is no Wind which is an Archery 5, Essence 2 power for solars. It doesn't have the same &quot;accuraccy bonus is the same as if she had shot at short range&quot; stuff though so that might be why TinW is so much higher requirements. The Solar version does not require an aim, but nor does it relieve the requirement for an aim past short range.<br /> <br /> The second one is utterly useless for any weapon except the hand crossbow. The hand crossbow is literally the only thing that qualifies as an archery medium range weapon. You can't apply this to flame pieces because the flame tag explicitly forbids it without a callout. There is no call out for flame weapons. You can't use it on thrown weapons because it's the wrong ability. Literally every other archery weapon has long range and would take an aim action to fire at that range anyway. <br /> <br /> Then there's air aura: You don't need to take the aim action beforehand. Now it seems that most people are interpreting this as the two effects becoming:<br /> <br /> ignore environmental penalties to the shot.<br /> extend the range of a shot by one range band (max long)<br /> <br /> The first one is nice because you can make shots at any range regardless of weather. Nice<br /> The second one is either really, really good or really, really shit. Either it means you can make medium/or perhaps even long range shots reflexively or it only applies to a single, light weapon in the core and nothing else that we've got stats for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:22:55-07:00","id":1238268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8804_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8804\" data-vbnamecard=\"8804\">armyofwhispers</a> <br /> <br /> Like I said in the post while you were typing, Vance already said the Charm is getting revisioned, since yeah, it is very lackluster at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:31:59-07:00","id":1238298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238259#post1238259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can just say &quot;I'm performing a short range withering attack and using this charm to extend it to medium range without spending a turn aiming&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am reasonably confident that you can't just announce an attack without specifying a target - in which case your original target is either already at short range, thus obviating the need for the Charm, or they're not, and your announcement that you're making a &quot;short range withering attack&quot; becomes invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:35:58-07:00","id":1238305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238298#post1238298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am reasonably confident that you can't just announce an attack without specifying a target - in which case your original target is either already at short range, thus obviating the need for the Charm, or they're not, and your announcement that you're making a &quot;short range withering attack&quot; becomes invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet otherwise this charm does nothing except ignore penalties from environmental effects. So... I guess we'll just have to see what the tweaks are gonna be that the Devs are planning when the final version hits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T13:37:09-07:00","id":1238348,"title":"","content":"It also works for elemental bolt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T15:18:34-07:00","id":1238385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238181#post1238181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In Air Aura <i>the charm</i> may be used without spending a round aiming. DrLoveMonkey appears to be interpreting this as negating the need to take an Aim Action <i>entirely</i>.<br /> <br /> (Normally an Aim Action must to be taken for an archery attack to be even <i>attempted</i> at long range.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you need to take an Aim Action before even attempting an archery attack at MEDIUM range even. Also I made a mistake, I forgot that one aim action was all you needed to fire a shot at Long range. Forgive me, I've only ever ST'd for Solar archers who don't tend to give a fuck. Which made sense to me, you aim for one round to get to medium and then pop the charm to extend it to Long range for one aim action instead of two. Clearly that isn't the case.<br /> <br /> I have to say I didn't even consider that the effect extended the maximum range for an archery attack. Almost every archery weapon in the game has a maximum range of Long anyway, I think just the hand crossbow doesn't, and EBA if we're including charms. It's basically a non-effect that exists exclusively for people using EBA or hand crossbows, which is just so strange. That needs to be changed for the final release.<br /> <br /> It's not even like it's a god-awful garbage charm without that effect, -3 is a pretty common penalty, -5 isn't unheard of, so it's a little underwhelming but not like FBI levels of situational, fighting while in a storm or on a windy plane happens decently often. Even if they just drop the wording about extending range would help the charm not be confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T15:41:59-07:00","id":1238396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238239#post1238239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just am not ever gonna play Ex3 Dragonblooded. The problems with the set for me are too baked in. Starting at Essence 3 doesn't solve the problem of Aura, for instance, and the other problems still <i>exist.</i> I don't wanna deal with them as a splat, everytime I try my depression spirals and my night gets ruined. I'm just gonna use homebrew Dragonblooded when I need them as NPCs for Lunars later on, and hope 4th Edition Dragonblooded are better.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the double post, I tried to edit this into my post above but my browser is refusing to let me, it just says WORKING... at the top of the page and then doesn't save the change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, looks like it. Maybe give it another look when the book releases? It looks like a lot of us have brought concerns like this to Vance and he's mentioned that they're slated to change. I'd be okay with them as they are, personally, but I'd definitely like them to get buffed obviously. Just as long as it's not so far that it changes the DB dynamic where everyone needs to pitch in when they get charged by half a dozen Blood Apes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T17:54:20-07:00","id":1238430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238396#post1238396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, looks like it. Maybe give it another look when the book releases? It looks like a lot of us have brought concerns like this to Vance and he's mentioned that they're slated to change. I'd be okay with them as they are, personally, but I'd definitely like them to get buffed obviously. Just as long as it's not so far that it changes the DB dynamic where everyone needs to pitch in when they get charged by half a dozen Blood Apes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, six individually statted blood apes means it's like...the Blue Banded Beasts, the elite group of martial artist blood ape assassins who are trained in Supernatural Martial Arts. Otherwise six blood apes is just a Might 2 battlegroup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T19:52:09-07:00","id":1238484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1238430#post1238430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean, six individually statted blood apes means it's like...the Blue Banded Beasts, the elite group of martial artist blood ape assassins who are trained in Supernatural Martial Arts. Otherwise six blood apes is just a Might 2 battlegroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I did that a few times in this one campaign I ran. It was a whole demons of the southern sands thing where some nefarious individual was using an artifact to summon demons from hell whereafter he trained them and equipped them with special weapons and armor and stuff. They ended up getting so numerous that even with the individual style of them I had to start sticking them in battle groups, but it was a cool escalation from fighting 5 of them in the first session or two to cutting through over 100 in one combat by the end of the campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T14:04:47-07:00","id":1240207,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to make a Dragonblooded for a game I just got a place in. Reading this book is <i>soul-crushing.</i> I can only assume the rest of you have some kind of stockholm syndrome, because <i>goddamn</i> this is a shitty Charmset to try to and make something remotely fun out of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T14:28:20-07:00","id":1240214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240207#post1240207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to make a Dragonblooded for a game I just got a place in. Reading this book is <i>soul-crushing.</i> I can only assume the rest of you have some kind of stockholm syndrome, because <i>goddamn</i> this is a shitty Charmset to try to and make something remotely fun out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, my players are extremely excited for the campaign that I am gearing up to run in September, and they do not view their charmset as debilitating in the slightest. Instead, they have gotten more and more excited as we draw closer to our start so /shurg/. Your opinions on the matter are not objective fact nor does the fact that you may not find the charmset satisfying in anyway shape or form take away from other player's enjoyment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T14:51:15-07:00","id":1240220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237973#post1237973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the blood ape thing is misleading because I'd actually buff blood apes a good bit if I could. A blood ape really isn't much stronger than an elite mortal hero, which is not my preference in the slightest. But my problem isn't actually in their pure strength. Their Excellency plus some Ox-Bodies is all they really need to be as <i>strong</i> as I want, in terms of the fights they can win. The problem I have is that so many of their effects are so glaringly <i>miniscule.</i> They feel like all they really are is their Excellency and two or three decent Charms around E2. That most of the Charms on my sheet are speedbumps to deplete my XP so I can't have too many <i>good</i> effects.<br /> <br /> This is why I say I'd only have Evocations or MA. So that I can just write or pluck the effects I want, the proper damage adders and boosters, and grab the social Excellencies, and thus everything on my sheet is a valueable thing with purpose. And not a lie meant to keep me from having cool powers I want to use.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I'm fairly certain if I made an Essence 1 Dragonblooded, I'd beat a size 5 battlegroup of battle ready troops, or Size 3 of Blood Apes. I'd back that same Essence 1 DB against two individually statted blood apes, or 4 individual mortal heroes. The powers that matter most in terms of winning fights are your artifacts and your Excellencies and your Ox-Bodies. Everything else is cool powers, flavor, it's the ability to do fun magic that feels like the strength of a Prince of the Earth, or do cool feats that your Excellency alone can't, or enhance your Excellency in some way.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded set has all the power I need it to have. It unfortunately <i>also</i> has a ton of speedbump Charms surrounding the powers I'd actually want to have, which clutter up my sheet and make character designing a mess, because so much of this is stuff I don't want.<br /> <br /> Thus, &quot;fuck it, I'm just making a daiklave and a suit of heavy armor to do the stuff I like&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then I get really depressed because Dragonblooded are my favorite Exalted of all and I can't engage with their Charmset in any way but getting angry at it, and then getting sad about how angry I am at it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is incoherent. First you're saying that 3e Dragon-Blooded have all the power you want them to have, right now, with just the excellencies and a few ox-bodies. Okay, so you're satisfied with that representing the floor of Exalted power. But then you say you'd only buy Evocations or MA for greater mechanical power. Bwuh? <br /> <br /> Earlier you stated that you want the DB baseline to be all the benefits of the Aura keyword at all times, but you go on to reiterate that the DB set has all the power you need it to have. And what are the 'speedbump' charms in the way of your enjoyment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1237973#post1237973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything else is cool powers, flavor, it's the ability to do fun magic that feels like the strength of a Prince of the Earth, or do cool feats that your Excellency alone can't, or enhance your Excellency in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...cool powers? Elemental flavor? Fun magic? Seems like these things are a major reason to want to play the Dragonblooded, especially if you're happy with their mechanical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T16:54:53-07:00","id":1240245,"title":"","content":"I don't really get how it can be difficult to grasp that a group of people who want to have fun playing dragon blooded crafted this charmset, tested it, and decided &quot;yeah, this is fun. I think players will enjoy playing a character with these charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then they released them, and shockingly, the vast majority of players... <i>agreed</i><i> with them? </i>And haven't developed &quot;stockholm syndrome&quot; from... what, exactly? This is the first charmset released by the new dev team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T17:33:36-07:00","id":1240259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240220#post1240220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is incoherent. First you're saying that 3e Dragon-Blooded have all the power you want them to have, right now, with just the excellencies and a few ox-bodies. Okay, so you're satisfied with that representing the floor of Exalted power. But then you say you'd only buy Evocations or MA for greater mechanical power. Bwuh?<br /> <br /> Earlier you stated that you want the DB baseline to be all the benefits of the Aura keyword at all times, but you go on to reiterate that the DB set has all the power you need it to have. And what are the 'speedbump' charms in the way of your enjoyment?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So...cool powers? Elemental flavor? Fun magic? Seems like these things are a major reason to want to play the Dragonblooded, especially if you're happy with their mechanical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Reroll dice based on the tens in your roll, but only if you stunt a jump.&quot; &quot;Negate one point of penalty on your defense.&quot; &quot;Negate strength/2 hardness.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't see many cool powers. Or elemental flavor. Or fun magic. I see a dull as dishwater Charmset that is carried by the fact that Excellencies and Ox-Bodies exist, and the 3e system allows Dragonblooded to simply overwhelm their opponents by outnumbering them with repeated max-Excellencies. Even the signatures are shit half the time.<br /> <br /> I don't want to have a dice trick to enhance an attempt at jumping. I'd like to just be better at athletics period, thanks, and not spend my Charms on minor dice enhancers on specific actions. My excellency does that plenty, thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240245#post1240245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get how it can be difficult to grasp that a group of people who want to have fun playing dragon blooded crafted this charmset, tested it, and decided &quot;yeah, this is fun. I think players will enjoy playing a character with these charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then they released them, and shockingly, the vast majority of players... <i>agreed</i><i> with them? </i>And haven't developed &quot;stockholm syndrome&quot; from... what, exactly? This is the first charmset released by the new dev team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's <i>awful</i> for anyone who is of the opinion that maybe Dragonblooded shouldn't be the worst in <i>literally every way, by a mile.</i> That there's more to Charms than enhancing niche actions. That if the Excellency outshines the Charmset so much you feel like you need to limit it to give the Charms actual use, then <i>maybe you should be enhancing the Charms.</i><br /> <br /> I loathe this Charmset. I loathe the mentality behind it. I'd take 2.5 over this every time. I want to have <i>actual fun</i> with my magic. Not occasionally reroll tens. Not have two thirds of my powers be situational nonsense best replaced by taking 12 Excellencies and 3 Ox-Bodies, or Resonant Evocations. I want the meat of the set to be Essence 1, not Essence 3, you know, like the Solar powers were, so you start with strong, easily applicable powers.<br /> <br /> If I have dice tricks, I want them to be at least <i>good,</i> not tied to how many tens get rolled. If there has to be penalty negation, it should be <i>good.</i> Not &quot;One point, three in Aura.&quot; <i>I wouldn't want the three as its own Charm, let alone the one.</i><br /> <br /> Second Edition was at least <i>honest</i> about you being nothing compared to the Solars. &quot;You have cool powers, but they won't function against a Solar&quot; is something I'll take every single time over &quot;You have cool powers, that apply only sometimes, and are really expensive so you can't maintain them, and you can't grab all the good ones, and a lot of them are really bad unless you fiddle with Aura, and if you ever meet a Solar you will be reduced to a smear that he scrapes off his shining boot if you dare to imagine you might so much as put up a fight without outnumbering 3-1.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just having a stronger mote pool, a higher dice cap, and all those insane extra actions and free Excellencies is more than enough. Everything else didn't need to be bottom of the barrel. It wasn't in 2e!<br /> <br /> You might be happy with this. Goody for you. I'm not, because I really thought we'd moved past this. Past Dragonblooded being _the weakest_ of the Exalted, rather than the weakest _of the Exalted._ But, no. They're still hampered by relentless inferiority whenever a comparison to Solars comes up. By uneven XP costs and differing Essence progression. By rules that make me ask why I <i>ever</i> thought playing one of the Dragonblooded would be cool, rather than staring at the resources given and asking why I'm bothering with any of this. I can't casually leap from building to building, can't fly until the game is almost over, and even then not without shutting off all my other Charms. Can't duel one of the Anathema in a glorious losing battle, shining brightly and holding the line long enough for my heroics to matter, for my loss to have meaning and dignity.<br /> <br /> Because, hah, no. That Anathema is gonna grapple me and kill me in one action while I flail pointlessly. Or attack three times a round to my one, with a passive 9 Defense that they can raise even higher if I max Excellency. Can launch their free full Excellencies and instantly gain a further 10+ mote lead on me. Can do all the cool wuxia stuff I thought I'd be allowed to do, since how can you reduce Solar athletics much more than it is, it's already really straightorward, reducing it a bunch would just make it useless. And <i>that's literally what they did.</i><br /> <br /> What am I missing? The lack of uncountable damage defenses, gotta make sure DBs are less than Solars there, can't let them have any powers that prove that they're not gonna be deprotagonized by natural disasters. The lack of solid damage and accuracy enhancers, can't let them readily hit Solars, nope nope. The best defensive Charm is in <i>fucking stealth</i> for some nonsense reason.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, this is an <i>amazing</i> Charmset, it totally isn't a repeat of Second Edition. The big difference is that it doesn't <i>spell out</i> that you'll never, ever beat a Solar, ever, because you're just a Mookblooded, barely even a real Exalt. It leaves that as an unpleasant surprise the second you meet a Solar the ST didn't deliberately nerf.<br /> <br /> God forbid they meet a Second Circle Demon, either, or a powerful god. They even lost their ability to spirit kill! They literally lost something they've always had, to show <i>how much better the Solars are than you.</i><br /> <br /> It's never enough for the Solars to be stronger, faster, and better than you. They need to have all the tricks you lack, the power to back it up, and be able to best your five Charms to their one every time. They even get free Excellencies, while Dragonblooded have to buy theirs. Essence 1 Solars easily have a 6-10 Charm advantage, because they get free Excellencies, and you don't. And their Charms are insanely better, more efficient, more motes. Everything. Every little thing reminds me.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why am I doing this? Every little detail is telling me not to bother with the mookblooded, go play a Solar instead, be someone who <i>matters.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded used to have <i>that, </i>too. Used to be more efficient! They lost that too. This is what I mean when I say I liked 2.5 better. Because I could cheaply pile on the damage and the dice, and feel like a cool badass, even if the Solars got a higher tier of magic I couldn't match. Because my powers were cool and badass, and not tiny numbers for huge costs, with extra fiddly details and endless little reminders: &quot;There's a spirit Charm that does literally this, for a Essence 2 god, except it isn't restricted to &quot;strength&quot; and doesn't cost a willpower.&quot;<br /> <br /> I hate this. I hate <i>feeling</i> like this. I hate hating my<i> favorite splat.</i> But I don't want to do this <i>again.</i> Don't want to spend another edition knowing that the Solars are the only ones who actually matter, and everyone else is the dirt beneath their feet. I hated that feeling in Second Edition, and I'd rather just do what the book obviously wants me to do, and use the Dragonblooded as an NPC only splat, mooks to challenge the Solars on their inevitable road to ultimate triumph.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you think I'm spitting with rage right now. But I'm not. I'm angry, yeah. But mostly? I'm sitting in a chair, staring at my screen, more depressed than I've been in a long time, wondering how the hell this happened, when just four months ago I was happier and less depressed than I'd been in years, because Dragonblooded was just around the corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 07-29-2018, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:05:51-07:00","id":1240279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240259#post1240259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Reroll dice based on the tens in your roll, but only if you stunt a jump.&quot; &quot;Negate one point of penalty on your defense.&quot; &quot;Negate strength/2 hardness.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't see many cool powers. Or elemental flavor. Or fun magic. I see a dull as dishwater Charmset that is carried by the fact that Excellencies and Ox-Bodies exist, and the 3e system allows Dragonblooded to simply overwhelm their opponents by outnumbering them with repeated max-Excellencies. Even the signatures are shit half the time.<br /> <br /> I don't want to have a dice trick to enhance an attempt at jumping. I'd like to just be better at athletics period, thanks, and not spend my Charms on minor dice enhancers on specific actions. My excellency does that plenty, thanks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Here are a collection of cool E1-2 powers just from casually skimming the manuscript: Dragon's Hidden Treasure, Speech Without Words, Elemental Bolt Attack, Dragon-Graced Weapon, Fivefold Resonance Sense. All of them either expand your toolkit of what you can do or provide cool elemental flavor or both. The utility bread and butter charms that manipulate dice or negate penalties are worth using for their mote cost - for example, if you're suffering a defense penalty and you want to raise your DV to max they're a no-brainer.<br /> <br /> The common theme I'm seeing here is a constant comparison of mechanical power to the Solar Exalted, not a sober evaluation of how good a given charm is to use in the context of a DB game. Saying, &quot;I don't like the balance of power between Solars and DBs&quot; is a very different statement from &quot;The Dragon-Blooded charmset sucks and is full of useless speedbump charms.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240259#post1240259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate this. I hate <i>feeling</i> like this. I hate hating my<i> favorite splat.</i> But I don't want to do this <i>again.</i> Don't want to spend another edition knowing that the Solars are the only ones who actually matter, and everyone else is the dirt beneath their feet. I hated that feeling in Second Edition, and I'd rather just do what the book obviously wants me to do, and use the Dragonblooded as an NPC only splat, mooks to challenge the Solars on their inevitable road to ultimate triumph.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you think I'm spitting with rage right now. But I'm not. I'm angry, yeah. But mostly? I'm sitting in a chair, staring at my screen, more depressed than I've been in a long time, wondering how the hell this happened, when just four months ago I was happier and less depressed than I'd been in years, because Dragonblooded was just around the corner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:21:05-07:00","id":1240283,"title":"","content":"I've been following this whole thread and still don't see where you're coming from, Fenrir. DB can grapple with tendrils of water, use their essence to rig bodies to explode, literally fly, run up surfaces buoyed by the essence of fire, summon a sweet tree to turn into a turret, play some pure perception tricks on people to fool them into thinking you're a prince or a pauper, and more while also having selections of dice tricks and effect boosters that are mechanically less efficient than Solars but not so that they don't feel fun to play, at least for my group.<br /> <br /> There are a few lemons in there, like FBI, but those hopefully will get a rework before the final release and even still don't manage to drag down the play experience for my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:30:22-07:00","id":1240288,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Fenrir's comments mostly seem to be &quot;these suck compared to Solar charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> And... yes? That's kind of how Terrestrials roll?<br /> <br /> But the difference is they can, for fleeting moments, achieve comparable effects if they try very hard and even at lower power their charms don't actually lock them out of even being a threat. (The aforementioned, many times, 'perfect defense useless against anything using magic, which is to say any attack by another Exalt').<br /> <br /> They just roll less dice, generally. On the other hand, there's a lot of people like you, you aren't literally considered a demon by the major religion of the world (quite the contrary) and making more Dragonblooded is a fairly simple and even enjoyable process, for some.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:41:22-07:00","id":1240292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240279#post1240279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here are a collection of cool E1-2 powers just from casually skimming the manuscript: Dragon's Hidden Treasure, Speech Without Words, Elemental Bolt Attack, Dragon-Graced Weapon, Fivefold Resonance Sense. All of them either expand your toolkit of what you can do or provide cool elemental flavor or both. The utility bread and butter charms that manipulate dice or negate penalties are worth using for their mote cost - for example, if you're suffering a defense penalty and you want to raise your DV to max they're a no-brainer.<br /> <br /> The common theme I'm seeing here is a constant comparison of mechanical power to the Solar Exalted, not a sober evaluation of how good a given charm is to use in the context of a DB game. Saying, &quot;I don't like the balance of power between Solars and DBs&quot; is a very different statement from &quot;The Dragon-Blooded charmset sucks and is full of useless speedbump charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon's Hidden Teasure: Meh, elsewhere storage. I'd rather just, you know. Carry my sword. Also requires one of the distinctly unmagical ones as prereq, so double <i>meh.</i><br /> Speech WIthout Words: Oh, joy. Telepathy, except people can notice, with a prerequisite Charm that...mildly enhances my ability to eavesdrop. Once again, I'm left wondering: Was this written explicitly to remind us that Dragonblooded don't get to have anything without a glaring hole in it. Just give me the damn telepathy without this &quot;oh but mookblooded, better make sure mortals get a chance to notice.&quot;<br /> Elemental Bolt Attack: oh joy, once more Fire is the only one worth buying. Hard pass, I'll get an artifact with Evocations instead. Way, way better use of my resources.<br /> Dragon-Graced Weapon: It's a mortal sword with a crappy little elemental bonus. No thanks, I'll just <i>use my daiklave.</i><br /> Fivefold Resonance Sense: This is the only one I would spend a Charmslot on, congrats, you found one cool Charm.<br /> <br /> Two out of five Charms is something worth the Charmslots to get to, rather than just using my Excellency and artifacts. Of those two, one has a Charm that I cannot for the life of me imagine wasting XP on, the other's prereq is...the fucking Excellency, oh joy, we're gating Charms behind Excellencies, awesome.<br /> <br /> Fuck. Mookblooded.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240288#post1240288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Fenrir's comments mostly seem to be &quot;these suck compared to Solar charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> And... yes? That's kind of how Terrestrials roll?<br /> <br /> But the difference is they can, for fleeting moments, achieve comparable effects if they try very hard and even at lower power their charms don't actually lock them out of even being a threat. (The aforementioned, many times, 'perfect defense useless against anything using magic, which is to say any attack by another Exalt').<br /> <br /> They just roll less dice, generally. On the other hand, there's a lot of people like you, you aren't literally considered a demon by the major religion of the world (quite the contrary) and making more Dragonblooded is a fairly simple and even enjoyable process, for some.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't actually <i>have</i> to suck compared to Solar Charms. They could be <i>not as good, but still strong.</i> Also, hah, no. They're not a threat to a Solar unless they have enough to overwhelm the Solar's motes. Not even a little. At Essence 1, the Solar can easily attack them three times for every one attack. Two withering, one decisive, reset to back, two withering, one decisive, reset to base. Repeat until your inevitable victory.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded's best possible decisive attack pool: 5/5/1+6, +2 for Stunt. That's 19.<br /> <br /> Solar's casual low Essence defense: 5+5+1+Medium Weapon for base defense 7. 2m on Dipping Swallow, ignore all penalties. Fivefold Bulwark Stance: Dipping Swallow is now 1m, and raises parry by one. The Solar has an unlowerable defense of 9 after their stunt. Hail-Shattering Practice. They rob one or two of your Successes, depending on if this is an Essence one Solar with Supernal Melee, or an Essence 2 Solar.<br /> <br /> How much are you spending on those damage Charms and Excellencies? How much is the Solar Spending on maintaining this (Hint: Less than you. A lot less.)<br /> <br /> Excellent Strike, Dipping Swallow, Bulwark, Fivefold Bulwark, One Weapon, Two Blows, Solar Counterattack. Six Charms. That leaves 9 free. One Essence 2 Charm. Feel free to drop Fivefold Bulwark, it makes their defense moderately less efficient. But that just means that have some <i>other</i> Supernal. Melee is the worst offender, but Brawl isn't much less unstoppable. My personal favorite is Resistance, but it's also not nearly as broken. Just infinitely better than anything you can even try to do.<br /> <br /> This isn't even super optimized, this is just grabbing all the early Melee Charms because you have Supernal Melee, woo!<br /> <br /> Once I actually start playing this for real, not just with grabbagging early Melee Charms, but actually <i>trying, </i>it just gets worse and worse.<br /> <br /> Don't even get me <i>started</i> on Black Claw+Dodge.<br /> <br /> I don't want them to be equal to Solars, that's not what this is about. I want a Solar who stares down a Dragonblooded to not <i>be assured of victory</i> unless it's an Essence 5 Immaculate Master. I want there to be an actual back in forth. I want the Solar to have a strong edge, and the advantage of a Supernal. Not &quot;honestly, given the sheer disparity between your Essence 3 Charms and his Essence 1 Charms, do we even want to run this?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 07-29-2018, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:10:31-07:00","id":1240302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240292#post1240292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon's Hidden Teasure: Meh, elsewhere storage. I'd rather just, you know. Carry my sword. Also requires one of the distinctly unmagical ones as prereq, so double <i>meh.</i><br /> Speech WIthout Words: Oh, joy. Telepathy, except people can notice, with a prerequisite Charm that...mildly enhances my ability to eavesdrop. Once again, I'm left wondering: Was this written explicitly to remind us that Dragonblooded don't get to have anything without a glaring hole in it. Just give me the damn telepathy without this &quot;oh but mookblooded, better make sure mortals get a chance to notice.&quot;<br /> Elemental Bolt Attack: oh joy, once more Fire is the only one worth buying. Hard pass, I'll get an artifact with Evocations instead. Way, way better use of my resources.<br /> Dragon-Graced Weapon: It's a mortal sword with a crappy little elemental bonus. No thanks, I'll just <i>use my daiklave.</i><br /> Fivefold Resonance Sense: This is the only one I would spend a Charmslot on, congrats, you found one cool Charm.<br /> <br /> Two out of five Charms is something worth the Charmslots to get to, rather than just using my Excellency and artifacts. Of those two, one has a Charm that I cannot for the life of me imagine wasting XP on, the other's prereq is...the fucking Excellency, oh joy, we're gating Charms behind Excellencies, awesome.<br /> <br /> Fuck. Mookblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dragon's Hidden Treasure allows you to store any held object in solid stone. It's a perfect fit for both Larceny and the elemental flavor of Earth magic, it has way more applications than just storing a weapon somewhere.<br /> <br /> So your problem with being able to speak telepathically is that people get a chance to notice. How many truly perfect effects do you think there are in the game? You can defeat Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise and Flawless Pickpocketing technique in 3e.<br /> <br /> Fire is the only EBA worth taking? It's telling that you seem to be unaware of how powerful the Smashing Tag is 3e Exalted, or cheap ranged decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> Also, summoning a mortal sword isn't even what Dragon-Graced Weapon does. It provides an elemental bonus to a jade artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> Again, those are just charms I brought up from casually skimming the manuscript. Rather than try to refute that they are examples of toolbox enhancers that convey the elemental theme of the Dragon-Blooded, you nitpick or misrepresent what they actually do. Frankly you seem more interested in trolling rather than having a discussion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:24:13-07:00","id":1240306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240302#post1240302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dragon's Hidden Treasure allows you to store any held object in solid stone. It's a perfect fit for both Larceny and the elemental flavor of Earth magic, it has way more applications than just storing a weapon somewhere.<br /> <br /> So your problem with being able to speak telepathically is that people get a chance to notice. How many truly perfect effects do you think there are in the game? You can defeat Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise and Flawless Pickpocketing technique in 3e.<br /> <br /> Fire is the only EBA worth taking? It's telling that you seem to be unaware of how powerful the Smashing Tag is 3e Exalted, or cheap ranged decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> Also, summoning a mortal sword isn't even what Dragon-Graced Weapon does. It provides an elemental bonus to a jade artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> Again, those are just charms I brought up from casually skimming the manuscript. Rather than try to refute that they are examples of toolbox enhancers that convey the elemental theme of the Dragon-Blooded, you nitpick or misrepresent what they actually do. Frankly you seem more interested in trolling rather than having a discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, it provides a shitty bonus to an artifact weapon. <i>I'd still rather buy an Evocation.</i> Also, fucking <i>lol.</i> Trolling? Not agreeing with you is trolling, right.<br /> <br /> I still wouldn't want to buy any of these Charms. If I want the smashing tag, I will use a smashing weapon. Or have an Evocation that triggers the effect. They're toolbox enhancers, sure. So's a 5 dollar swiss army knife that snaps the first time you try to use it on something you actually need it for. I don't really care what elemental themes they convey, I want them to be good. I want a reason to use the native Charms of the Dragonblooded rather than Evocations and Martial Art Charms.<br /> <br /> You have given me no such reason. The only thing you've done is prove that they are not <i>literally, actually useless.</i><br /> <br /> Fortunately, that was never my point. My point was that they're crappy. Underwhelming. Underpowered and overpriced. Godblooded design space. Not Exalted.<br /> <br /> And, yes. I expect my goddamned telepathy Charm to not be subject to being seen. That's the point of being psychic. Having hidden conversations. &quot;But other Charms have failure states-&quot; <i>I don't care.</i> This one shouldn't. Particularly not such an obvious one.<br /> <br /> None of these give me a particularly compelling reason to not just burn motes on my Excellency, save arguably Dragon's Hidden Treasure and definitely the crappy telepathy, but it's still got the glaring hole, so <i>meh.</i> That's my whole beef. The Charms are completely superfluous when you have the Excellency. And if you <i>do</i> find a problem your Excellency can't solve, and you need Charms? Your Charms suck so completely that you still are better off spamming the stupid Excellency.<br /> <br /> My answer to cheap ranged decisives, fyi? White-jade crossbow. Wah-wah-waaaaaaah once again I come out ridiculously ahead for not bothering with the crappy native Charmset, because <i>I</i> get to have the power of Resonant Evocations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:27:52-07:00","id":1240308,"title":"","content":"You're not even trying to defend your original argument that, 'WFHW is full of useless speedbump charms that aren't worth using.' You just jumped over to comparing them unfavorably to Solar charms. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240292#post1240292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want them to be equal to Solars, that's not what this is about. I want a Solar who stares down a Dragonblooded to not <i>be assured of victory</i> unless it's an Essence 5 Immaculate Master. I want there to be an actual back in forth. I want the Solar to have a strong edge, and the advantage of a Supernal. Not &quot;honestly, given the sheer disparity between your Essence 3 Charms and his Essence 1 Charms, do we even want to run this?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What about your statement that you were totally fine with DB power as just the excellency and a few ox-bodies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240292#post1240292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Their Excellency plus some Ox-Bodies is all they really need to be as </i><i>strong</i><i> as I want, in terms of the fights they can win.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like you actually want more than that. <br /> <br /> Additionally, the example you chose was full of implicit assumptions about the relative combat investment of the Solar and DB. You can get what you claim you want by just having a far more combat invested DB relative to a Solar. In your example you choose a heavily invested Dawn Caste...well, yeah, not only are they the strongest Exalted, they're the foremost fighters of the Solar Exalted. Yeah, I think being assured of victory against a single Dragon-Blooded pretty correctly reflects the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:36:59-07:00","id":1240310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240306#post1240306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, it provides a shitty bonus to an artifact weapon. <i>I'd still rather buy an Evocation.</i> Also, fucking <i>lol.</i> Trolling? Not agreeing with you is trolling, right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, but your hostile tone and condescending attitude is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240306#post1240306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I don't really care what elemental themes they convey,</div> </div> </div> </div>You said earlier that you wanted cool powers and you were a DB fan, but now you also don't care if your charmset has elemental themes that tie into what they do. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240306#post1240306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My answer to cheap ranged decisives, fyi? White-jade crossbow. Wah-wah-waaaaaaah once again I come out ridiculously ahead for not bothering with the crappy native Charmset, because <i>I</i> get to have the power of Resonant Evocations!</div> </div> </div> </div> Weapon agnostic ranged decisive attacks that don't require a ready/weapon misc action are powerful in 3e. The bonus they get on top of that is considerable too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:55:03-07:00","id":1240314,"title":"","content":"You're never going to sway me. I'm never going to sway you. This is just pointless, and I should have realized it a long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 07-30-2018, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T21:03:40-07:00","id":1240317,"title":"","content":"You're never going to sway me. I'm never going to sway you. This is just pointless, and I should have realized it a long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 07-30-2018, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T23:29:47-07:00","id":1240337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240314#post1240314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're never going to sway me. I'm never going to sway you. This is just pointless, and I should have realized it a long time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, because so far it seems like you never actually wanted to play a Terrestrial Exalt; you want a Solar with different special effects and none of the social issues of Solars.<br /> <br /> That's never been the intended DB experience. They're the most social Exalted because there's enough for a *society*. Which means they aren't as individually powerful, but they're still not &quot;mooks&quot;. There is no point where you have a battle group.of DBs.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with a more powerful elemental Exalt, and I hope Exigents will help there. But what you claim to want, and what your words say you want, are two very different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T00:38:00-07:00","id":1240346,"title":"","content":"I don't know why people keep shitting on Graceful Flowing Defense. 1 point of parry penalty negation for 2m, 1i is actually pretty solid, when you consider that you're essentially paying 1i to make a point of parry non-charm in what is likely a situation where the discount on the excellency wouldn't apply. <br /> <br /> That seems to be a theme of the non-excellency melee charms, actually. The excellency works best one-on-one, and the charms that follow seem to be intended to plug the gap that come up if they have multiple opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:04:43-07:00","id":1240357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240207#post1240207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to make a Dragonblooded for a game I just got a place in. Reading this book is <i>soul-crushing.</i> I can only assume the rest of you have some kind of stockholm syndrome, because <i>goddamn</i> this is a shitty Charmset to try to and make something remotely fun out of.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>I warned you about your posts very recently. Take a month off to reconsider how you talk to people. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:52:09-07:00","id":1240370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240346#post1240346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why people keep shitting on Graceful Flowing Defense. 1 point of parry penalty negation for 2m, 1i is actually pretty solid, when you consider that you're essentially paying 1i to make a point of parry non-charm in what is likely a situation where the discount on the excellency wouldn't apply.<br /> <br /> That seems to be a theme of the non-excellency melee charms, actually. The excellency works best one-on-one, and the charms that follow seem to be intended to plug the gap that come up if they have multiple opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Graceful Flowing Defense is fine. There's one or two charms I think are a bit weak, but DB melee offers multiple viable build paths - depending on element - and their E1-2 charms are mostly solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T03:58:44-07:00","id":1240383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240292#post1240292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar's casual low Essence defense: 5+5+1+Medium Weapon for base defense 7. 2m on Dipping Swallow, ignore all penalties. Fivefold Bulwark Stance: Dipping Swallow is now 1m, and raises parry by one. The Solar has an unlowerable defense of 9 after their stunt. Hail-Shattering Practice. They rob one or two of your Successes, depending on if this is an Essence one Solar with Supernal Melee, or an Essence 2 Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And this is why the assumption of maximum optimization as the default is literally poisonous to the game line.<br /> <br /> (Granted, medium weapons' omni-applicable free +1 Defense doesn't help.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T05:55:06-07:00","id":1240401,"title":"","content":"Well, not defending Fenrir's particular style of getting their message across, but must admit there is a basis to the basic complaint.<br /> <br /> Essence 3 really is a long way off, even if, like us, you condense the progression chart. I too thought that the printed Martial Arts and evocations usually offer a tighter and more focused package of charms that seem much easier to build around than their regular charm trees, especially in the area of combat. I can also see Aura as not being too loved by many players in my regular group for whom Exalted is already at the very edge of their crunch-comfort zone and <i>really </i>don't need yet another thing to track.<br /> <br /> Now, as to comparing with Solars, in my opinion it is not something to shy away from. After all, my tables, mine included, really enjoy mixed splat games, and while admittedly it is just an impression based on just reading and not actual in-game experience with the DB, just the Solars, but to me the gap looks a great deal wider than it was before, and further exacerbated by Solars having Supernal abilities. In Ex2.5, if your DB wasn't combat focused, the xp charts were fixed and there was some minimal niche protection agreed upon, it was actually rather fine, while, if you play the DB in a Solar party now, I'm not so sure you feel you are not a total chump and henchman, even with your cultural advantages.<br /> <br /> Again, a lot of this stems from Supernals and how shockingly fast Solars can shift the game into perfect-or-die territory, which I personally find more problematic than the design of the Dragon-Blooded, to be honest. The fact remains: if you can't mix the splats and have a fun and exciting game without too much work to make it work, I personally find it a failure, and from that point of view this iteration of DB's look to be firmly in the camp of 'NPC only' or 'Single splat only', except perhaps for a pre-gen'd short story arc. In a longer more regular campaign by the time the DB's reach Essence 3 and their signature charms the Solars will be so ridiculously ahead on the power-curve it takes a rare kind of player who can stomach that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:23:10-07:00","id":1240410,"title":"","content":"It's kind of expected that a dragon blooded is gonna have an artifact, and a few evocations with it. Those are their best powers, after all. But evocations can supplement their native charm tree, not just supplant it. <br /> <br /> Like, lots of evocations enhance native charms, or provide more opportunities to use one that might be a bit niche. And the fact that they're aura-neutral can help you keep one up when you need it. <br /> <br /> Also I'm not sure how a game can get into perfect-or-die territory when perfects no longer exist. Everyone dies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T06:23:30-07:00","id":1240411,"title":"","content":"I feel like mixed game usually means 'mixed celestials'. If you come in with a DB to a Solar game you are going to have a tough time and it seems no worse this edition, and in fact you finally have some unique powers Solars can't fully replicate to recommend it.<br /> <br /> That being said I feel like in 3e the power gap exists but unlike 2e a group of DB can actually kill a Solar at similar exp totals if you bring your friends and best advantages (artifacts, soldiers) rather than it being mechanically impossible at a certain point as it got to in 2e. I don't see that as a widening of the power gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:38:05-07:00","id":1240427,"title":"","content":"rehash, forgot had answered already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:46:46-07:00","id":1240430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240411#post1240411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like mixed game usually means 'mixed celestials'. If you come in with a DB to a Solar game you are going to have a tough time and it seems no worse this edition, and in fact you finally have some unique powers Solars can't fully replicate to recommend it.<br /> <br /> That being said I feel like in 3e the power gap exists but unlike 2e a group of DB can actually kill a Solar at similar exp totals if you bring your friends and best advantages (artifacts, soldiers) rather than it being mechanically impossible at a certain point as it got to in 2e. I don't see that as a widening of the power gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it basically falls out that at early essence Dawn's are the combat monsters and all the other Solars are combat capable at best or straight up combat averse depending on character concept whereas DB really feel like they pretty well always have something to contribute to combat even without combat skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:50:19-07:00","id":1240431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240410#post1240410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm not sure how a game can get into perfect-or-die territory when perfects no longer exist. Everyone dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, yes? That's what we are seeing a lot of. Revolving Shot with the follow-up kill shot, multi-attacking Brawl or Melee builds, Perma-stealth assassin or the rampaging familiar who never resets after decisive, and I could name a few more ways in which Solars can totally <i>destroy</i> their opponents in about 1 to 2 rounds without them really having even a shadow of a chance without a perfect counter to break these kinds of combo's, and more importantly without nuking their mote pool. And no, not just the Dawns. All of these can be relatively easily be achieved by essence 1-2 characters.<br /> <br /> And to address the power-gap, no, imho it is wider than in the previous edition, also, the DB's had just as much tricks which the other splats couldn't pull back then, and we certainly included them in our games as players. They were a great deal of fun and as long as you picked your niche wisely, you could pull your weight in the group. Especially if you knew what you were doing, and even up till E5. Trust me, we did it plenty. <br /> <br /> But in Ex3 the Solars start out with 15 Charms, no excellency speed bumps and, of course, the big, bad Supernals. 40 or 50 xp into the campaign they are very likely playing with the most powerful and effective charms in their chosen field and be starting to broaden their capabilities as they are hitting some serious diminishing returns, or at least that is what I have seen. Even if the Solars just dabble in the DB's specialty, they will outmatch them, which in a party of 5 players is more difficult to avoid than you imagine. A substantial % of the DB's charm budget will go to excellencies, and they can't go 'deep', so the DB will be spread out by default and as said before, the Solar will hit the win-even-more-oh-so-unbelievably-more section of his tree before long.<br /> <br /> I believe to have them in mixed groups house-ruling in a Supernal, and the same deal as Solars on excellencies will be a necessity to have them be enjoyable to play. Not a disaster, but it must be said that at some point it was said that better mixed play was one of the goals. Not to mention that having played without bought excellencies and a supernal and just getting right to giving your character cool and defining powers which no other character at the table could have access to (unless someone has the same Supernal or the group is E5, but how likely is that?), this seems like a huge step back.<br /> <br /> Ah, and to clarify: note that none of these concerns of mine are relevant in a pure DB game, except the fear that some players will be turned off by the Aura adding more stuff to track and build around. I think playing a lower-powered game than what the Solars have to offer will be quite enjoyable and in fact, looking quite forward to that myself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:42:29-07:00","id":1240480,"title":"","content":"Ok, but how does a dragonblooded who can go all-out compare to a solar who's trying not to flare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:09:19-07:00","id":1240492,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I feel like that's just as much a problem of playing with 5 players, rather than purely a Solar vs. DB powerlevel thing. One of my friends recently played in a mixed circle game of 2 Solars 1 DB and enjoyed it, but with only three players its much easier to have a niche and also to just get more attention during a game. That said, yeah, you do have to be willing to accept being considerably less powerful as a DB in a mixed Solar/DB game, but the devs have always been honest about this being the case.<br /> <br /> As to lethality, firstly its not a pvp game so your DB doesn't have to be built to tank the onslaught of a Solar. Secondly, in my experience, Solar lethality is exaggerated at low essence levels and a DB could easily significantly contribute to a fight. It's highly dependent on both your circle and the kind of fights your group gets in, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240431#post1240431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not a disaster, but it must be said that at some point it was said that better mixed play was one of the goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall this being said, at least where Solars/DBs are concerned. In fact, the devs have said that DBs remain considerably less powerful than Solars in 3e, and mixed splat is not the default assumption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:16:52-07:00","id":1240495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240492#post1240492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As to lethality, firstly its not a pvp game so your DB doesn't have to be built to tank the onslaught of a Solar. Secondly, in my experience, Solar lethality is exaggerated at low essence levels and a DB could easily significantly contribute to a fight. It's highly dependent on both your circle and the kind of fights your group gets in, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not but it's highly dependent on minmaxing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:18:47-07:00","id":1240498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240492#post1240492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't recall this being said, at least where Solars/DBs are concerned. In fact, the devs have said that DBs remain considerably less powerful than Solars in 3e, and mixed splat is not the default assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I've said this. I find it a very desirable thing to want to encourage mixed circle play. Though a lot of that was stemming from 2E's Solars being the most bland and boring 'I win' button I could imagine and most of the people I play with gravitate towards different things. In 3E this isn't as much of an issue since solars are playable again (for me) and based on DB the overall power gap doesn't seem as big. <br /> <br /> My biggest problem wasn't even playing at a lower power level than a solar. I had lots of fun as a lunar and Alchemical in mixed circles. No, the biggest BS was the experience charts. Everything progressed slower for non-solaroids. It was painful! Either the ST gives out more xp to the non-sloar characters or they consistently fell behind in charms, abilities and attributes. Easy fix was of course to scrap the built-in progression stuff and just use solar's xp chart with tweaks for attribute exalts and whatnot but the fact that it was the default was crap!<br /> <br /> This edition that isn't a thing anymore, so I'm pretty much happy with how it's going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T10:43:28-07:00","id":1240505,"title":"","content":"Cross-splat play is very desirable to me, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:36:20-07:00","id":1240526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240480#post1240480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but how does a dragonblooded who can go all-out compare to a solar who's trying not to flare?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Solar hide what they are even while doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T11:40:24-07:00","id":1240527,"title":"","content":"Well, there's a couple of charms that probably give the game away, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T22:58:06-07:00","id":1240727,"title":"","content":"I have to say, my favourite takeaway from this thread is the term \u201cMookblooded\u201d. That for sure is finding its way into a Lunar insult. \ud83d\ude06","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T23:58:31-07:00","id":1240742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240401#post1240401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not defending Fenrir's particular style of getting their message across, but must admit there is a basis to the basic complaint.<br /> <br /> Essence 3 really is a long way off, even if, like us, you condense the progression chart. I too thought that the printed Martial Arts and evocations usually offer a tighter and more focused package of charms that seem much easier to build around than their regular charm trees, especially in the area of combat. I can also see Aura as not being too loved by many players in my regular group for whom Exalted is already at the very edge of their crunch-comfort zone and <i>really </i>don't need yet another thing to track.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, depending on the style of campaigns that people are running I can definitely see this as being an issue. There's some really cool stuff in the signature charms that you really should be looking forward to, not treating like level 20 powers in DnD. You know, like something you might get to use for 4 sessions ever or something. I'm not sure if that's necessarily a flaw with the charmset, but the charmset does not very easily support 20 game campaigns. Not without some kind of bonus granted xp or something.<br /> <br /> Especially coming off Solars, who's every power is either interesting or very powerful, or both. It can be very difficult to refocus on the strengths that the DBs have after playing badass Solars and seeing how starkly the DBs lack in those same ways. On the other hand if you wanted your DB to be able to duel a second circle demon like Octavian on her own, then sorry but what you're looking to play is a Solar.<br /> <br /> Some of the charms could definitely use a tweak though. There's a difference between being kind of situational and being next to useless. Extending the range of a class of weapons to (long) when they're almost exclusively long anyway, or adding 5 dice for 5 motes with no other effect when the excellency already does that but better. They're not the whole charmset but they could use a little overhaul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240401#post1240401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as to comparing with Solars, in my opinion it is not something to shy away from. After all, my tables, mine included, really enjoy mixed splat games, and while admittedly it is just an impression based on just reading and not actual in-game experience with the DB, just the Solars, but to me the gap looks a great deal wider than it was before, and further exacerbated by Solars having Supernal abilities. In Ex2.5, if your DB wasn't combat focused, the xp charts were fixed and there was some minimal niche protection agreed upon, it was actually rather fine, while, if you play the DB in a Solar party now, I'm not so sure you feel you are not a total chump and henchman, even with your cultural advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the gap is wider in some areas and thinner in others, it will vary overall depending on how min-maxy your group is. First of all, you'll be incomparable to a Solar at chargen in their Supernal, if they wish it. They'll have essence 5 Solar charms and you'll have essence 2 DB charms. On the other hand you'll have access to higher essence evocations, martial arts and natural charms than any non-MA Solar, admittedly with the terrestrial keyword. They'll catch up by like 70xp-80xp but that's a fair bit of time. Your dicecap is still lower but your excellencies are still more efficient, and as long as you're not going up against a Solar in their Supernal I'd say you stand a solid chance. If you're lucky or clever anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240480#post1240480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but how does a dragonblooded who can go all-out compare to a solar who's trying not to flare?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty favourably. That's kind of where DBs leverage their power too. They get an additional specialty, WAY more merit dots, more bonus points, and cooler anima powers*. As far as I'm concerned non-excellency charms are almost just the bonus on top of your real strength.<br /> <br /> What a &quot;white room&quot; fight between a DB and a Solar looks like is a bloody exhausted Dawn stumbling through the doors of your fortress's main hall after you had your cousin poison his tea, and then he killed his way past all your guards and summoned demons and hired exigent mercenary. At which point you pounce on him with your most elite bodyguards and local mortal immaculate monks to rightly end him.<br /> <br /> I say this is a white room because his merit list says:<br /> **** Daiklave of killing<br /> *** Armor of not-getting-killed<br /> *** Danger Sense<br /> *** Fast Reflexes<br /> <br /> And yours says:<br /> *** Daiklave of burning<br /> *** Fullplate of the unburnt<br /> **** Backing (House Cathak)<br /> ***** Command (16th Legion and Attached Support Forces)<br /> *** Contacts (Nation of Zabarek)<br /> ***** Influence (Satrap of Zabarek)<br /> ***** Resources<br /> *** Ally (Cousin Ylale)<br /> *** Mighty Thews<br /> <br /> <br /> Now imagine you've got a whole sworn kinship of DBs like that. Spies absolutely everywhere, thousands of elite soliders, or tens of thousands of lesser ones, fleets of warships, money and influence that place you in a truly dizzying position of power and authority. Your group might as well be the Emperor, Shogun, High Priest, Champion and Spymaster of your own little Japan. Seriously, if you've all got 20+ story merits like that your idea of a fun sailing trip <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/70/1e/ad/701eadc4b1988d145cf2bc22247d8ed1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">looks like this</a>.<br /> <br /> Your solar can spend a one mote to reroll all 1s on a melee attack? That's so cute, I can speak one word, unenhanced by essence, and a city burns to the ground. As a DB it's not even hard to get to that point off chargen, and when you do you don't need to worry that the Realm will unite with Lookshy and come fight you out of fear either.<br /> <br /> Then after all that, toss on the ability to hurl a boulder or feel the weight of an assassin on the flagstones behind her.<br /> <br /> Man I have spent way too long on this the night before an exam.<br /> <br /> *Yes they are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:55:36-07:00","id":1240820,"title":"","content":"Eh, five players and an ST has in my experience been the standard, as well as mixed play, so, yes, imho that must be taken into account. Obviously Solar charms are, and should be, more powerful and the sort of player who goes for the Dragonblood over the Solar is looking for the kind of play experience in which they are the underdog. However, not only are you stuck at essence 2 charms for what will effectively be the lion's share of the campaign, your really iconic toys just out of reach while the rest gets the whole shop, a large part of your charm selection which is already lower-powered, must go to stuff the others get <i>for free</i>. <br /> <br /> These are the type of mechanical constraints to subject a splat to that can really breed frustration and a decidedly not-fun experience when you mix it with one who doesn't suffer from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:36:34-07:00","id":1240887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240820#post1240820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a large part of your charm selection which is already lower-powered, must go to stuff the others get <i>for free</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even having seen that it doesn't cause a lot of issues, in DB-only play at least, it still <i> bugs</i> the hell out of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:49:23-07:00","id":1240893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240820#post1240820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, five players and an ST has in my experience been the standard, as well as mixed play, so, yes, imho that must be taken into account. Obviously Solar charms are, and should be, more powerful and the sort of player who goes for the Dragonblood over the Solar is looking for the kind of play experience in which they are the underdog. However, not only are you stuck at essence 2 charms for what will effectively be the lion's share of the campaign, your really iconic toys just out of reach while the rest gets the whole shop, a large part of your charm selection which is already lower-powered, must go to stuff the others get <i>for free</i>.<br /> <br /> These are the type of mechanical constraints to subject a splat to that can really breed frustration and a decidedly not-fun experience when you mix it with one who doesn't suffer from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remove the Supernal Keyword. Solars at E1 are still stronger but not overwhelmingly stronger than DBs with that limitation. I'm not a fan of the idea myself and I hope no one goes, &quot;but lets them beat bigger things than them at the start of the game.&quot; That only applies to the solars who happen to be good at one of three skills out of twenty five skills. The rest still get destroyed by death ray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-31-2018, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:55:51-07:00","id":1240898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240727#post1240727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, my favourite takeaway from this thread is the term \u201cMookblooded\u201d. That for sure is finding its way into a Lunar insult. \ud83d\ude06</div> </div> </div> </div>This smacks of the bavado of inexperienced youth so, maybe fresh lunars who've never faced a wyld hunt but I'm pretty sure the elders would tell them to shut the hell up about things they don't understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:08:24-07:00","id":1240927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240898#post1240898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This smacks of the bavado of inexperienced youth so, maybe fresh lunars who've never faced a wyld hunt but I'm pretty sure the elders would tell them to shut the hell up about things they don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;That boy is so hard-headed, he put a dent in the Newspaper of Wisdom.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:42:16-07:00","id":1241145,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t have to be a callow stripling to insult the enemy such that he loses his composure mid swing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:49:24-07:00","id":1241163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241145#post1241145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t have to be a callow stripling to insult the enemy such that he loses his composure mid swing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that any Dragon-Blooded would see enough truth in the accusation to find it insulting.<br /> <br /> They aren't mooks. They are Exalted; Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> If you called me a green-skinned banana, I would just wonder what the hell you're talking about. That's how little purchase the insult would find in my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T22:03:50-07:00","id":1241171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1240927#post1240927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>&quot;That boy is so hard-headed, he put a dent in the Newspaper of Wisdom.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a rooster totem Lunar I see? &quot;Now boy-ah-say-boy! Lookit here naw, you've got this crusade thing all wrong y'see? All wrong! Y'keep goin' on like that and yer gonna end up-ah-say end up dead! D-E-A-D dead! You've gotta respec'tem see? Treat'em like a proper foe! They sure's shootin respect you! Now com'ere and let me show you how it's done. I swear this boy's got gusto but he's dumber than a bag of hammers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course if it followed the actual theme of most of those cartoons you'd have Foghorn Leghorn lining up a shot against a Dynast while the young chickenhawk Lunar is already holding all the artifacts of the sworn kinship he killed earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T22:07:24-07:00","id":1241173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241163#post1241163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that any Dragon-Blooded would see enough truth in the accusation to find it insulting.<br /> <br /> They aren't mooks. They are Exalted; Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> If you called me a green-skinned banana, I would just wonder what the hell you're talking about. That's how little purchase the insult would find in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cHey! How many mookblooded does it take to take down a single Anathema? I dunno, they just keep showing up and stumbling onto their fancy weapons. I\u2019ve collected 29 skulls so far!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, how many mookblooded does it take to run a satrapy? 20! 1 to be a corrupt asshole and 19 to go running back to big-red Mommy when a rabble gathers at their gate!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you know that Mook Blooded are Exalted by the fail worms of can\u2019t do a damn thing by themselves? It\u2019s true!\u201d<br /> <br /> And etcetera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 08-01-2018, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:34:28-07:00","id":1241253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And etcetera. </div> </div> </div>In addition to having similar doubts to Sunder about that actually registering with a DB (after all, DBs can and have done plenty by themselves; read some of the Aspect books if you don't believe me), I have my doubts that &quot;mook&quot; is even a term in Creation, considering it was only coined <i>here</i> in the 1930's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:57:49-07:00","id":1241266,"title":"","content":"&quot;Out of the way, extras&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Those aren't even a thing this edition&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:14:23-07:00","id":1241271,"title":"","content":"Jumping off of that reference to My Hero Academia, no Dragon-Blood is a mook just as no hero student or professional hero is a mook.<br /> <br /> A mook is one of the faceless minions that Gang Orca brought to the provisional license exam. Characters so unimportant that they all wear indentical masks. They have no individuality, being equipped with the same weapons, and having no apparent unique abilities. <br /> <br /> Compare that to the girl from the rival school whose only known ability is to pull her body parts into herself like a nightmarish turtle without a shell. She has a face, a name, a distinct appearance, a known place of origin, and a unique special ability. It doesn\u2019t seem like much of one, but MHA is frequently showing us that underestimating people is foolish. <br /> <br /> An even better example might be Mirio, a boy who worked hard to make a really difficult, double-edged sword of a Quirk into a game-breaking power. The likes of Bakugo and Todoroki would have easily outclassed him in his first year, but his additional year of experience puts him ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:29:27-07:00","id":1241318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241253#post1241253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to having similar doubts to Sunder about that actually registering with a DB (after all, DBs can and have done plenty by themselves; read some of the Aspect books if you don't believe me), I have my doubts that &quot;mook&quot; is even a term in Creation, considering it was only coined <i>here</i> in the 1930's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it was, the main reason we can see the term Mookblooded and safely assume it refers to Dragon-Blooded is because we experience Creation through the Exalted gameline.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T21:03:32-07:00","id":1241666,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> Was wondering where you can purchase WFHW? Don't see it on DrivethruRPG...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T22:49:45-07:00","id":1241686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241666#post1241666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> Was wondering where you can purchase WFHW? Don't see it on DrivethruRPG...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you backed the Kickstarter one of the things you got was a preview of the entire unfinished text of WFHW. The actual book should be available for purchase on Drivethru early next year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:11:27-07:00","id":1241862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241318#post1241318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> we experience Creation through the Exalted gameline.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean maybe you do. I experience Creation exclusively through the consumption of hallucinogens and wandering into the desert and let me tell you, the talking rock formations have some really weird ideas about Solars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:33:12-07:00","id":1241879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241666#post1241666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> Was wondering where you can purchase WFHW? Don't see it on DrivethruRPG...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it looks like I was wrong, you can also get it by preordering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241768-is-there-a-legit-way-to-get-wfhw-if-you-missed-the-kickstarter\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241768-is-there-a-legit-way-to-get-wfhw-if-you-missed-the-kickstarter\"> Is there a legit way to get WFHW if you missed the Kickstarter? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241768-is-there-a-legit-way-to-get-wfhw-if-you-missed-the-kickstarter\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241768-is-there-a-legit-way-to-get-wfhw-if-you-missed-the-kickstarter </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Looking through the forum threads, and even talking to my RL friends, I'm starting to feel like I'm the only person who was late to the kickstarter party. I missed out on getting the WFHW manuscript. I was living at a blockade camp, far away from everything except a coal baron's sinister ambitions. I've googled around a few times, and all I've turned up is an option on the OPP website to pre-order the pdf when it's released. Is there any legitimate way to lay my disconcertingly eager hands on that manuscript, or do I have to wait until late 2019? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:42:25-07:00","id":1241885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241862#post1241862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean maybe you do. I experience Creation exclusively through the consumption of hallucinogens and wandering into the desert and let me tell you, the talking rock formations have some really weird ideas about Solars</div> </div> </div> </div>Say hi to Cecelyne for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:44:51-07:00","id":1242547,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Will see if I can grab it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:05:27-07:00","id":1245881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241173#post1241173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cHey! How many mookblooded does it take to take down a single Anathema? I dunno, they just keep showing up and stumbling onto their fancy weapons. I\u2019ve collected 29 skulls so far!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, how many mookblooded does it take to run a satrapy? 20! 1 to be a corrupt asshole and 19 to go running back to big-red Mommy when a rabble gathers at their gate!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you know that Mook Blooded are Exalted by the fail worms of can\u2019t do a damn thing by themselves? It\u2019s true!\u201d<br /> <br /> And etcetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>The continued existence of comments like these are my thesis for buffing Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:12:57-07:00","id":1245885,"title":"","content":"Making Deebs stronger won't make the notions behind those comments any more inaccurate than they already are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:45:58-07:00","id":1245959,"title":"","content":"I don't know. I feel like having them at level of power where any Chargen Dawn fighting 1 v 5 against a Hearth is edge given to the Hearth, people might actually regard them as the setting antagonists they are. But, really, at that point, my complaint is more that Solar combat is a bit too strong - defense and onslaught negators especially, and that it kinda trivializes the effect of numbers as an equalizing factor. In an edition made largely as a reaction to how much iron wall defense characters ruin the setting, that's especially galling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:01:53-07:00","id":1245969,"title":"","content":"Are you sure that this isn't the case already? Because, while I haven't run a test scenario, what I've seen of the charmset (and what I've been hearing from sources I trust) is such that the Dawn is in serious trouble if he's alone vs 5 DB of the Wyld hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:28:40-07:00","id":1245985,"title":"","content":"I think it's not Solar combat charms per-se, so much as combat supernals.<br /> <br /> I think most chargen Solars, even with a combat stat at 5, would lose to most Hearths, because Essence 1 combat charms are not nearly enough to take out 5 Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> I'm actually not convinced a chargen Dawn does have the edge against 5 chargen Dragonblood, because... well, there's 5 of them. Between them, they've got far more attacks, health levels, etc. But I admit that a chargen Dawn can be a terrifying combat encounter, due to their Essence 3 or 4 combat charms (technically 5, but I doubt many Dawns will get an Essence 5 charm when they need to cover bases with their 15 charms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:31:48-07:00","id":1245990,"title":"","content":"Even with onslaught negators <i>and</i> defense boosters, five DBs still have quite an advantage - they get to take five times as many actions as the Solar does.*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b_______________________<br /> \u200b*Unless the Solar has Single Point Martial Arts Supernal, the daiklave Flying Silver Dream, dots in Command, and a Tyrant Lizard Familiar, anyway. But contrariwise, many of these are things that DBs can get as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-14-2018, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:18:40-07:00","id":1246018,"title":"","content":"There's all kinds of things you can do like distract gambits, poisons or the like. <br /> <br /> Plus a Dawn at character generation is supposed to be one who isn't just fresh out of the box exalted. They're supposed to have been around for 'less than a year' but a brand new solar exalt is only supposed to start with 10 charms right out of the gates (see the Everyday Heroes: Playing Mortals sidebar on page 125 for how to convert a mortal to a Solar in play)<br /> <br /> These are the ones that the Wyld Hunt wants to get to, and fast, before they get up to even the 15 charm mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T16:30:10-07:00","id":1246108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1245881#post1245881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The continued existence of comments like these are my thesis for buffing Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much comments as in-character insults. I personally think the DB charms are okay, and power-wise they are in a good place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T17:50:44-07:00","id":1246133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246108#post1246108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much comments as in-character insults.</div> </div> </div> </div>As we've said earlier in the thread, though, it's not actually something that'd make sense to say in-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T18:06:23-07:00","id":1246138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246133#post1246133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we've said earlier in the thread, though, it's not actually something that'd make sense to say in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y\u2019see I\u2019m not sure about that. In places where the Realm is a big red boot pressing on the necks of everyone, sure. But in the wild lands of the threshold or beyond or the Caul where Sha\u2019a Oka a is winning and there is a prevalent Jurassic Park vibe? <br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure DBs are going to be open to the concept that they are definitely not the top of the food chain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 08-15-2018, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T21:09:13-07:00","id":1246175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246138#post1246138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y\u2019see I\u2019m not sure about that. In places where the Realm is a big red boot pressing on the necks of everyone, sure. But in the wild lands of the threshold or beyond or the Caul where Sha\u2019Oka is winning and there is a prevalent Jurassic Park vibe?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure DBs are going to be open to the concept that they are definitely not the top of the food chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Lunars... ah, Lunars find a way...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T02:29:39-07:00","id":1246227,"title":"","content":"&quot;We emphasise unity because TOGETHER, the dragon blooded are the mightiest force in creation. Individually, however, there is shit out there that will chew you up and spit you back out. Don't be a lone wolf, and don't be a weak link. These bastards can smell fear.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T02:36:04-07:00","id":1246228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241253#post1241253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my doubts that &quot;mook&quot; is even a term in Creation, considering it was only coined <i>here</i> in the 1930's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, here we're getting back into the subject of how nobody in the setting is actually speaking English, so anything that anybody is presumed to say has to function as a stand-in for something in-character.<br /> <br /> As for colloquialisms, different people are going to have different standards for what breaks immersion, and there's probably nothing essentially wrong with any given thing.<br /> <br /> As an in-character insult employed by the Lunar Exalted, something like Moon-blooded, or anything else that might invoke the image of them as interchangeable and expendable minions, is fine by me. I can certainly think of worse things for the Lunars to have called, and done to, many of the Dragon Blooded who reign over Creation.<br /> <br /> As for the insult registering, I think it's perfectly plausible for it to play off of things like many Terrestrials knowing that many Lunars widely disseminate the narrative that they were the lowest ranked Exalted in a prior age of the world, or how Immaculate mythology still kind of says that they used to be servants under the thumb of the Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T12:18:25-07:00","id":1246406,"title":"","content":"I'm entirely against any perspective that portrays the Dragon Blooded as interchangeable antagonists because that really just sees the setting backsliding into some of the worst parts of 2e. 30 Dynasts should be a cataclysm to face at the same time. A non - elder Lunar saying they have the skulls of 30 of them from a single battle should be a boast the same way a 14 year old on Call of Duty saying they have a 3 foot cock is a boast; it makes the person saying it sound like a braggart and a fool. <br /> <br /> At weakest, Dragon Blooded should be the terrifyingly competent second in commands of the setting. The Odd Job, Boba Fett, or Starscream to a God, Celestial Exalt, or Older Dragon Blood. Fighting one should be the part of the movie where the hero clearly has to put actual effort into victory. The fact that there are ten thousand more where the one you just killed came from shouldn't anonymize them, it should make them terrifying. Absent that, we're back to needing other celestial circles or third circle demons to challenge parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T17:02:42-07:00","id":1246471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246406#post1246406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm entirely against any perspective that portrays the Dragon Blooded as interchangeable antagonists because that really just sees the setting backsliding into some of the worst parts of 2e. 30 Dynasts should be a cataclysm to face at the same time. A non - elder Lunar saying they have the skulls of 30 of them from a single battle should be a boast the same way a 14 year old on Call of Duty saying they have a 3 foot cock is a boast; it makes the person saying it sound like a braggart and a fool.<br /> <br /> At weakest, Dragon Blooded should be the terrifyingly competent second in commands of the setting. The Odd Job, Boba Fett, or Starscream to a God, Celestial Exalt, or Older Dragon Blood. Fighting one should be the part of the movie where the hero clearly has to put actual effort into victory. The fact that there are ten thousand more where the one you just killed came from shouldn't anonymize them, it should make them terrifying. Absent that, we're back to needing other celestial circles or third circle demons to challenge parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think of Samson killing an army of Philistines with a donkey's jawbone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T19:00:12-07:00","id":1246505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246471#post1246471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you think of Samson killing an army of Philistines with a donkey's jawbone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't normally let somebody use that as a form weapon for White Reaper Style, but it made sense for the character concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T20:35:47-07:00","id":1246527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1245959#post1245959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. I feel like having them at level of power where any Chargen Dawn fighting 1 v 5 against a Hearth is edge given to the Hearth, people might actually regard them as the setting antagonists they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen this rough scenario twice in actual play. The Dragonbloods won one fight, and forced the Solar to retreat or die in the other encounter. Terrestrial power-level is far better this edition then in previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 08-15-2018, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T00:24:27-07:00","id":1246554,"title":"","content":"My point was that it's perfectly in keeping with the setting to have people mythologise their accomplishments, and to dismiss grandiose exaggeration as infantile and pathetic is to discount many old cultural practices that certain people placed a lot of stock in, such as the Skalds of old Scandinavia; I find myself doubting that you'd call a tenth century Norseman a braggart and a fool to his face if he spun a tale of having slain thirty Englishmen in a single stroke of his sword.<br /> <br /> That and the idea that people should be perfectly capable of separating out-of-character assessments and things employed in-character, such as slurs and insults (that are either carefully calculated to get a rise out of people, or reflect the irrational hatreds and prejudices of characters, which many of the Lunars of the Silver Pact should definitely have towards a lot of the Dragon Blooded). <br /> <br /> Or what; there are members of the Silver Pact who absolutely would and have murdered Dynastic children that they could get within reach of, but they were unfailingly polite about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T06:12:01-07:00","id":1246625,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I do largely dismiss grandiose exaggeration people do with the expectation that it be taken seriously to be insecure and juvenile. But there are a range of social actions in and out of game you can take that don't involve calling some big dude a bullshitter. Even mentally noting that they are an immature bullshitter and going along with it is possible. I'm just saying that the default response from characters with basic knowledge of what the Exalted are should probably be, &quot;Oh. This person is a bullshitter.&quot;<br /> <br /> People still do it, of course. It just doesn't make them impressive. At best, it makes them funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T06:24:13-07:00","id":1246628,"title":"","content":"The proper response is to get into a bragging contest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thirty? I once took on a <i>hundred</i> enemy soldiers, with one arm hacked off and bleeding from the stump!&quot;<br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> &quot;It grew back&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T06:39:08-07:00","id":1246633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246628#post1246628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The proper response is to get into a bragging contest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thirty? I once took on a <i>hundred</i> enemy soldiers, with one arm hacked off and bleeding from the stump!&quot;<br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> &quot;It grew back&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a couple in mind. If it is a lunar PC, one of their mortal warriors steps forward and says, &quot;and while you were doin that, I got the other forty.&quot;<br /> <br /> If it's a Lunar Antagonist, the PCs' Hearth springs their ambush and says, &quot;then you'll have no problem with five.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T06:46:27-07:00","id":1246636,"title":"","content":"I find the casual dismissal of an artistically elaborate practice of a rich historical culture to be irritating, as I do dancing around the key point that Lunars might level such insults as a means of getting a rise out of their enemies.<br /> <br /> When Commodus is telling Maximus about reports on the last moments of his wife and child, whether or not what he's saying is accurate, or whether Maximus believes it is not the point; the point is that Commodus is being a dick about it.<br /> <br /> Actually, I can do one better than that; in Batman Begins, we have that scene in which Falcone punctuates his dressing down of Bruce by talking about his cell mate (the guy who killed the Wayne parents) talked about how Bruce's father begged like a dog as he died. The dramatic and emotional tension of that moment is remarkably <i>not</i> based in whether or not Bruce will respond with &quot;um, actually, that <i>didn't</i> happen, I was there&quot;.<br /> <br /> Jesus, a Lunar dismissing Terrestrial Exalted as mook blooded is inaccurate? Yeah, so is every racially motivated prejudice ever. And yet in the real world, the capacity to not be provoked by such things (and the attempt to fight against those who would invoke them), is not something based in rationally presented empirical arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T07:17:54-07:00","id":1246640,"title":"","content":"Wait...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246636#post1246636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet in the real world, the capacity to not be provoked by such things (and the attempt to fight against those who would invoke them), is not something based in rationally presented empirical arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>{he said as he was trying to rationally argue against somebody's deeply held prejudice against Dragon Blooded being dismissed in-character}<br /> <br /> Touch\u00e9, salesman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T07:27:39-07:00","id":1246645,"title":"","content":"I just had a vision of a lunar slur for deebs that when you trace the etymology is actually a first age rank equivalent to lieutenant or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T07:37:38-07:00","id":1246648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246645#post1246645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a vision of a lunar slur for deebs that when you trace the etymology is actually a first age rank equivalent to lieutenant or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like that one. Noted. I suppose any and all Soldier type put-downs are fair game for Lunars insulting deebs.<br /> <br /> Edit: Consulting a military jargon glossary, Shavetail is a pejorative term for a green Lieutenant (dating from when greenhorn Calvary Lieutenants were given horses with shaved tails to inform others that they were inexperienced) and given the actual terminology probably fits Lunar use quite well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 08-16-2018, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T08:18:44-07:00","id":1246658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246640#post1246640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> {he said as he was trying to rationally argue against somebody's deeply held prejudice against Dragon Blooded being dismissed in-character}<br /> <br /> Touch\u00e9, salesman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to partly run back and partly clarify. I do not have a problem with Lunars, or anybody for that matter, boasting about killing lots of deebs. I have a problem with attributing it to them having an anonymous position in the setting.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between &quot;I have killed countless of your kin because I am exceptionally mighty&quot; vs. &quot;I have killed countless of your kin because you are anonymous, interchangeable mooks.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that &quot;you are weaker than me&quot; enhances the setting and &quot;you are weak within the context of this setting&quot; harms it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T08:54:16-07:00","id":1246665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246471#post1246471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you think of Samson killing an army of Philistines with a donkey's jawbone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with this example is that the Philistines aren't...well, they aren't people with identies in the narrative. I'd say a better example of &quot;I'm so grand, I slaughtered my way through heroes to get here&quot; is Achilles' ...what's it called? Killing spree? Buzzaw moment? What have you, in the Illiad, where he does rampage through men who the text provides names and narratives of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:24:17-07:00","id":1246691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246628#post1246628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The proper response is to get into a bragging contest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thirty? I once took on a <i>hundred</i> enemy soldiers, with one arm hacked off and bleeding from the stump!&quot;<br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> &quot;It grew back&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of our campaigns, I had certain sects of very powerful and very zealous regenerating people (werewolves and the like) test themselves by fighting off numbers of their students. Before doing so, they would take various handicaps, such as disembowelment or limb removal. As part of the exercise, they'd have to use their magical and physical prowess to retain blood and escape long enough to regrow enough limbs to fight. They'd also have to balance the reduced amount of calories and oxygen available, plus the expenditure of supernatural resources in the middle of combat. <br /> <br /> It was presented (and received!) as being esoteric and unreasonable... but the ones who tried were definitely the NPC combat exemplars in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T12:47:55-07:00","id":1246728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246665#post1246665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem with this example is that the Philistines aren't...well, they aren't people with identies in the narrative. I'd say a better example of &quot;I'm so grand, I slaughtered my way through heroes to get here&quot; is Achilles' ...what's it called? Killing spree? Buzzaw moment? What have you, in the Illiad, where he does rampage through men who the text provides names and narratives of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a technical name for this sort of scene in Greek Epic. It's called an Aristeia.<br /> <br /> I also love how in Homer there is so much violence, death and destruction, but no one dies nameless, no one is <i>just</i> a prop in the protagonist's big action scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12943,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","user":"Handigar","date":". 08-16-2018, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12943-handigar","name":"Handigar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T14:35:15-07:00","id":1246750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Handigar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246728#post1246728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's a technical name for this sort of scene in Greek Epic. It's called an Aristeia.<br /> <br /> I also love how in Homer there is so much violence, death and destruction, but no one dies nameless, no one is <i>just</i> a prop in the protagonist's big action scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aristeia! That was the word! Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T15:26:24-07:00","id":1246779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246658#post1246658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not have a problem with Lunars, or anybody for that matter, boasting about killing lots of deebs. I have a problem with attributing it to them having an anonymous position in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that it's a thing that is genuinely provocative to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that &quot;you are weaker than me&quot; enhances the setting and &quot;you are weak within the context of this setting&quot; harms it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, I think the idea that all of the Lunars are rather polite about the people that many of them have reason to truly despise does its own kind of harm. It's so sterile and toothless.<br /> <br /> &quot;There are Lunars who are going to boast about having killed many Dragon Blooded, but they'll only do so in a manner that validates and reinforces the legitimacy of the Dragon Blooded, even though the fact that they're fighting <i>against</i> that is probably why that Lunar killed so many Dragon Blooded.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T15:56:04-07:00","id":1246792,"title":"","content":"My useless contribution: In setting, I'd tend to see a Lunar who claimed to slay 30 Dragonblooded in a battle, to demonstrate how lightly he thought of them, as equivalent roughly to.... an Immaculate who turned up and claimed to regard Lunars lightly as he claimed he had killed a circle of 5 them in a single battle, and these five, and Lunars in general, were too merely pathetic to be named.<br /> <br /> It's at the limits of what can happen in battle (because outcomes are not foreordained and such things could happen), but on the whole it's hard to buy that most characters in the setting with good awareness wouldn't be like the Creation equivalent of &quot;OK, bro, whatever&quot;, and even if they did believe it, would be unlikely to regard this as anything like an reasonable assessment of Lunar skill to use. Even Dragonblooded, I could hardly see leaping into &quot;You are right friend, and your story demonstrate, the Lunar Anathema are truly worthy of contempt and unworthy of notice as individuals&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T16:38:16-07:00","id":1246805,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't expect any Dragon Blooded to believe such a boast. I wouldn't expect them to be intimidated by it.<br /> <br /> I would expect them to be <i>pissed off</i>! How <i>dare</i> this Anathema make such claims?! How dare they dishonour the memory of brave Dragon Blooded who died fighting and killing others of that kind. How dare they perpetuate the disgusting, hideous <b>lie</b> that the Dragon Blooded were ever considered to be so insignificant.<br /> <br /> And the Lunar laughs, because rising to that provocation leaves their enemies unbalanced. Also, because the Lunar hates them, and wants them to feel unpleasant emotions.<br /> <br /> (If they're making the boasts among one another, the point isn't to get other Lunars to believe it; it's in the artistry of the compelling exaggeration)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T02:37:31-07:00","id":1246929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246805#post1246805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't expect any Dragon Blooded to believe such a boast. I wouldn't expect them to be intimidated by it.<br /> <br /> I would expect them to be <i>pissed off</i>! How <i>dare</i> this Anathema make such claims?! How dare they dishonour the memory of brave Dragon Blooded who died fighting and killing others of that kind. How dare they perpetuate the disgusting, hideous <b>lie</b> that the Dragon Blooded were ever considered to be so insignificant.<br /> <br /> And the Lunar laughs, because rising to that provocation leaves their enemies unbalanced. Also, because the Lunar hates them, and wants them to feel unpleasant emotions.<br /> <br /> (If they're making the boasts among one another, the point isn't to get other Lunars to believe it; it's in the artistry of the compelling exaggeration)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was a really dickish Lunar, I\u2019d do all the above while wearing the form of their bosom hearth-sibling whose heart\u2019s blood I\u2019d taken previously. <br /> <br /> For emphasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T03:11:05-07:00","id":1246939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246929#post1246929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I was a really dickish Lunar, I\u2019d do all the above while wearing the form of their bosom hearth-sibling whose heart\u2019s blood I\u2019d taken previously.<br /> <br /> For emphasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, if there's not a Charm to empower an action along the lines of making some really exaggerated boast and/or cruel mockery of another, I'd darn well make one; especially with that preview, it would not be out of place in their milieu.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be the same as a Protean Charm to be increasingly provocative through means of appropriating the form of somebody that a target cares about, but it would combine well with such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T06:03:29-07:00","id":1246986,"title":"","content":"I'm wary of the scenario, less because of the fanbase's history of treating the Dragon-Blooded as insignificant and more because it tends to help cast the Lunar Exalted as thwarted monsters.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T07:11:12-07:00","id":1247008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246986#post1246986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wary of the scenario, less because of the fanbase's history of treating the Dragon-Blooded as insignificant and more because it tends to help cast the Lunar Exalted as thwarted monsters.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why thwarted? On account of the Ursupation? Wouldn't not doing this just cast them as Thwarted (as opposed to Thwarted Monsters, which I actually prefer)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T07:48:06-07:00","id":1247018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1246986#post1246986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wary of the scenario, less because of the fanbase's history of treating the Dragon-Blooded as insignificant and more because it tends to help cast the Lunar Exalted as thwarted monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this wariness. A magically-enhanced boast seems to me something that will just draw players toward tearing it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T09:09:21-07:00","id":1247043,"title":"","content":"Well, Dragonblooded have a charm called Unbearable Taunt Technique which is a mocking joust so powerful that it provokes imidiate violence towards the Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> That might be more DB charmspace though because being a condescending asshole and then using that to intentionally get inside your enemy\u2019s head to screw them up is a pretty dynast thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T11:11:46-07:00","id":1247438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1247008#post1247008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why thwarted? On account of the Ursupation? Wouldn't not doing this just cast them as Thwarted (as opposed to Thwarted Monsters, which I actually prefer)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you acknowledge that the Realm is a better equipped and numerically superior enemy then surviving and establishing a power base beyond its reach becomes a valid victory condition.<br /> If you view Dragon-Blooded as interchangeable worthless foes, either the Realm falls or you die trying and the fact it's Realm Year 768 is a pretty good clue of how that one tends to end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T13:38:07-07:00","id":1247482,"title":"","content":"Lunars had a similar charm in 1e called Foe Taunting Utterance that not only made a character attack them instead of anyone else, but also made them abandon using defenses. It was pretty hilarious to fuck up big bads and leave them wide open to your allies. But it was a social charm and with no real social system it was always going to be a lulzy result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T16:28:51-07:00","id":1247543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1247438#post1247438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you view Dragon-Blooded as interchangeable worthless foes, either the Realm falls or you die trying and the fact it's Realm Year 768 is a pretty good clue of how that one tends to end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really suggesting that any Lunars would sincerely believe such a thing, rather than using it as a carefully cultivated insult that cuts right to the heart of Dragon Blooded pride, but I also feel as though this is a kind of simplified attitude to how people in life or death struggles, often persisting across generations, characterize their enemies.<br /> <br /> Still, even accounting for how irrational a Lunar that might sincerely believe in such a thing is*, there are ways in which the rhetoric can account for their victory taking a while. The degree to which they're outnumbered (which can itself be incorporated into a wider rhetoric of the Dragon Blooded being a kind of infesting vermin). Attributing their success to their happening to possess the legacy of the Solar Exalted, or the support of the Sidereals. All sorts.<br /> <br /> * And how writing off irrational beliefs as insignificant is kind of to discount the fact that they've actually resulted in countless deaths over the entire length of human history, right up to the modern day. There are quite a few people in the world today locked in struggle against the United States of America who are kind of impervious to any kind of logical argument about the futility of that, and they are still the cause of many many murders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T12:44:48-07:00","id":1247781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1247043#post1247043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Dragonblooded have a charm called Unbearable Taunt Technique which is a mocking joust so powerful that it provokes imidiate violence towards the Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> That might be more DB charmspace though because being a condescending asshole and then using that to intentionally get inside your enemy\u2019s head to screw them up is a pretty dynast thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me an amusing mental image of the taunt backfiring.<br /> <br /> Lunar: &quot;oh another mook blooded, I killed 30 of you one time from House.. oh I forget, you all look alike to me&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;I've got it on good authority that your mom could take 30 Dragon-Blooded too&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;MY MOTHER WAS A SAINT!&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;oh she was certainly on her knees enough&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;YOU MOTHERFUCKER I'LL KILL YOU!&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;Oh no I never had the pleasure personally, the line outside her bedroom door was far too long&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T13:29:07-07:00","id":1247791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1247781#post1247781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gives me an amusing mental image of the taunt backfiring.<br /> <br /> Lunar: &quot;oh another mook blooded, I killed 30 of you one time from House.. oh I forget, you all look alike to me&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;I've got it on good authority that your mom could take 30 Dragon-Blooded too&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;MY MOTHER WAS A SAINT!&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;oh she was certainly on her knees enough&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;YOU MOTHERFUCKER I'LL KILL YOU!&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;Oh no I never had the pleasure personally, the line outside her bedroom door was far too long&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, it can turn into a ricochet...<br /> <br /> Double Backfire Scenario 1<br /> <br /> Lunar: &quot;So I guess that's why you went to your own, instead?&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;YOU COMMONERS AND YOUR SALACIOUS RUMORS! I'LL PUT A STOP TO THAT TALK HERE AND NOW!&quot;<br /> Lunar: &quot;You sure you can do it alone? Don't need your matriarch to watch and give you pointers?&quot;<br /> <br /> Double Backfire Scenario 2<br /> <br /> Lunar: &quot;You know, you are so totally right about that.&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: &quot;So why are you smiling?&quot;<br /> Lunar (shapeshifting back into original form): &quot;Why do you think, sister?&quot;<br /> Dragon-Blooded: (Gintama-style horrified reaction face with eyes hidden in shadow)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T14:14:17-07:00","id":1247803,"title":"","content":"Except they both change the context of the original taunt, considerably in the case of the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-19-2018, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T21:14:40-07:00","id":1247897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1247803#post1247803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they both change the context of the original taunt, considerably in the case of the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it fertile ground for using the retroactively pre-planned type of effect. The original taunt ends up being the last one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T14:02:18-07:00","id":1248208,"title":"","content":"<i>Looks at DB Presence</i><br /> <br /> I mean... they seem to be pretty damn good at taunting people~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T06:53:54-07:00","id":1251652,"title":"","content":"I was kind of disappointed with the &quot;police procedural&quot; feel of the Investigation charms. I think it really clashes thematically with the rest of the setting <span style=\"font-size:9px\">and I also hate cop shows.<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> I'd love to see Investigation charms focus more on spies, scavenger lords, blackmailers, courtiers, or basically anything else.<br /> <br /> Though I have to admit, the Dragon-Blooded charms were still better for this than the Solars'. There were a significant minority of non-cop Investigation charms. And I guess you could rationalise it to a degree because a lot of Terrestrials with Investigation will be the Empress' Magistrates, and it's plausible that they fulfilled a similar role in the First Age. Even then, I think I'd still rather that Investigation charms designed for other purposes have secondary applications that you could use to catch criminals if that's what your character is about. (Possibly that last part is my anti-cop show bias showing, but I stand by the rest.)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T08:21:48-07:00","id":1251672,"title":"","content":"Is there a list anywhere of Charms that Minton and Vance have said are probably getting reworked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T08:42:00-07:00","id":1251676,"title":"","content":"Vance has mentioned the Excellencies being reworked in a few cases, and the Signature Craft Charms. Not much else beyond that. We have to wait for the final pdf to check them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T09:01:21-07:00","id":1251680,"title":"","content":"There's been at least a couple charms that the community has pointed out as being very niche, or almost impossible to use which Vance has stated will get looked at/clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T13:19:16-07:00","id":1251747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1251676#post1251676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance has mentioned the Excellencies being reworked in a few cases, and the Signature Craft Charms. Not much else beyond that. We have to wait for the final pdf to check them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've personally seen him mention Sky Calming Draw and Flame Born Interception as being flagged for a second look, as well as Ringing Anvil Onslaught.<br /> <br /> I don't think the tweaks have to be major though, just a little smoothing out for a bump here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T13:51:37-07:00","id":1251752,"title":"","content":"There's the Wood 'add stamina to your grapple control roll' charm that is almost always less efficient than the excellency, which I'd hope to see tweaked...<br /> <br /> Also elusive heat-shimmer technique is so fragile and in a way so completely out of the player's control. I just had a character in a fight where it was actually a good thing that I'd forgotten I just bought it, because it would have poofed in the first round. Even just giving the option to immediately repay the cost would leave it only slightly edging out the dodge Excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 09-05-2018, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T14:37:07-07:00","id":1251761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1251752#post1251752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the Wood 'add stamina to your grapple control roll' charm that is almost always less efficient than the excellency, which I'd hope to see tweaked...<br /> <br /> Also elusive heat-shimmer technique is so fragile and in a way so completely out of the player's control. I just had a character in a fight where it was actually a good thing that I'd forgotten I just bought it, because it would have poofed in the first round. Even just giving the option to immediately repay the cost would leave it only slightly edging out the dodge Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in fact considering the excellency adds a bonus effect even when it's at its most efficient it isn't as efficient, you need to be in Wood Aura for it to do anything really, in which case it should just be an Aura charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T03:30:56-07:00","id":1251874,"title":"","content":"It's not an aura charm because it also adds stamina to withering damage, which is perfectly functional as it's not subject to dice caps nor can it be used with the excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T05:34:30-07:00","id":1251891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1241171#post1241171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a rooster totem Lunar I see? &quot;Now boy-ah-say-boy! Lookit here naw, you've got this crusade thing all wrong y'see? All wrong! Y'keep goin' on like that and yer gonna end up-ah-say end up dead! D-E-A-D dead! You've gotta respec'tem see? Treat'em like a proper foe! They sure's shootin respect you! Now com'ere and let me show you how it's done. I swear this boy's got gusto but he's dumber than a bag of hammers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course if it followed the actual theme of most of those cartoons you'd have Foghorn Leghorn lining up a shot against a Dynast while the young chickenhawk Lunar is already holding all the artifacts of the sworn kinship he killed earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... going to do this. <br /> <br /> And he's going to be evil and grand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:24:05-07:00","id":1251925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1251874#post1251874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not an aura charm because it also adds stamina to withering damage, which is perfectly functional as it's not subject to dice caps nor can it be used with the excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is so wasteful to use on a control roll that that half of the charm is a trap option.<br /> <br /> Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic is the biggest disappointment to me, though, to the extent that I'm going to ask my ST to let me un-buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 09-06-2018, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:28:51-07:00","id":1251931,"title":"","content":"This is true. As-written it's a two-in-one charm that's more 1 and a half in 1. <br /> <br /> My instinct would be to declare the bonus to clinches non-charm and see if anything breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T12:19:44-07:00","id":1251973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1251925#post1251925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it is so wasteful to use on a control roll that that half of the charm is a trap option.<br /> <br /> Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic is the biggest disappointment to me, though, to the extent that I'm going to ask my ST to let me un-buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s a tough one, I think it would be okay as a reflexive charm. As a simple it\u2019s very situational and only really decent against enemies with large dice pools who can\u2019t reroll 1s, or in fire aura against enemies with really small attack pools, although even then the chances aren\u2019t good.<br /> <br /> At least with reflexive you\u2019re paying 2 initiative to gamble on a few free excellencies.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually after doing some math the chances of rolling at least one 1 on a big attack pool like 16 dice is pretty decent, so I\u2019d say definitely solid in those situations as a reflexive charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-06-2018, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}